    {
      "number": 21,
      "question_en": "A 48 year-old male complained of a breathing problem which is worsened with the appearance of shortness of breath. He had a chronic cough and an excess amount of grayish mucous for many years. During the examination he was breathing heavily and exhaling through pursed lips. During breathing he had rattling sounds and kept coughing. He reported that he was a heavy smoker of two packs per day for the past 20 years. The physical examination revealed that his lips and fingertips were of a normal color and not cyanotic. His complexion was reddish. His chest had a barrel appearance, deep from front to back. Observing his breathing showed that his diaphragm moved very little. He had a dorsal kyphosis with a hump at the top of his spine. Auscultation of his chest revealed rhonchi, crackles, and decreased breath sounds throughout his chest. He had some slight ankle edema. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一名48歲男性主訴呼吸問題,並隨著呼吸急促的出現而惡化。他多年來有慢性咳嗽,並咳出大量灰色黏液。檢查時他呼吸費力,並以噘嘴方式呼氣。呼吸時可聽到囉音,並持續咳嗽。他表示自己每天吸兩包菸,已持續20年。理學檢查發現他的嘴唇與指尖顏色正常,並無發紺。面色偏紅。胸廓呈桶狀,前後徑加深。觀察其呼吸顯示橫膈膜活動極少。他有駝背合併脊椎上端隆起。胸部聽診發現囉音、爆裂音,且全肺呼吸音減弱。他的腳踝有輕微水腫。最可能的診斷為何?",
