          "key": "D",
          "en": "congestive heart failure (CHF)",
          "hant": "充血性心臟衰竭(CHF)",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This patient has elements of both pink puffer COPD (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease) and blue bloater COPD. There can be an overlap between these two types of categories. Generally, the blue bloater refers to those suffering from chronic bronchitis and the pink puffer refers to someone suffering from emphysema. This patient has elements of both but without the cyanosis found in the blue bloater type. The term pink puffer comes from the reddish complexion and the \"puffing\" or hyperventilation seen in patients suffering from COPD. Pink puffers are typically a thin patient that breathes with pursed lips. A pink puffer has tachypnoeic (increased respiratory rate) and experiences breathing difficulty. A pink puffer suffers primarily from emphysema. The prognosis for pink puffers is better than for blue bloaters. The term blue bloater is derived from the bluish color of the lips and skin commonly seen in patients with COPD. Blue bloaters are typically overweight. A blue bloater has a cough with sputum for 3 months to one year or more. A blue bloater experiences cyanosis due to a decrease in sufficient amounts of oxygen reaching the blood. Ankles and legs may be swollen and distention in the neck veins may be apparent. A blue bloater primarily suffers from chronic bronchitis. Blue bloaters develop signs of right-sided heart failure. This patient needs to discontinue smoking, receive treatment for heart failure (digitalis, diuretics), and prescribed bronchodilators and expectorants. CHF typically presents with more pronounced signs of fluid overload, such as jugular venous distension, pulmonary edema (wet crackles or rales on auscultation), and orthopnea, which are not described. The patient���s barrel chest, pursed-lip breathing, and long smoking history strongly point to a pulmonary rather than cardiac etiology. The absence of cyanosis and the presence of rhonchi and decreased breath sounds further support COPD over CHF. Bronchiectasis typically produces large volumes of purulent (yellow/green) sputum, often with hemoptysis, and is less associated with a barrel chest or hyperinflation. The patient���s grayish mucus and 20-year heavy smoking history align more with COPD. Additionally, the physical findings of minimal diaphragm movement and dorsal kyphosis suggest emphysema-related hyperinflation, which is not typical in bronchiectasis Western Physical Exam Skills for Practitioners of Asian Medicine, 2009, Robinson, Wolfe, page 48, 49",
      "exp_hant": "此病患同時具有『粉紅喘息型』(pink puffer)慢性阻塞性肺病與『藍腫型』(blue bloater)慢性阻塞性肺病的特徵。這兩種分類之間可能會有重疊。一般而言,『藍腫型』指的是罹患慢性支氣管炎的病患,而『粉紅喘息型』則指罹患肺氣腫的病患。此病患兼具兩者特徵,但沒有『藍腫型』常見的發紺現象。『粉紅喘息型』一詞源自於慢性阻塞性肺病病患常見的偏紅面色與『喘息』(即換氣過度)。粉紅喘息型病患通常體型偏瘦,並以噘嘴方式呼吸。粉紅喘息型病患呼吸速率增快(呼吸急促)且有呼吸困難。粉紅喘息型病患主要患有肺氣腫。粉紅喘息型的預後優於藍腫型。『藍腫型』一詞源自於慢性阻塞性肺病病患常見的嘴唇與皮膚發藍現象。藍腫型病患通常體重過重。藍腫型病患的咳嗽伴痰已持續3個月至一年以上。藍腫型病患因血液中氧氣供應不足而出現發紺。腳踝與腿部可能腫脹,頸靜脈可能出現怒張。藍腫型主要患有慢性支氣管炎。藍腫型病患會發展出右側心臟衰竭的徵象。此病患需要戒菸,接受心臟衰竭治療(毛地黃、利尿劑),並使用支氣管擴張劑與化痰藥。充血性心臟衰竭(CHF)通常會呈現更明顯的體液過量徵象,例如頸靜脈怒張、肺水腫(聽診可聞及濕囉音或爆裂音)及端坐呼吸,而本案例並未描述這些徵象。此病患的桶狀胸、噘嘴呼吸及長期吸菸史更強烈指向肺部而非心臟病因。缺乏發紺、且出現囉音與呼吸音減弱,進一步支持慢性阻塞性肺病而非充血性心臟衰竭的診斷。支氣管擴張症通常會產生大量膿性(黃綠色)痰液,常伴隨咳血,且較少合併桶狀胸或肺部過度充氣。此病患灰色黏液及20年重度吸菸史更符合慢性阻塞性肺病。此外,橫膈膜活動極少及駝背等理學發現,提示與肺氣腫相關的肺部過度充氣,這在支氣管擴張症中並不常見。Western Physical Exam Skills for Practitioners of Asian Medicine, 2009, Robinson, Wolfe, page 48, 49"
    },
