      "exp_en": "The main function of the parathyroid glands is to regulate calcium levels in the blood. If calcium levels are low, PTH (parathyroid hormone) levels increase. If calcium is high, PTH levels are reduced. Calcium is important in the regulation and processes such as bone formation, hormone release, and muscle contraction, as well as nerve and brain function. PTH regulates calcium by influencing absorption in the GI tract, excretion in the urine, and release from the bones. If too much calcium is released from the bones, the result can be osteoporosis. In osteoporosis the bones become weak and are more likely to break (fractures). tcmtests.com, July 2020",
      "exp_hant": "甲狀旁腺的主要功能是調節血液中的鈣濃度。當鈣濃度偏低時,副甲狀腺素(PTH)濃度會上升;當鈣濃度偏高時,PTH濃度會下降。鈣在骨骼形成、荷爾蒙釋放、肌肉收縮,以及神經與腦部功能的調節過程中都很重要。PTH透過影響腸胃道的吸收、尿液中的排泄,以及骨骼中的釋放來調節鈣濃度。若骨骼釋放過多鈣質,可能導致骨質疏鬆症。骨質疏鬆症會使骨骼變得脆弱,更容易發生骨折。tcmtests.com, July 2020"
