          "en": "a displaced posterior rib fracture",
          "hant": "移位性後肋骨折",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A posterior rib fracture in a toddler is many times the result of violently grabbing and squeezing the chest. This type of injury is very suspicious of abuse. A spiral tibial fracture is a common injury that is often mistaken for abuse but not often caused by abuse. A spiral fracture occurs when torque is applied along the axis of a bone. Spiral tibial fractures often occur when the body is in motion while one leg is planted. Bruises over bony prominences (shins, knees, forehead) are common in falls while the toddler learns to walk. Well padded body areas (thigh, buttock, cheeks) that are bruised can also increase the possibility of child abuse. Case Files in Family Medicine, Toy, Briscoe, Britton, Heidelbaugh, Fourth edition, page 393",
      "exp_hant": "幼兒的後肋骨折多半是由於用力抓握並擠壓胸部所造成。這類傷害高度令人懷疑虐待。脛骨螺旋型骨折是一種常見的損傷,常被誤認為是虐待所致,但實際上並非虐待造成的常見原因。螺旋型骨折發生於扭轉力沿骨骼軸向施加時。脛骨螺旋型骨折常發生於身體處於運動狀態、而一隻腳固定不動時。骨性突起部位(脛部、膝蓋、前額)的瘀傷,在幼兒學步跌倒時很常見。若軟組織保護較多的部位(大腿、臀部、臉頰)出現瘀傷,則會提高虐待的可能性。Case Files in Family Medicine, Toy, Briscoe, Britton, Heidelbaugh, Fourth edition, page 393"
