      ],
      "exp_en": "The thyroid hormones Thyroxine (T4) and Triiodothyronine (T3) are produced and secreted by the thyroid gland. T4 is produced by the thyroid gland in much greater amounts than T3, around 90 percent more. This is because when T4 reaches organs and body tissue, it is converted into T3. T4 is basically a stepping stone required for T3. Thyroid hormone is 90 percent T4 (thyroxine) and 10 percent T3 (triiodothyronine). As much as 99 percent of T4 is bound to proteins and only 1-5 percent is unbound or free. It is the free T3 that is the active thyroid hormone in the body. Elevated levels are associated with primary hyperthyroid diseases (Graves disease, Plummer disease) and acute thyroiditis. Low levels are associated with hypothyroid states (pituitary insufficiency, hypothalamic failure, iodine deficiency, Hashimoto thyroiditis). Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 465",
      "exp_hant": "甲狀腺荷爾蒙甲狀腺素(T4)與三碘甲狀腺素(T3)由甲狀腺分泌產生。甲狀腺分泌的T4遠多於T3,約多出90%。這是因為當T4到達器官與身體組織後,會轉換為T3。T4基本上是產生T3所必須的前驅物質。甲狀腺荷爾蒙中約90%為T4(甲狀腺素),10%為T3(三碘甲狀腺素)。高達99%的T4與蛋白質結合,僅有1-5%為游離態。發揮活性作用的甲狀腺荷爾蒙是游離的T3。數值升高與原發性甲狀腺功能亢進疾病(葛瑞夫氏病、普盧默氏病)及急性甲狀腺炎有關。數值偏低則與甲狀腺功能低下狀態(腦下垂體功能不足、下視丘功能衰竭、碘缺乏、橋本氏甲狀腺炎)有關。Mosby's Manual of Diagnostic and Laboratory Tests, 7th Edition, Pagana, page 465"
