    {
      "number": 49,
      "question_en": "A 45 year-old male had a right shoulder injury due to slipping in the shower six months earlier. He tried to stop the fall by hanging on to the towel rack. After the fall, the pain became progressively worse with the shoulder becoming stiff. He had trouble trying to reach behind his back to put a coat on and when lifting the arm over head. He has a history of mild diabetes. The physical examination showed that the neck exam was normal. The left shoulder ROM was normal. The right shoulder ROM was limited to 20 degrees of abduction and little internal rotation. Mild atrophy could be observed on the right deltoid when compared to the left. There was mild swelling of the right hand. Neuromuscular function of the right hand was normal. What is the first action you should take?",
      "question_hant": "一名45歲男性因六個月前在浴室滑倒導致右肩受傷。他試圖抓住毛巾架以阻止跌倒。跌倒後,疼痛逐漸加劇,肩部也變得僵硬。他在試圖將手伸到背後穿外套,以及將手臂舉過頭頂時感到困難。他有輕度糖尿病病史。理學檢查顯示頸部檢查正常。左肩活動範圍(ROM)正常。右肩活動範圍受限,外展僅達20度,內旋活動也很少。與左側相比,右三角肌可觀察到輕微萎縮。右手有輕微腫脹。右手神經肌肉功能正常。您應採取的第一步行動是什麼?",
