      "exp_en": "The red flag is shoulder pain and progressive inability to abduct the arm due to stiffness in the shoulder. Adhesive capsulitis (frozen shoulder) is assumed present until proven otherwise. In a frozen shoulder there may be scattered trigger points around the affected joint. The ROM, especially internal rotation and abduction, steadily decreases until there is very little movement in any direction (frozen shoulder). Due to not using the arm and shoulder there can be muscle atrophy. Hand swelling and discoloration can exist in serious cases. If detected early, the development of a totally frozen shoulder can be prevented with acupuncture. Preventing a frozen shoulder is much easier than treating a frozen shoulder. If the condition worsens or is unresponsive to acupuncture, a referral to a physiatrist, orthopedic surgeon or primary care physician is advisable. An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 130-131",
      "exp_hant": "警示徵象為肩部疼痛,並因肩部僵硬而逐漸無法外展手臂。除非證實並非如此,否則應假定為沾黏性關節囊炎(冰凍肩)。冰凍肩患者的患側關節周圍可能散布著激痛點。活動範圍,尤其是內旋與外展,會持續減少,直到任何方向的活動幅度都非常有限(冰凍肩)。由於手臂與肩部不常使用,可能出現肌肉萎縮。嚴重病例中可能出現手部腫脹與變色。若能及早發現,針灸可預防完全冰凍肩的發展。預防冰凍肩遠比治療冰凍肩容易。若病情惡化或對針灸治療反應不佳,建議轉介復健科醫師、骨科醫師或初級照護醫師。An Acupuncturist's Guide to Medical Red Flags and Referrals, 2012, Anzaldua, pages 130-131"
