      "exp_en": "This formula clears Liver heat, directs rebellious qi down, and stops vomiting. The chief herb huang lian which is bitter-cold has two functions. The first function is the draining Heart fire which has the result of also draining Liver fire. In Five Elements theory this is draining the fire-child (Heart) of wood-mother (Liver). When Liver fire is drained it will no longer attack the Stomach. The second function is clearing Stomach fire, which when drained will direct the Stomach qi down to treat acid reflux. The herb huang lian simultaneously treats both the root and branch of the disorder. The deputy herb wu zhu yu, which is acrid-hot, promotes qi movement to release stasis by dispersing the Liver. wu zhu yu also directs rebellious qi of the Stomach downward. The dosage of huang lian is six times the dosage of wu zhu yu. This allows the hot nature of the deputy herb to be moderated by the cold nature of the chief herb huang lian. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 205",
      "exp_hant": "此方清瀉肝熱,降逆氣,止嘔吐。君藥黃連苦寒,具有兩種功用。第一種功用是瀉心火,其結果也連帶瀉肝火。以五行理論而言,這是瀉子(心屬火)以奪母(肝屬木)之實。當肝火被瀉除後,便不再犯胃。第二種功用是清胃火,胃火得清後可使胃氣下降,以治療反酸。黃連同時治療本病的標與本。臣藥吳茱萸辛熱,能行氣散結以疏肝,吳茱萸亦能引胃之逆氣下行。黃連的劑量為吳茱萸的六倍,如此可使臣藥燥熱之性受君藥黃連寒涼之性所調節。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 205"
