      "exp_en": "The 8-Principles diagnosis is Channel-Collateral with an Interior pattern, Hot, Excess. The etiology is Invasion by External Pathogenic Wind. The channel pattern is Heat Stagnation in Yang Ming and Shao Yang Channels (windstroke). The organ pattern is some Heat Stagnation in the Yang Organs. The treatment principle is Expel Pathogenic Wind-Heat and Remove Obstruction from the Channel-Collaterals. The local facial points of the prescription remove local obstruction and regulate local qi and blood circulation. Yang ming points are chosen because these channels affect the face. LI-11 clears heat, harmonizes ying and wei qi, and removes wind from the collaterals. GB-20 removes wind and relieves symptoms of the head and eyes. TB-7 removes channel obstruction, promotes local circulation of qi and blood, and alleviates pain. GB-8 is a local point that also clears heat arising from stagnation in the shao yang channel. When the patient returned complaining of dizziness after her facial symptoms resolved, she was treated for heat stagnation in the shao yang and yang ming channels disrupting the organs and the Spirit. The treatment principle was to Clear Heat form the Yang Organs and Calm the Shen. GB-20 and LI-11 were selected to clear heat in shao yang and yang ming. DU-6 was selected to clear the heat from the middle burner. HT-7 was selected to calm the Shen which was agitated from the excess heat. The prescription with ST-40 focuses on tonifying the Spleen-Stomach to resolve dampness and phlegm (heavy head, dizziness, slippery pulse, thick tongue coating). It does not directly address the Shen disturbance (nightmares, insomnia, restlessness) nor the shao yang obstruction and heat (dry mouth, dry tongue coating, right sided headache). The prescription with LR-8 focuses on Liver Blood deficiency which is not a consideration in this case. The prescription with REN-4 focuses on tonifying Heart Yin and Calming the Mind which does not address the yang ming and shao yang heat. In terms of western medicine, the MRI was used to rule out Cranial Nerves VII and VIII schwannomas (tumors composed of Schwann cells, which normally produce the insulating myelin sheath). The Audiometry test was used to rule out internal and/or auditory canal tumors. Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi, Pages 127-132",
      "exp_hant": "八綱辨證為經絡病證屬裡證、熱證、實證。病因為外感風邪侵襲。經絡證型為陽明與少陽經熱鬱(中風/面癱)。臟腑證型為陽經略有熱鬱。治療原則為袪除外感風熱、疏通經絡阻滯。處方中的局部面部穴位可疏通局部阻滯,調理局部氣血循環。選用陽明經穴位,是因為此經影響面部。曲池(LI-11)清熱,調和營衛,袪除絡脈之風。風池(GB-20)袪風,緩解頭部與眼部症狀。會宗(TB-7)疏通經絡阻滯,促進局部氣血循環,並止痛。率谷(GB-8)為局部穴位,亦能清瀉少陽經鬱結所生之熱。當病患顏面症狀消退後回診主訴頭暈時,治療是針對少陽與陽明經熱鬱擾及臟腑與神明的病機。治療原則為清瀉陽經之熱、安神定志。取風池與曲池以清瀉少陽與陽明之熱。取脊中以清中焦之熱。取神門以安撫因實熱擾動而躁動的心神。以豐隆為主的處方著重於健運脾胃以化濕祛痰(頭重、頭暈、脈滑、舌苔厚),並未直接處理心神擾動(噩夢、失眠、躁動)或少陽經之鬱結與熱象(口乾、舌苔乾、右側頭痛)。以曲泉為主的處方著重於肝血虛,而此病例中並無此考量。以關元為主的處方著重於補心陰安神,並未處理陽明與少陽的熱象。就西醫角度而言,MRI檢查用於排除第七與第八對腦神經許旺細胞瘤(schwannoma,由通常負責產生髓鞘的許旺細胞所構成的腫瘤)。聽力檢查(Audiometry)則用於排除內耳道及/或聽道腫瘤。Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi, Pages 127-132"
    },
