      "exp_en": "The pin yin for radix aconiti is fu zi . Fu zi also goes by the common name of monkshood. Fu zi has strong warming properties, more so than ginger. Fu zi warms the yang and relieves deficient cold. It is only to be used when cold symptoms are caused by persistent and chronic yang deficiency. Fu zi is acrid, hot, and toxic. It can return the yang, supplement fire, aid the yang, disperse cold, and stop pain. Moxa with fu zi is selected to treat any kind of yang vacuity, premature ejaculation, seminal emission, wounds that will not close, and chronic tooth pain due to Kidney vacuity. A coin-sized cake is made from fu zi powder mixed with alcohol or hot water. Make a cake about 0.5 cm (0.19 inch) thick. Several holes are punched through the cake to allow the heat to penetrate through. Moxa with a flat base and pointed tip is placed on top of the cake and ignited. Remove the burnt moxa and place another cone. Repeat the process until the surrounding skin area is red. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 365; CAM, 4th Edition, page 440-441; Moxibustion: A Modern Clinical Handbook, Wilcox, 2018, page 83",
