      "exp_en": "This is the most accurate aswer. The HIPAA Privacy Rules allow a physician to leave a message directly with a family member or companion of the patient. Physicians are allowed to disclose information regarding care of the patient to a family members or friends, even if the patient is not present or has not given the physician permission, as long as the professional judgment of the physician concludes that the disclosure is in the best interest of the patient unless the patient has directly asked the physician not to do so. On the other hand, a physician should not share patient information with the family members or friends if the physician professionally believes a disclosure would be inappropriate. In leaving voice mail messages, the privacy of the patient must be protected and the information be limited necessary to confirm the appointment time or to request that the patient call the office. Unless the patient specifically requests that postcards should not be sent or that mail from the physician be sent to an alternate address, it is OK to send postcard appointment reminders. www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "此為最正確的答案。HIPAA隱私規則允許醫師直接向患者的家屬或陪同者留言。即使患者不在場或未給予明確同意，醫師仍可向家屬或朋友透露有關患者照護的資訊，只要醫師依專業判斷認為此揭露符合患者的最佳利益，且患者未曾明確要求醫師不要這麼做。另一方面，若醫師依專業判斷認為揭露資訊並不恰當，則不應向家屬或朋友分享患者資訊。留語音訊息時，須保護患者隱私，內容僅限於確認預約時間或請患者回電辦公室所需的必要資訊。除非患者特別要求不寄送明信片，或要求將郵件寄至其他地址，否則寄送明信片提醒預約是可以的。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
