      ],
      "exp_en": "The first clinical presentation indicates an external wind-heat pattern. The points LI-4 and LI-11 release the exterior and clear heat. DU-14 clears heat. BL-12 expel exterior wind and TB-5 releases the exterior. The heat from the external wind-heat pattern has traveled internally and has affected the Lungs. This can be seen as a Lung Heat pattern or a Lung pattern within the qi level. The heat has impaired the descending qi function of the lung causing cough and breathlessness. Thirst, being hot and the red tongue with a yellow coating reflect the internal heat. In this case the overflowing-rapid pulse reflects full heat. An overflowing pulse extends beyond the pulse position, is superficial, and feels that it overflows the normal pulse channel. The chest ache is due to heat obstructing the flow of qi in the chest. In the prescription, LU-5 and LU-10 clear Lung heat. LU-7 descends the Lung qi. LI-11 clears heat. BL-13 clears Lung heat and descends Lung qi. In the third clinical presentation the Lung heat has injured the yin fluids, which was already weakened as evidenced by her menopause. The internal Lung heat aggravated her yin deficiency and burned up the Lung yin. The drying up of fluids (dry throat, dry skin, dry stools) resulted in a malnourishment of the muscles leading to atrophy syndrome (wei syndrome). In her situation, she was unable to walk normally and the atrophy did not progress to paralysis. The treatment principle is to clear Lung heat, nourish yin, tonify leg yangming. In this patient both the root (yin xu, Lung heat) and the branch (leg yangming weakness) are treated simultaneously. The weakness in yangming arises from the yin xu and the Lung heat injuring fluids. KI-3 nourishes yin. LU-5 clears Lung heat. ST-36, ST-31, and ST-41 on the left side tonify leg yangming to treat leg weakness. The classical text Plain Questions recommends using mainly yangming points in the treatment of wei syndrome. The Stomach is the source of acquired qi and the Stomach yangming channel is full of qi and blood. ST-36 tonifies the Stomach channel, ST-31 tonifies qi and blood in the leg and helps to facilitate walking and rasing the leg, and ST-41 facilitates lifting the foot when the foot drags. Other supporting points to treat atrophy of the lower leg include GB-30 (tonfies leg qi and blood), GB-34 (affects tendons), and GB-39 (affects marrow), The prescription with REN-4 focuses solely on tonifying Kidney and Lung yin and fails to address weakness in yangming. This prescription could be considered when the leg weakness has resolved. The prescription with LU-7 only focuses on clearing Lung heat and descending Lung qi. The prescription with LU-9 tonifies Lung yin but uses reducing technique on leg yangming which should be tonified. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 581, 584, 385; Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2nd Edition, page 1223, 1224; CAM, 2010, page 465, 467",
      "exp_hant": "第一次的臨床表現顯示外感風熱證。合谷（LI-4）與曲池（LI-11）解表清熱，大椎（DU-14）清熱，風門（BL-12）袪除外風，外關（TB-5）解表。此風熱之邪由外傳裡，影響及肺，可視為肺熱證，或屬氣分之肺證。熱邪影響肺氣肅降功能，導致咳嗽及氣短。口渴、發熱，以及舌紅苔黃，皆反映內熱。此案中洪數之脈反映實熱。洪脈脈體寬大超出正常脈位，浮取即得，感覺脈氣充盈溢出脈道。胸部悶痛乃因熱邪阻滯胸中氣機所致。此處方中，尺澤（LU-5）與魚際（LU-10）清肺熱，列缺（LU-7）降肺氣，曲池（LI-11）清熱，肺俞（BL-13）清肺熱並降肺氣。第三次臨床表現顯示肺熱已損傷陰液，而其陰液本因更年期而已顯不足。內在肺熱加重了原本的陰虛，並耗灼肺陰。津液枯涸（咽乾、皮膚乾燥、大便乾結）導致肌肉失於濡養，形成痿證。此患者的情況是無法正常行走，但痿證尚未進展至癱瘓。治療原則為清肺熱、養陰、補足陽明。此患者需標本同治：本為陰虛與肺熱，標為足陽明經之無力。陽明經無力乃因陰虛及肺熱傷津所致。太谿（KI-3）滋陰，尺澤（LU-5）清肺熱，左側足三里（ST-36）、髀關（ST-31）及解谿（ST-41）補益足陽明經以治療腿部無力。經典古籍《素問》建議治療痿證應以陽明經穴為主。胃為後天之氣血生化之源，足陽明胃經多氣多血。足三里補益胃經，髀關補益腿部氣血並助於行走與抬腿，解谿則有助於改善足下垂時的提足動作。其他可輔助治療下肢痿證的穴位包括環跳（GB-30，補益腿部氣血）、陽陵泉（GB-34，作用於筋）及懸鐘（GB-39，作用於髓）。以關元（REN-4）為主的處方僅著重於補益腎肺之陰，未能處理陽明經之無力，此方可用於腿部無力已緩解之後。以列缺（LU-7）為主的處方僅著重於清肺熱及降肺氣。以太淵（LU-9）為主的處方雖能補肺陰，卻對本應施補法的足陽明經使用瀉法。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 581, 584, 385; Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2nd Edition, page 1223, 1224; CAM, 2010, page 465, 467"
    },
