      "exp_hant": "此為提插法：進針後將針上提或下插，力道可輕可重。古籍（《靈樞》、《難經》及《八法歌》）對於何者屬補、何者屬瀉的記載並不一致。然而可以確定的是，緩慢進針及提插會產生較輕的刺激，而用力提插則產生較強的刺激。這些差異在臨床上具有明確的應用價值。Acupuncture: A Comprehensive Text, Bensky, 1981, page 521-522; CAM, 4th Edition, page 405-406"
    },
    {
      "number": 121,
      "question_en": "In a cardiac arrest the person has no heartbeat, is unresponsive and is",
      "question_hant": "心臟停止時，患者無心跳、無反應，且",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "gasping for air",
          "hant": "喘氣掙扎呼吸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "making high pitched gurgling sounds",
          "hant": "發出高頻咯咯聲",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "not breathing",
          "hant": "無呼吸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "not breathing or is gasping for air",
          "hant": "無呼吸或喘氣掙扎呼吸",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most accurate and complete answer. A cardiac arrest is not the same as a heart attack. However, a heart attack can lead to cardiac arrest. In a heart attack blood flow to the heart muscle is blocked. In a cardiac arrest the person collapses and becomes unresponsive. The heart stops beating when the electrical impulses that control the heartbeat become irregular or chaotic. When the heart stops beating breathing will soon stop or the person gasps for air. In an unresponsive person gasping in the absence of normal breathing is called agonal breaths which can occur when the heart has stopped beating. Agonal breaths is not breathing but is a sign of cardiac arrest as the person has no heartbeat. Agonal breathing describes struggling to breathe or gasping. It is often a sign of a severe medical emergency, such as stroke or cardiac arrest. The gasping associated with agonal breathing is real breathing. It is a brainstem reflex. Agonal breathing often occurs because the heart is no longer circulating oxygen-rich blood. First Aid/CPR/AED, Participant Manual, Red Cross, 2016, page 40",
      "exp_hant": "此為最準確且完整的答案。心臟停止（cardiac arrest）與心臟病發作（heart attack）並不相同，但心臟病發作可能導致心臟停止。心臟病發作時，流向心肌的血流受阻；心臟停止時，患者會倒下並失去反應。當控制心跳的電訊號變得不規則或紊亂時，心臟便會停止跳動。心臟停止跳動後，呼吸會很快停止，或患者會出現喘氣掙扎呼吸的情形。在無反應的患者身上，若在無正常呼吸下出現喘氣，稱為瀕死呼吸，這可能發生在心臟已停止跳動時。瀕死呼吸並非真正的呼吸，而是心臟停止的徵象，因為此時患者已無心跳。瀕死呼吸的表現為呼吸掙扎或喘氣，通常是嚴重醫療緊急狀況（如中風或心臟停止）的徵象。瀕死呼吸伴隨的喘氣是一種真實的呼吸動作，屬於腦幹反射。瀕死呼吸的發生通常是因為心臟已無法再輸送富含氧氣的血液。First Aid/CPR/AED, Participant Manual, Red Cross, 2016, page 40"
    },
