      "exp_en": "The 8-Principles diagnosis is Interior, Excess, Heat. The diagnosis according to etiology is Pathogenic Fire. The organ pattern diagnosis is Liver Fire Scorching the Lung. The treatment principle is Remove Lung Heat, Stop Coughing, Sedate Liver Fire. The treatment principle is to sedate Liver fire, remove Lung heat, and stop coughing. The original treatment just focused on clearing lung heat and alleviating coughing. REN-22 regulates the Lung qi , treats the upward distending sensation in the lung, and Clears Heat. ST-25 regulates the descending function of the Large Intestine and, by alleviating constipation, removes heat from the hand yang ming. LU-6, the xi-cleft point, regulates the Lung descending function, Clears Heat, and treats the bloody sputum. LU-5 removes Heat from the Blood Level (the point can be bled to draw heat from the blood). The preceding prescription did not address the Liver (Liver attacks the Lung) as evidenced by the result of the treatment. To that effect, LR-2, the ying-spring point, was added to remove Liver Fire. GB-34 was selected to remove Liver and Gall Bladder heat. Both these points, one on yin channel and the other on a yang channel, is strong combination for removing heat in the Liver. The other Rx do not address the Liver involvement in the diagnosis. In terms of western medicine, body temp and WBCs are elevated. BP is also slightly elevated. Pertussis bordetella is the bacteria associated with pertussis or whooping cough. Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi, Pages 26-29",
