      "exp_en": "Amphetamines are a group of synthetic psychoactive drugs called central nervous system stimulants (CNS). The collective group of amphetamines includes amphetamine, dextroamphetamine, and methamphetamine. Medications containing amphetamines are prescribed for narcolepsy, obesity, and attention deficit/hyperactivity disorder. Amphetamines release the neurotransmitters dopamine and norepinephrine and their reuptake is inhibited. This results in a buildup of these neurotransmitters at synapses in the brain which increases mental focus, concentration, and wakefullness. Short-term effects include high body temperature, dry mouth, dilated pupils, decreased appetite, increased heart rate, increased blood pressure, euphoria, and talkativeness. Long-term effects include psychosis, cardiac arrhythmias, repetitive movements, convulsions, coma, malnutrition, skin disorders, and flushed or pale skin. LSD is an hallucinogen. Heroin is an opiate. Benzodiazepines such as Valium are CNS depressants. tcmtests.com, February 2019",
      "exp_hant": "安非他命是一類合成的精神活性藥物，屬於中樞神經系統興奮劑（CNS）。安非他命這一類藥物包括安非他命、右旋安非他命及甲基安非他命。含安非他命成分的藥物可用於治療嗜睡症、肥胖症及注意力不足過動症。安非他命會促使神經傳導物質多巴胺與正腎上腺素釋放，並抑制其再吸收，導致這些神經傳導物質在腦部突觸處堆積，進而提升專注力、注意力與清醒程度。短期作用包括體溫升高、口乾、瞳孔放大、食慾降低、心跳加快、血壓升高、欣快感及多話。長期作用則包括精神病、心律不整、重複性動作、抽搐、昏迷、營養不良、皮膚病變，以及皮膚潮紅或蒼白。LSD屬於迷幻劑。海洛因屬於鴉片類藥物。苯二氮平類藥物（如煩寧）則屬於中樞神經抑制劑。tcmtests.com, February 2019"
