      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. It is a function of the Liver and not the sanjiao to control the free flow of qi especially in the Spleen, Stomach, and Intestines while the sanjiao function of qi penetration extends to all organs, especially body cavities (the Liver has no such function). The Lungs' control of the ascending/descending and entering/exiting of qi is mostly in the Upper Burner while the sanjiao exerts this influence on all the organs. This is one of the three functions of the sanjiao: The sanjiao controls the transportation and penetration of qi. Qi can have a directional flow. The Spleen qi ascends while the Stomach qi descends. The Lung qi descends. The qi in each channel flows in an ascending-descending sequence. Qi also enters and exits the organs and body structures. The qi enters and exits the space between the muscles and the skin, an area called the cou li space. Qi enters and exits body cavities. The sanjiao ensures that the qi passes through and has a free passage in all of the cavities and organs. The sanjiao controls the movement and passage of the zong qi (Gathering qi) of the Upper Burner, the ying qi (nutritive qi) of the Middle Burner, and the wei qi (Defensive qi) of the Lower Burner. Though the wei qi works through the Upper Burner, the wei qi originates the Lower Burner from the ming men (Gate of Life). The point SJ-6 (zhi gou) activates the sanjiao function of transportation and penetration of qi. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 221",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。疏泄氣機主要是肝的功能，而非三焦的功能，尤其是對脾、胃、腸的疏泄作用；三焦通行氣機的功能則遍及全身各臟腑，尤其是各體腔（肝並無此功能）。肺主氣之升降出入，主要作用於上焦，而三焦則對全身臟腑均有此影響。這是三焦三大功能之一：三焦主司氣的運行與通行。氣具有方向性的運行，脾氣主升，胃氣主降，肺氣主降。各經脈之氣依序升降運行。氣亦於臟腑及身體組織間出入，氣於肌肉與皮膚之間出入之處稱為腠理，氣亦於體腔間出入。三焦確保氣能通行無阻，並於各體腔及臟腑間自由往來。三焦主司上焦宗氣、中焦營氣及下焦衛氣的運行與通行。衛氣雖運行於上焦，但其源頭則發自下焦命門。SJ-6（支溝）能激發三焦通行氣機之功能。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 221"
