      "question_hant": "患者出現急性後頭痛、微熱、頸項強直、畏寒、流涕、噴嚏，脈浮緊。何者為其病本（本）？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "External wind",
          "hant": "外風",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "cold",
          "hant": "寒",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Wind",
          "hant": "風",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Wind-Cold",
          "hant": "風寒",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In TCM there is a saying: \"To treat a disease, find the Root\". The practitioner needs to be able to look at the clinical manifestations and trace them back to their root (ben) which is primary in relation to clinical symptoms and signs (biao). A patient with headache, stiff neck, slight fever, fear of cold, runny nose, sneezing, and floating-tight pulse are all manifestations which point to the root (wind-cold). Treating the root (expelling wind-cold from the superficial layer) restores the diffusing-descending function of Lung qi and resolve all the symptoms. The practitioner treats the root (wind-cold) and not the individual symptoms (e.g. runny nose, headache). Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 1175; 2005 Edition, page 1119",
      "exp_hant": "中醫有言：「治病必求於本」。醫者須能從臨床表現追溯其病本（本），本相對於臨床症狀與體徵（標）而言居於主導地位。此患者出現頭痛、頸項強直、微熱、畏寒、流涕、噴嚏及脈浮緊，皆為指向病本（風寒）之表現。治本（袪除表層風寒）可恢復肺氣宣降之功能，進而解除所有症狀。醫者所治者為病本（風寒），而非個別症狀（如流涕、頭痛）。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 1175; 2005 Edition, page 1119"
    },
    {
      "number": 150,
      "question_en": "In wet cupping, what should the practitioner do?",
      "question_hant": "施行濕拔罐（刺絡拔罐）時，執業者應如何操作？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "wear gloves and eye protection when applying cups",
          "hant": "施罐時配戴手套及護目裝備",
