        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "chemicals that destroy the DNA",
          "hant": "能破壞DNA的化學物質",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "a procedure that destroys all microbial life",
          "hant": "能殺滅所有微生物的處理程序",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "An agent that destroys viruses",
          "hant": "能殺滅病毒的製劑",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Both antiseptics and disinfectants eliminate disease-causing pathogens. The difference between the two is how each is used. Antiseptics are applied to living skin or tissue to prevent infection. Disinfectants are applied to surfaces or other inanimate objects. Disinfectants are stronger and more toxic. Sterilization kills or removes all living organisms (viruses, bacteria, cells) from an object. Disinfection kills disease-causing organisms, but not all organisms present on an object. Heat, radiation, or chemical processes are used to sterilize objects (medical instruments). Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 227",
      "exp_hant": "抗菌劑與消毒劑皆能消滅致病病原體，兩者差異在於使用方式：抗菌劑用於活體皮膚或組織以預防感染；消毒劑則用於物體表面等非生物體，效力較強且毒性較高。滅菌是殺滅或去除物體上所有生物（病毒、細菌、細胞）；消毒則僅殺滅致病微生物，並非物體上所有微生物皆被消滅。滅菌物品（如醫療器械）常使用熱、輻射或化學方式處理。Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 227"
