        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Each sharps container must either be labeled with the universal biohazard symbol and the word \"biohazard\" or be color-coded red. Sharps containers shall be maintained upright throughout use, replaced routinely, and not be allowed to overfill. When removing sharps containers from the area of use, the containers shall be: 1) Closed immediately prior to removal or replacement to prevent spillage or protrusion of contents during handling, storage, transport, or shipping. 2) Placed in a secondary container if leakage is possible. The second container shall be a) closable, b) constructed to contain all contents and prevent leakage during handling, storage, transport, or shipping, and c) labeled or color-coded. Reusable containers shall not be opened, emptied, or cleaned manually or in any other manner which would expose employees to the risk of percutaneous injury. Upon closure, duct tape may be used to secure the lid of a sharps container as long as the tape does not serve as the lid itself. Sharps containers must be easily accessible to employees and located as close as feasible to the immediate area where sharps are used or can be reasonably anticipated to be found. Sharps containers can be made from a variety of products from cardboard to plastic. As long as they meet the definition of a sharps container, (containers must be closable, puncture resistant, leakproof on sides and bottom, and labeled or color-coded), then OSHA would consider them to be of an acceptable composition. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 61",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。每個利器容器必須標示通用生物危害標誌及「biohazard（生物危害）」字樣，或以紅色作為顏色標示。利器容器於使用期間須保持直立，並定期更換，不可任其過滿。將利器容器自使用區域移出時，須符合下列規定：1）於移動或更換前立即封閉，以防止內容物於搬運、儲存、運輸或寄送過程中溢出或突出。2）若有滲漏可能，須置於第二層容器內；第二層容器須：a）可封閉，b）其構造須能容納所有內容物並防止於搬運、儲存、運輸或寄送過程中滲漏，且c）須有標示或顏色標示。可重複使用之容器不得以人工方式或任何可能使工作人員暴露於經皮損傷風險之方式開啟、清空或清潔。容器封閉後，可使用膠帶固定容器蓋，惟膠帶本身不得作為蓋子使用。利器容器須讓工作人員易於取用，並盡可能設置於利器實際使用或可合理預期出現的區域附近。利器容器可由紙板至塑膠等多種材質製成，只要符合利器容器的定義（須可封閉、防穿刺、上下側面均不滲漏，並有標示或顏色標示），OSHA即視其材質為可接受。Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 61"
    },
