      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Kidney Yang Deficiency with Water Overflowing to Heart. The weak Kidney yang (back pain, edema, tinnitus) fails to transform Body Fluids which then accumulate to affect the Heart (palpitations, cold hands, breathlessness). The expected pulse in this pattern is a Deep-Slow-Weak pulse. This pulse indicates Internal, Cold, and Deficiency respectively. The expected tongue is pale (empty cold from yang xu) and swollen-wet (failure to transform body fluids leading to accumulation of dampness). A Long pulse tends to indicate Heat. A Tight pulse can indicate either exterior or interior cold depending on how it is paired with other pulse qualities (floating, deep, full). Ankle edema, breathlessness, palpitations, and deep-slow pulse are sufficient to diagnose Kidney Yang Deficiency with Water Overflowing to Heart. The treatment principle is Tonify and Warm Kidney Yang, Transform Water, Tonify Spleen Yang, and Tonify Heart Yang. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 635; 2005 Edition, page 601; 1989 Edition, page 257",
      "exp_hant": "診斷為腎陽虛、水氣凌心。腎陽虛弱（腰痛、水腫、耳鳴）無法運化水液，水液積聚而上凌於心（心悸、手冷、氣短）。此證預期脈象為沉遲弱脈，此脈分別提示裡證、寒證及虛證。預期舌象為舌淡（陽虛所致之虛寒）且胖嫩濕潤（水液運化失常，濕邪積聚）。長脈多主熱證。緊脈則可依其與其他脈象特徵（浮、沉、實）的搭配，提示表寒或裡寒。足踝水腫、氣短、心悸及沉遲脈已足以診斷為腎陽虛、水氣凌心。治療原則為溫補腎陽、化氣行水、補脾陽、補心陽。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 635; 2005 Edition, page 601; 1989 Edition, page 257"
    },
