      "exp_en": "From a biomedical standpoint, this patient has contracted a bout of food poisoning. From a Chinese medical perspective, this patient has contracted a wind-cold invasion with a pre-existing internal dampness causing the digestive upset. For this pattern, huo xiang zheng qi san is the correct prescription. Ping wei san treats a pattern of cold-damp in the middle burner. The floating and soft pulse suggests that this is not the current pattern for this patient. Huang lian jie du tang is inappropriate as this treats heat toxicity in the body and there is no indication that there is heat in this pattern. Xiao chai hu tang treats a pathogen in the shao yang stage, but the floating pulse suggests that it is still on the exterior. Typically, a wiry pulse will be present for this diagnosis. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 687-688; 691-694; 167-169; 104-109",
      "exp_hant": "從西醫角度而言，此患者罹患了一次食物中毒。從中醫角度而言，此患者感受風寒外邪，並兼有原本內蘊之濕邪，因而導致消化功能失調。此證型的正確處方為藿香正氣散。平胃散主治中焦寒濕證，然浮軟之脈顯示此並非該患者目前之證型。黃連解毒湯並不適合，因其主治體內熱毒，而此證並無熱象表現。小柴胡湯主治邪在少陽，然浮脈顯示邪仍在表，此診斷通常應見弦脈。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 687-688; 691-694; 167-169; 104-109"
