      "exp_en": "The Chief herbs are gui zhi and fu ling. The Deputy herb is shao yao. The Assistant herbs are tao ren and mu dan pi. The Envoy herb is honey. The main actions of the formula are to invigorate blood, transform blood stasis, and reduce fixed abdominal masses. The chief herbs are gui zhi and fu ling. The herb gui zhi is acrid-warm and unblocks the blood vessels and moves blood stasis by promoting blood circulation. The herb fu ling leaches downward to promote the downward circulation of blood when there is blood stasis. The herb fu ling also nourishes Heart and Spleen qi, calms the Heart and spirit to help calm the fetus. The herb fu ling also helps to transform phlegm to promote urination because phlegm-dampness can be associated with the formation masses or blockages due to blood stagnation. The deputy herb is shao yao and the type used depends on the condition. The herb chi shao promotes blood circulation to alleviates stasis while the herb bai shao relaxes spasms and relieves abdominal pain. Both can be used if needed. The assistant herbs tao ren and mu dan pi transform blood stasis, clear constraint heat, break up blood stasis, reduces fixed abdominal masses, and moves accumulation. Honey is used making the pills. The honey acts as an envoy which moderates the harshness of the other herbs which dispel blood stasis. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 583",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為桂枝與茯苓。臣藥為芍藥。佐藥為桃仁與牡丹皮。使藥為蜂蜜。本方的主要功效為活血化瘀、消癥塊。君藥為桂枝與茯苓。桂枝辛溫，能通利血脈，藉由促進血液循環以行血化瘀。茯苓滲利下行，在血瘀時促進血液向下運行。茯苓亦能滋養心脾之氣，寧心安神以助安胎。茯苓還能化痰利水，因為痰濕常與血瘀所致的癥塊或阻塞相關。臣藥為芍藥，依病情選用不同品種：赤芍活血化瘀，白芍緩急止腹痛，兩者可視情況並用。佐藥桃仁與牡丹皮能化瘀血、清鬱熱、破血消癥、行積滯。蜂蜜用於製丸。蜂蜜為使藥，能緩和其他祛瘀藥物之峻烈之性。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 583"
