      "exp_en": "The patient can have burning diarrhea or no bowel movements. The main actions of the formula are harmonize and release shao yang and drain internal clumping due to heat. This disorder ahs a concurrent shao yang and yang ming patterns. The alternating fever and chills, chest fullness, hypochondriac fullness, bitter mouth taste and wiry pulse are reflection of shao yang. The hard focal distention, no bowel movement or hot burning diarrhea, and yellow tongue coating and forceful pulse are a reflection of yang ming. These yang ming symptoms and signs indicate that the pathogenic factor has moved deeper into the body. When compared to a pure shao yang pattern, the heat here is more severe and constrained. The more severe heat is reflected in the continuous and uncontrolled vomiting, melancholy, and irritability. In this pattern there can also be a flooding and excess pulse. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 286",
      "exp_hant": "患者可能出現灼熱下利，亦可能大便不通。本方的主要功效為和解少陽、內瀉熱結。此病證兼有少陽與陽明兩種證候。往來寒熱、胸脅苦滿、口苦、脈弦，皆為少陽證之表現。硬滿拒按、大便不通或下利灼熱、舌苔黃、脈有力，則反映陽明證。這些陽明證候顯示邪氣已深入體內。與單純少陽證相較，此處熱勢更為嚴重且鬱結。更嚴重的熱象表現為持續不止的嘔吐、情緒抑鬱與煩躁。此證亦可見洪脈或實脈。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 286"
