    {
      "number": 232,
      "question_en": "A patient is on the second day of fever, feeling thirsty, and constipated. The Su wen states, \"The first day is Tai Yang, the second day is Yang Ming, and the third day is Shao Yang\". This suggests that one can know at which stage a disease is at by the number of days it has been present. Does the Shan Han Lun support or refute that this patient is in Yang Ming because of the two days?",
      "question_hant": "一位患者發熱已第二天，感到口渴且便秘。《素問》記載：「一日太陽，二日陽明，三日少陽」。此說法暗示可依發病天數判斷病邪所在的階段。《傷寒論》是支持還是反駁「此患者因病程已兩日而屬陽明」的說法？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Zhang Zhong Jing supports this claim, and as a scholar of classical medicine, follows strictly the principles in the Huang Di Nei Jing",
          "hant": "張仲景支持此說法，身為古典醫學學者，嚴格遵循《黃帝內經》之原則",
