          "hant": "張仲景反駁此說法，而以邪氣之盛衰、正氣強弱及治療是否得當作為判斷依據",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Zhang Zhong Jing refutes this claim instead writing that the pernicious spends two days at each stage according to his clinical observations",
          "hant": "張仲景反駁此說法，並依其臨床觀察指出邪氣在每一階段皆停留兩日",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Zhang Zhong Jing supports this claim based on his clinical experience during the plagues in which the transmission of disease was rapid",
          "hant": "張仲景支持此說法，其依據為瘟疫流行期間疾病傳變迅速的臨床經驗",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In line 270 of the Shao Yang chapter, it states \"[When] cold damage [has lasted] three days, the three yang [channels] have all been run through, and the three yin [channels] should contract the evil, [but] instead, the person is able to eat and retching is absent, which means that the three yin will not contract the evil.\" Although this appears to support the statement from the Su Wen, it actually opposes it and relies throughout the Shang Han Lun text on other factors such as the strength of the pathogenic factor versus the anti-pathogenic factor as well as transmuted patterns due to improper treatments. Although Zhang Zhong Jing truly was the highest of scholars and did intently study the Nei Jing, it was vague and basic as it relates to the contraction of external evils and the progression of external diseases. The plagues that happened during Zhang's time reinforces the principle of the strength of the pernicious being a major factor in the fast transmission of the diseases during that time. One of the major themes coming out of the Shang Han Lun is that there is no set way in which disease moves forward. Zhang himself states in his preface that one who follows every word of the Shang Han Lun will be successful in treatment only half of the time. There are so many factors that can confound cases and lead to success or failure in the clinical setting. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 443.",
      "exp_hant": "《傷寒論》少陽篇第270條記載：「傷寒三日，三陽為盡，三陰當受邪，其人反能食而不嘔，此為三陰不受邪也。」此條文表面上似乎支持《素問》之說法，實則反駁之，並在《傷寒論》全書中皆以邪正盛衰及誤治所致的傳變等因素作為判斷依據。雖然張仲景確實是醫學大家，對《內經》有深入的研究，但《內經》對於外邪感受及外感病傳變的論述較為籠統而基礎。張仲景所處時代的瘟疫流行，更加印證了邪氣之盛衰乃是當時疾病快速傳變的重要因素。《傷寒論》的一大核心思想，即疾病傳變並無固定規律。張仲景本人在自序中亦言，若拘泥於《傷寒論》每一字句而不知變通，治療成功的機率僅有一半。臨床上有太多因素會使病情變得複雜，進而影響治療的成敗。Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 443."
