      "exp_en": "Huai hua san treats either wind heat or damp-heat lodged in the intestines and stomach leading to heat toxicity and bloody stools. This patient's main concern is to stop bleeding and as the formula will serve to treat the pattern causing the bloody stools, using the charred version of jing jie will increase the formula's ability to stop bleeding. Combining the formula with bai tou weng tang is used when there is a case of amebic dysentery. These cases typically originate from areas of warm climates and considering he first got sick while on an ice mountain climbing trip, this is unlikely. Adding zhi zi and huang qin is indicated for vigorous liver heat pouring downwards into the intestines. Without a wiry pulse, this situation does not seem likely. Ce bai ye is a very important herb in the formula to stop bleeding. Taking this herb out of the formula would be counterproductive to this patient's condition. Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 605-606",
      "exp_hant": "槐花散治療風熱或濕熱蘊結腸胃，導致熱毒下注而便血之證。此患者最主要的訴求為止血，本方既能治療導致便血的證型，使用炒炭後的荊芥穗更能增強止血之效。與白頭翁湯合用適用於阿米巴痢疾病例，此類病例通常源自溫暖氣候地區，考量患者最初是在攀登冰山旅行時發病，此情況並不太可能。加梔子與黃芩適用於肝火熾盛、下注腸道之證，若無弦脈，此情況似乎不太可能。側柏葉是本方中極為重要的止血藥，將此藥去除將不利於此患者的病情。Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 605-606"
