      "exp_en": "The Chief herbs are chai hu and da huang. The Deputy herbs are huang qin and zhi si. The Assistant herb is shao yao. The Envoy herbs are sheng jiang and da zao. The formula harmonizes and release shao yang and drains internal clumping due to heat. The formula focuses on the shao yang and yang ming stages. The treatment principle is to harmonize and to also drain down. Harmonization vents the pathogen in the exterior via shao yang. The draining expels internal knotting heat downward. The two chief herbs are chai hu and da huang. chai hu dredges shao yang and releases the exterior. da huang enters yang ming to drain heat and open the bowels. The two deputy herbs huang qin and zhi si amplify the actions of the chief herbs. The herb huang qin is bitter-cold and when combined with chai hu clears heat from shao yang and assists da huang in draining bowel heat. The herb zhi shi breaks up qi constraint to reduce focal distension and abdominal and chest fullness. When zhi shi is combined with chai hu there is a greater increase in the flow of qi. When zhi shi is combined with da huang there is an increase in the breaking up of bowel clumping. The assistant herb shao yao relaxes urgency and alleviates pain. Together with zhi shi and da huang, the herb shao yao alleviates excess pain in the abdomen. The other assistant herb is zhi ban xia which harmonizes the middle jiao and redirect rebellious Stomach qi down. When zhi ban xia is combined with the envoy herb sheng jiang they stop vomiting. The other envoy herb is da zao amplifies the ability of shao yao to soften the Liver and alleviate abdominal spasms. The combination of da zao and shao yao also protect the yin from being harmed by heat and from the draining nature of da huang and zhi shi. The combination of da zao and sheng jiang regulate the ying and wei qi to assist in the release of the pathogenic factor. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 286",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為柴胡與大黃。臣藥為黃芩與枳實。佐藥為芍藥。使藥為生薑與大棗。本方能和解少陽、內瀉熱結。本方著重於少陽與陽明兩個階段。治療原則為既和解又瀉下。和解能使邪氣由少陽透達於外，瀉下則能使內結之熱邪向下排出。兩味君藥為柴胡與大黃。柴胡疏達少陽、解表；大黃入陽明以瀉熱通便。兩味臣藥黃芩與枳實能增強君藥之功效。黃芩苦寒，與柴胡合用能清少陽之熱，並輔助大黃瀉腸腑之熱。枳實能破氣散結，以緩解痞滿及腹脹胸滿。枳實與柴胡合用能加強行氣之效；枳實與大黃合用則能加強破除腸腑積滯之效。佐藥芍藥能緩急止痛，與枳實、大黃合用，能緩解腹部之實痛。另一佐藥為製半夏，能和中降逆，導胃氣下行。製半夏與使藥生薑合用能止嘔。另一使藥為大棗，能加強芍藥柔肝緩急之效。大棗與芍藥合用亦能保護陰液，避免受到熱邪及大黃、枳實瀉下之性所傷。大棗與生薑合用能調和營衛，以助邪氣外解。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 286"
