      ],
      "exp_en": "Both formulas treat spontaneous perspiration and aversion to wind but with different clinical applications. The formula gui zhi tang is a formula that releases the exterior to treat external wind-cold due to an imbalance between the wei qi and ying qi. It treats patients who are actually experiencing the symptoms of an exterior pattern with deficiency (fever, aversion to cold, headache, stuffy nose, sweating, floating pulse). The formula yu ping feng san also treats sweating with aversion to cold but the symptoms are caused by a deficiency of wei qi failing to consolidate the exterior (leaking of sweat, frequent catching of colds, pale complexion, general weakness, deficient pulse). The formula yu ping feng san is appropriate for patients who frequently contract an exterior wind pattern but are not currently having any symptoms. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: The formula gui zhi tang is contraindicated in taiyang cold syndrome because gui zhi is too weak to expel excess cold, with wind-heat syndrome, with exterior cold and interior heat, absence of sweating with irritability, exterior excess disorder without perspiration, or early stages of febrile disorders (fever, sore throat, thirst), and with patients who drink alcohol as the formula can cause damp-heat. The formula yu ping feng san is contraindicated for those with excess patterns with patients who have night sweats from yin xu. Chinese Herbal Formulas and Applications, Chen and Chen, 2009, page 56",
      "exp_hant": "兩方皆能治療自汗惡風，但臨床應用有所不同。桂枝湯為解表劑，用於治療因營衛失調所致的外感風寒。此方適用於確實出現表虛證症狀的患者（發熱、惡寒、頭痛、鼻塞、汗出、脈浮）。玉屏風散亦能治療汗出惡寒，但其病因為衛氣虛弱、不能固表（自汗、易反覆感冒、面色蒼白、全身乏力、脈虛）。玉屏風散適用於經常感受外邪但目前並無症狀的患者。禁忌／注意事項：桂枝湯禁用於太陽傷寒證，因桂枝力薄，不足以祛除實寒；亦禁用於風熱證、表寒裡熱證、無汗而煩躁者、表實無汗者，或熱病初起（發熱、咽痛、口渴）；飲酒之患者亦應禁用，因本方可能導致濕熱。玉屏風散禁用於實證患者，及因陰虛所致盜汗者。Chinese Herbal Formulas and Applications, Chen and Chen, 2009, page 56"
