      "exp_en": "Some modern doctors says that the formula should only be prescribed when the pulse is empty and forceless and should not be prescribed when the pulse is forceful, firm, or wiry or when there is yin xu and hot blood, or during pregnancy. The formula breaks up and eliminates stagnant blood. It should not be used after a stroke due to cerebral bleeding. Unless the etiology for the stroke has been established and cerebral bleeding has been ruled out, the formula should not be prescribed. Before the formula is used in a stroke patient, the patients needs to have regained consciousness with normal body temperature, no bleeding, and the pulse is moderate. The main actions of the formula are to tonify qi, invigorate blood, and unblock the channels. The TCM diagnosis is qi xu leading to blood stagnation blocking the channels. The formula also treats atrophy disorders. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 568",
      "exp_hant": "部分現代醫家指出，本方僅應用於脈虛而無力之患者，若脈有力、堅實或弦，或有陰虛血熱之證，或值妊娠期間，皆不宜使用本方。本方能破血逐瘀。腦出血性中風後不應立即使用本方。除非已確認中風之病因並排除腦出血，否則不應處方本方。中風患者在使用本方之前，須已恢復神智清醒、體溫正常、無出血現象，且脈象和緩。本方的主要功效為補氣、活血、通絡。中醫診斷為氣虛血瘀，阻滯經絡。本方亦可治療痿證。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 568"
