      "exp_en": "Nancy is suffering from Yin deficiency concurrent with her cough, as shown by her night sweats and the blood in her phlegm. The formula bai he gu jing tang would be the most appropriate formula to stop her cough, transform the phlegm, and nourish her yin. The formula bei mu gua lou san is also good for a dry cough, but it is best used when the phlegm is more severe than the dryness. The formula ma huang tang treats wheezing due to wind-cold attack. Its warm, disseminating properties would make it contra-indicated for her blood-streaked phlegm, and its diaphoretic nature would likely aggravate her night sweats. The formula sheng mai san is more appropriate for a cough due to concurrent Lung Yin and Qi deficiencies. Along with a dry and choking cough, there would likely be symptoms such as fatigue, shortness of breath, and spontaneous sweating rather than night sweats. Prolonged sweating and cough in this case produces a thready, deficient pulse. Rather than blood-streaked sputum, it would be sparse and difficult to expectorate. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 7, 8, 328, 384, 386, and 802",
      "exp_hant": "南希咳嗽兼有陰虛之證，表現為盜汗及痰中帶血。百合固金湯是最適合她病情的方劑，能止咳、化痰並滋陰。貝母瓜蔞散亦適合治療乾咳，但更適用於痰重於燥之證。麻黃湯治療風寒外襲所致的喘鳴，其溫散之性不適合痰中帶血之證，其發汗之性也可能加重盜汗。生脈散更適合治療肺之氣陰兩虛所致的咳嗽，除乾咳外，通常會伴有疲倦、氣短、自汗（而非盜汗）等症狀。此證若汗出咳嗽日久，脈象會呈現細而虛，痰量稀少且難以咳出，而非痰中帶血。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 7, 8, 328, 384, 386, and 802"
    },
    {
      "number": 243,
      "question_en": "Which herbs in ban xia bai zhu tian ma tang (pinellia, atractylodes, macrocephala, and gastrodia decoction) combine to simultaneously treat the root and the branch?",
      "question_hant": "半夏白朮天麻湯中，哪些藥物合用能同時治標與治本？",
