      "exp_en": "The Chief herbs are zhi ban xia and tian ma. The Deputy herb is bai zhu. The Assistant herb is fu ling and chen pi. The Envoy herb is gan cao. This formula strengthens the Spleen, dispels dampness, transforms phlegm, and extinguishes wind. The two chief herbs are zhi ban xia and tian ma. The herb zhi ban xi dries damp, transforms phlegm, and directs rebellious qi downward to alleviate nausea and vomiting. The herb tian ma enters the Liver channel to nourish yin fluids, calm the liver, and extinguish wind. Zhi ban xia directs turbid yin down to control rebellious qi but its acrid nature has the potential to stir up more wind which is counteracted by the moisten nature of tian ma which extinguishes wind. The deputy herb bai zhu reinforces the chief herbs transform phlegm. The warm nature of bai zhu tonifies the Spleen while its bitter nature dries damp, and its aromatic nature benefits the transportive and transformative functions of the earth (Spleen). Bai zhu also promotes water metabolism and generate fluids to deal with the fluid disorder which is the root of the pattern. The assistant herb is fu ling which tonifies the spleen and leaches out dampness. The combination of fu ling with the deputy herb bai zhu simultaneously treats the root and branch. The other assistant herb is chen pi which regulates qi through directing it down and also transforms phlegm. The envoy herb gan cao harmonises the other herbs and regulates the middle jiao. gan cao combined with sheng jiang and da zao harmonize the earth (Stomach and Spleen). Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 811",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為製半夏與天麻。臣藥為白朮。佐藥為茯苓與陳皮。使藥為甘草。本方能健脾、袪濕、化痰、息風。兩味君藥為製半夏與天麻。製半夏能燥濕化痰，並降逆氣以止嘔。天麻入肝經，能滋養陰液、平肝息風。製半夏能導濁陰下行以制逆氣，然其辛燥之性有可能助長風邪，此則以天麻之潤性息風加以制衡。臣藥白朮能增強君藥化痰之效。白朮性溫能補脾，味苦能燥濕，氣香則有益於脾之運化功能。白朮亦能促進水液代謝、生津，以治療本病之本──水液失調。佐藥茯苓能補脾滲濕。茯苓與臣藥白朮合用，能同時治療標與本。另一佐藥為陳皮，能理氣降逆，並兼能化痰。使藥甘草能調和諸藥並調理中焦。甘草與生薑、大棗合用，能調和脾胃（土）。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 811"
    },
