      "exp_en": "The formula zhen wu tang focuses mainly the lower burner and Kidneys while ling gui zhu gan tang focuses mainly on the middle burner and the Spleen. The formula zhen wu tang warms the yang and promotes urination. It treats the root of the pattern which is Kidney yang xu by strengthening and warming the gate of fire. The chief herb is zhi fu zi which is very hot, tonifies fire, and restores Kidney yang. The formula ling gui zhu gan tang focuses more on the middle burner and Spleen. It warms and transforms phlegm and thin mucus, strengthens the Spleen, and resolves dampness. The chief herb fu ling tonifies the Spleen and drains dampness. The formula zhen wu tang has edema, difficult urination, swollen pale tongue with teeth marks, slippery-white tongue coating, deep-deficient pulse. The formula ling gui zhu gan tang has chest fullness, SOB, pale swollen tongue, white-greasy tongue coating, and slippery pulse. Both formulas warm yang and open the water passages. Both formulas include fu ling (poria) and bai zhu (rhizoma atractylodes). Both formulas are used for regulate body fluids in yang deficient patients. Bensky does not have a contraindication for zhen wu tang but Chen and Chen note that it should not be used when there is extreme thirst. The contraindications for ling gui zhu gan tang are thin mucous due to Damp-Heat or hyperactive Liver yang. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 738, 744",
      "exp_hant": "真武湯主要著重於下焦與腎，而苓桂朮甘湯則主要著重於中焦與脾。真武湯能溫陽利水，藉由溫補命門之火以治療腎陽虛此一病本。君藥為製附子，性大熱，能補火助陽、恢復腎陽。苓桂朮甘湯則更著重於中焦與脾，能溫化痰飲、健脾、袪濕。君藥為茯苓，能健脾滲濕。真武湯證見水腫、小便不利、舌淡胖有齒痕、苔白滑、脈沉弱。苓桂朮甘湯證見胸滿、氣短、舌淡胖、苔白膩、脈滑。兩方皆能溫陽、通利水道。兩方皆含茯苓與白朮。兩方皆用於陽虛患者以調節體液。Bensky並未列出真武湯之禁忌，然陳氏夫婦指出，若患者極度口渴則不宜使用。苓桂朮甘湯之禁忌為濕熱所致的痰飲，或肝陽亢盛之證。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 738, 744"
