      "exp_en": "In Jue Yin stage conditions, yang qi return is necessary for a recovery from this stage. An excessive yang qi return will cause heat and engender great thirst (unabated by drinking fluids). In this case, yin qi is abating and yang qi is returning and therefore the thirst in this patient is not as great as the dispersion thirst caused by excessive heat. Since the thirst was relieved in this situation, this is a sign that the prognosis is positive and treatment is likely not necessary and the yang is returning. Giving small amounts of water a little at a time in these cases allows the yin and yang to return in balance. Giving amounts of water that are too large can cause the pattern to transmute into a pattern in which water will gather below the heart and cause palpitations. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 569.",
      "exp_hant": "厥陰病階段中，陽氣來復乃是自此階段康復的必要條件。若陽氣來復過度，則會化熱並產生劇渴（飲水亦無法緩解）。此病例中，陰氣漸退而陽氣漸復，因此患者的口渴程度並不如熱盛所致的消渴那般嚴重。由於此患者飲水後口渴得以緩解，此為預後良好之徵象，顯示治療可能非必要，且陽氣正在恢復。此類情況下少量分次飲水，可使陰陽恢復平衡。若飲水量過大，則可能使證型轉變，導致水停心下而引發心悸。Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 569."
