      ],
      "exp_en": "Long term supplementation of yin can lead to dampness in certain individuals who have a weak spleen. This patient likely has chronic spleen weakness as evidenced by his fatigue syndrome. Dampness in turn further weakens the spleen and can combine with any pre-existing cold to attack the middle burner. The formula to treat cold-damp in the middle jiao is Ping Wei San. Bao he wan treats food stagnation leading into heat and would likely have heat signs accompanying a history of overindulging in food (relative to spleen strength). Li zhong wan treats yang deficiency cold of the middle burner which this is not at this point. This may be a formula to have on hand should the condition worsen, but it is not appropriate for the patient at this time. Gui pi tang treats a dual deficiency of spleen qi and heart blood. This is not the patient's current pattern and is inappropriate. Gui pi tang can be overly cloying with herbs like long yan rou as an ingredient for damp predominant conditions. Formulas and Strategies pgs. 826-828; 257-260; 687-688; 353-355",
      "exp_hant": "長期滋陰對於某些脾虛體質者而言，可能導致濕邪內生。此患者的疲勞證候顯示其可能存在慢性脾虛。濕邪反過來又進一步損傷脾臟，並可能與既有的寒邪結合，侵犯中焦。治療中焦寒濕之方為平胃散。保和丸治療食積化熱，通常伴有熱象，其病史多與飲食過量（相對於脾之運化能力而言）有關。理中丸治療中焦陽虛寒證，此並非此患者目前之證型。此方或可留待病情惡化時使用，但目前並不適合此患者。歸脾湯治療脾氣與心血兩虛之證，並非此患者目前之證型，故不適合。歸脾湯中如龍眼肉等藥物較為滋膩，對於濕邪偏盛之證可能不利。Formulas and Strategies pgs. 826-828; 257-260; 687-688; 353-355"
    },
    {
      "number": 279,
      "question_en": "A 12 year-old girl arrived with her parents at your office complaining of stomach and shoulder pain. She had an appetite but also had difficulty eating, and was brought to you only after she vomited several times as she was trying to snack while quietly reading a book at home. She wore a sweater and scarf on a nice spring day for reasons she could not explain. Her pulse was thin and wiry. Her tongue had a greasy coating and a slight quiver. You prescribed the formula Wu Zhu Yu Tang (Evodia Decoction) for five days. She now returns to your office after completing your course of herbs reporting that her stomach pain is gone but her shoulder pain has increased. She also reports feeling slightly light-headed and tired. She feels stiff and achy in general and reports numbness in her fingers and toes. She is sweating lightly. Her pulse is moderate. Which of the following formulas is the best choice for this patient's current condition?",
      "question_hant": "一名12歲女孩由父母陪同前來就診，主訴胃痛及肩痛。她有食慾但進食困難，且在安靜讀書時嘗試吃零食後嘔吐數次，因此才被帶來就診。她在天氣宜人的春日仍穿著毛衣與圍巾，原因說不清楚。脈細而弦，舌苔膩且微顫。您處方吳茱萸湯五日份。她完成療程後回診，表示胃痛已消失，但肩痛加劇。她也主訴略感頭暈與疲倦。她全身感覺僵硬痠痛，並主訴手指與腳趾麻木。她正微微出汗。脈象和緩。以下何方最適合此患者目前的病情？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Juan Bi Tang (Remove Painful Obstruction Decoction)",
          "hant": "蠲痺湯",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "xiao chai hu tang (minor bupleurum decoction)",
          "hant": "小柴胡湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Zhen Wu Tang (True Warrior Decoction)",
          "hant": "真武湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "ren shen bai du san (ginseng powder to overcome pathogenic influences)",
          "hant": "人參敗毒散",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This patient originally suffered from stomach deficiency cold leading to abdominal pain and vomiting. In certain disorders of the stomach, the body's yang qi becomes impaired by the stomach's lack of ability to aid in the process of maintaining the body's yang balance. Without the proper functioning of the stomach, the body's wei qi becomes unrooted and the resulting ying/wei imbalance leads to a wind-cold-damp invasion leading to the shoulder pain (wind dominant bi syndrome-xing bi). In cases such as this, juan bi tang is indicated for its warming and tonifying and wind-damp expelling capabilities. It aims to rid the body of the pathogens while harmonizing the ying/wei qi. Zhen wu tang is for kidney water overflowing due to yang deficiency in the shao yin stage of the six stages. This is not appropriate at this time. Xiao chai hu tang is the main prescription for cold obstructing the shao yang stage of the six stages and is not appropriate for this patient at this time. Ren shen bai du san is the second best choice of the formulas presented in this case as it treats externally contracted wind-cold-damp (with an emphasis on dampness). In addition, for this formula, there is a deficiency of the Upright qi and it is unable to expel the pathogen. In the pattern for this formula, there will be no sweating due to dampness blocking sweat from leaving the body. If the patient took this formula, she would probably receive some symptomatic relief, however juan bi tang is the better choice. Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 261-264, 756-757, 744-747, 104-109, 47-49",
      "exp_hant": "此患者原本罹患胃虛寒證，導致腹痛與嘔吐。在某些胃部疾患中，因胃無法協助維持人體陽氣平衡，導致身體陽氣受損。胃功能失常時，人體衛氣失去根基，由此導致的營衛失調可引發風寒濕邪入侵而致肩痛（風邪偏盛之行痺）。在此類病例中，蠲痺湯因其溫補及袪風濕之功效而適用。此方旨在袪除病邪的同時調和營衛之氣。真武湯用於六經辨證中少陰階段陽虛所致的腎水泛濫，此時並不適用。小柴胡湯為六經辨證中少陽階段寒邪阻滯的主方，此時亦不適用於此患者。人參敗毒散是本病例中次佳的選擇，因其能治療外感風寒濕邪（尤重於濕）。此外，此方所治之證有正氣虧虛，無力袪邪之象。此方所治之證因濕邪阻遏汗液外泄而無汗。若此患者服用此方，或許能獲得部分症狀緩解，然而蠲痺湯仍是較佳的選擇。Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 261-264, 756-757, 744-747, 104-109, 47-49"
    },
    {
      "number": 280,
      "question_en": "A 12 year-old female comes to your office with a biomedical diagnosis of otitis media (ear infection). She has a sensation of fever with a temperature of 99.9 degrees F and has head sensitivity in the area above and around her ears when pressed. She remarks that her mouth \"tastes like aspirin\". Her mother reports that she is a very quiet girl who does not show her emotions and hardly ever gets sick even when the rest of the family is ill. You prescribe the formula Xiao Chai Hu Tang (Minor Bupleurum Decoction) for her for 5 days. She returns after 3 days and her mother reports that her fever is very slight now and the head sensitivity is less. The strange taste in her daughter's mouth has gone away. Her daughter sits in her chair with her head tucked between her legs and her eyes closed. Her mom reports that the daughter has been complaining that the world is spinning and she feels strange and has no balance and feels \"sick\" when her eyes are open. Her mother would like to finish the formula that she purchased from you 3 days ago. How would you modify the formula to treat these new symptoms?",
      "question_hant": "一名12歲女性因西醫診斷為中耳炎（耳部感染）前來就診。她自覺發熱，體溫為華氏99.9度，按壓耳朵上方及周圍區域時有壓痛感。她表示口中「有阿斯匹靈的味道」。她的母親表示，她是個非常安靜、不表露情緒的女孩，即使家中其他人生病時她也很少生病。您為她處方小柴胡湯，療程5日。她於3日後回診，母親表示她的發熱已非常輕微，頭部壓痛感也減輕。女兒口中的異味已經消失。她的女兒坐在椅子上，頭埋在雙腿之間，雙眼緊閉。母親表示女兒一直抱怨天旋地轉，感覺很奇怪且失去平衡，睜開眼睛時感到「不舒服」。母親希望能將3天前向您購買的藥方服用完畢。您會如何加減此方以治療這些新出現的症狀？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Add Qiang Huo (rhizoma seu radix notopterygii) and Chuan Xiong (rhizoma chuanxiong)",
          "hant": "加羌活與川芎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Add Ju Hua (flos chrysanthemi), Gou Teng (ramulus cum uncis uncariae), and Jue Ming Zi (semen cassiae)",
          "hant": "加菊花、鉤藤與決明子",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Remove Ren Shen (radix ginseng), and Da Zao (fructus jujubae), and add Wu Wei Zi (fructus schisandrae), and Gan Jiang (rhizoma zingiberis)",
          "hant": "去人參與大棗，加五味子與乾薑",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Remove Chai Hu (radix bupleurum)",
          "hant": "去柴胡",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This young lady is suffering from vertigo as a complication from her original pattern of pathogen attacking the shaoyang. As wind-cold travels towards the interior, it converts to heat and cooling herbs are required to counter the symptomatic indicators. Ju hua, gou teng, and jue ming zi are all cooling herbs that expel wind and subdue rising liver yang (the main causes of the vertigo). These three herbs also are very much liver herbs which have the interior / exterior relationship with the shaoyang. Qiang huo and chuan xiong are warming herbs and expel wind but do not subdue the liver yang. Removing chai hu from the original formula would remove an ascending cooling herb (which is uncommon in cooling herbs) which is the most important herb for treating shaoyang stage disorders. Removing ren shen and da zao while adding wu wei zi and gan jiang is a classical modification for the presence of coughing. This is not present in the case as reported. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 104-109.",
      "exp_hant": "此少女的眩暈是原本邪犯少陽證的併發症。隨著風寒邪氣傳裡化熱，需使用寒涼藥物以對抗其症狀表現。菊花、鉤藤與決明子皆為性涼之藥，能袪風並平抑肝陽上亢（此為眩暈的主要成因）。此三藥亦皆屬肝經用藥，與少陽有表裡關係。羌活與川芎性溫，雖能袪風，但不能平抑肝陽。若從原方中去除柴胡，將失去一味升散性涼（此為寒涼藥中少見的特性）且為治療少陽證最重要的藥物。去人參與大棗，加五味子與乾薑，是針對咳嗽症狀的經典加減法，然此病例並無咳嗽之表現。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 104-109."
