      "exp_en": "The bleeding is due to scratching which results due to heat in the blood. Damp-heat that is trapped between the flesh and the interstices and pores combining with the blood heat leads to fire-toxins in the body. This is addressed in the original prescription through herbs like sheng di huang, shi gao, zhi mu, cang zhu, and ku shen. The herbs yi yi ren, bai xian pi, and di fu zi are for instances when there is severe dampness presenting with the base pattern symptom complex. To remove the herbs cang zhu and ku shen would take away the formulas ability to effectively treat the damp-heat leading to the fire toxin in the body. Likewise, removing shi gao and adding rou gui will add heat to the body which is not therapeutic in this situation. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 636-638.",
      "exp_hant": "此出血乃因搔抓引起，其根本原因為血中有熱。濕熱鬱於肌肉腠理之間，與血熱相合而生火毒。原方中之生地黃、石膏、知母、蒼朮、苦參等藥即針對此病機而設。薏苡仁、白蘚皮、地膚子則用於基礎證型兼見濕邪較重之情況。若去蒼朮、苦參，將削弱本方清化濕熱、進而消解火毒之效。同樣地，去石膏而加肉桂則會助長體內熱邪，於此情況並不適宜。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 636-638."
