    {
      "number": 315,
      "question_en": "A 50-year-old female goes to see an herbalist for a headache, irritability, and slight cough and is prescribed Tian Ma Gou Teng Yin (Gastrodia and Uncaria Decoction). This treatment has had little effect on her symptoms. She arrives at your office looking for another opinion on treatment for her condition. Currently, she complains of an increased coughing with white sputum for a week. It is in later autumn. She claims to have \"caught a cold\" and has the main symptoms of cough and headache. She took some antitussive after receiving no help from her former formula but did not get much help from that. Now she has coughing especially in the evening. She spits some white and thin foamy sputum. She also has a runny nose, chills, dry throat, a thin white tongue coating and a floating wiry pulse. Which prescription would you prescribe for this patient at this time?",
