    {
      "number": 340,
      "question_en": "Which herb may potentiate anticoagulant and antiplatelet effects of western drugs?",
      "question_hant": "何藥可能增強西藥抗凝血劑及抗血小板藥物之作用？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "gan cao (glycyrrhizae radix)",
          "hant": "甘草",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "yuan zhi (polygaleas radix)",
          "hant": "遠志",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "ban lan gen (isatidis radix)",
          "hant": "板藍根",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "wu wei zi (schisandrae fructus)",
          "hant": "五味子",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Use with caution when taken with anticoagulants such as heparin, warfarin (Coumadin) and enoxaparin (Lovenox) or antiplatelet such as aspirin, dipyridamole (Persantine) and clopidogrel (Plavix). Chen and Chen list ban lan gen as an antiplatelet but not as an anticoagulant but Flaws lists it as both. The herb ban lan gen drains Heat, relieves Fire toxicity, cools the Blood and benefits the throat. Other herbs that can potentiate anticoagulant and antiplatelets include chi shao, bai shao, tao ren, chuan xiong, pu huang, ding xiang, du huo, e zhu, and ge gen. Antiplatelets are drugs which interfere with platelet formation. These drugs may be used as prophylaxis for clot formation, to treat acute thrombotic events and as anti-inflammatory drugs. Anticoagulants drugs interfere with the coagulation process. Heparin and warfarin are the two most well-known anticoagulants. These drugs may be used as prophylaxis to prevent deep vein thrombosis, embolism, and also to treat thromboembolism, myocardial infarctions, and peripheral vascular diseases. Antiplatelet drugs block platelet plug formation while anticoagulants interfere with the extrinsic and intrinsic pathways. Antiplatelets usually can cause gastrointestinal bleeding due to increased acid secretion while anticoagulants may cause bleeding due to thrombocytopenia. Antiplatelets may be given while pregnant while warfarin is contraindicated in pregnancy. Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, pages 146-148",
      "exp_hant": "若患者同時服用抗凝血劑，如肝素、華法林（Coumadin）及依諾肝素（Lovenox），或抗血小板藥物，如阿斯匹靈、雙嘧達莫（Persantine）及氯吡格雷（Plavix），應謹慎使用。Chen與Chen將板藍根列為抗血小板藥物而非抗凝血劑，但Flaws則將其列為兼具兩種作用之藥物。板藍根能瀉熱、解火毒、涼血、利咽。其他可能增強抗凝血及抗血小板作用之藥物包括赤芍、白芍、桃仁、川芎、蒲黃、丁香、獨活、莪朮與葛根。抗血小板藥物為干擾血小板形成之藥物，可作為預防血栓形成、治療急性血栓事件及作為抗發炎藥物使用。抗凝血劑則干擾凝血過程，肝素與華法林為兩種最著名之抗凝血劑，可作為預防深靜脈血栓、栓塞之用，亦可治療血栓栓塞、心肌梗塞及周邊血管疾病。抗血小板藥物阻斷血小板栓子形成，而抗凝血劑則干擾外源性與內源性凝血途徑。抗血小板藥物常因增加胃酸分泌而導致胃腸道出血，抗凝血劑則可能因血小板減少而導致出血。抗血小板藥物在懷孕期間可酌情使用，而華法林則為妊娠禁忌。Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, pages 146-148"
    },
