      ],
      "exp_en": "This patient is having PMS due to liver qi stagnation. As the blood builds and fills, there is a point at which the blood is full and continues building without discharging. This causes the liver qi stagnation causing breast tenderness and irritability. Her pulse is also thin. Xiao Yao San is the prescription for her condition. Her new condition shows a more severe breast tenderness that reaches down into the hypochondriac area (rib-side). For this complication, removing bai zhu and adding xiang fu is the correct modification. Bai zhu is a spleen tonic and its use can result in qi stagnation. Xiang fu moves the liver qi and alleviates pain. Adding mu dan pi, yu jin, and san leng is a modification of this formula where there is intense, fixed pain due to blood stasis. The pain, though severe, has not been reported as being fixed and stabbing pain that is indicative of blood stasis. Adding bo he, xiang fu, and dan shen (also wei jiang, fo shou, and dang shen) is a modification of this formula for pain over the liver with fatigue and reduced appetite. This symptom complex has not been reported by the patient. Removing chai hu is not recommended as it is one of the primary herbs that move the liver qi and resolve constraint. Increasing bai zhu is also not recommended as this is a possible cause of further stagnation. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 120-124",
      "exp_hant": "此病人的經前症候群乃因肝氣鬱結所致。隨著血分逐漸充盈,達到滿溢卻未能適時疏泄之時,便會導致肝氣鬱結,出現乳房脹痛及易怒,其脈亦見細象。逍遙散正適用於此證。她此次病情顯示乳房脹痛加重並延伸至脅肋部位(肋側)。針對此併發變化,去白朮、加香附為正確的加減方式。白朮為補脾之藥,使用後可能導致氣滯加重。香附能疏肝行氣、止痛。加牡丹皮、鬱金、三稜的加減法適用於因血瘀所致的劇烈固定疼痛。此病人雖疼痛加劇,但並未報告有血瘀特徵的固定刺痛。加薄荷、香附、丹參(另有煨薑、佛手、黨參)的加減法則適用於肝區疼痛兼疲倦、食欲減退者,此病人並未出現此類症狀組合。去柴胡並不建議,因柴胡為疏肝解鬱的主要藥物之一。加重白朮用量亦不建議,因其可能是造成氣滯加重的原因之一。《方劑學》第二版,Bensky著,第120-124頁"
    },
