      "exp_en": "This patient has been receiving a very bitter and cold formula to treat the complications from the STD infection (fire and/or damp-heat in the liver and gallbladder). Due to this, the spleen has become damaged to the extent which it has lost its ability to raise the clear leading to the symptoms of unclear vision, dizziness, unsteady movement, and loose stools. The pulse, along with these symptoms leads to the pattern of spleen qi deficiency with the inability to raise the clear yang and the formula bu zhong yi qi tang. Tian ma gou teng yin treats dizziness, vertigo, hypertension, and other conditions related to liver yang rising and heat. This is not appropriate for this patient at this time. Shen ling bai zhu san treats spleen qi deficiency and would be particularly good to treat the loose stools but does not aid the spleen in raising the clear yang. Bu zhong yi qi tang utilizes chai hu, sheng ma , and huang qi for this purpose. Shen ling bai zhu san does not include any of these herbs. Dang gui bu xue tang treats blood deficiency with heat rising into the muscle layers. This is not the current pattern for this patient. Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 199-200, 317-322, 647-649, 314-316, 338-341",
      "exp_hant": "此病人一直服用極為苦寒的方劑,以治療性病感染所引起的併發症(肝膽火熱及/或濕熱)。因此,脾臟受損,失去升清的能力,導致視物不清、頭暈、行動不穩及大便溏瀉等症狀。結合脈象與這些症狀,可判斷此為脾氣虛、清陽不升之證,應選用補中益氣湯。天麻鉤藤飲治療頭暈、眩暈、高血壓及其他因肝陽上亢、肝熱所致的病症,目前並不適用於此病人。參苓白朮散治療脾氣虛,對緩解大便溏瀉特別有效,但無法幫助脾臟升發清陽。補中益氣湯運用柴胡、升麻、黃耆以達此目的,而參苓白朮散並不含這些藥物。當歸補血湯治療血虛兼熱邪上乘肌肉層,並非此病人目前的證型。《方劑學》第二版,Bensky著,2009年,第199-200、317-322、647-649、314-316、338-341頁"
