      ],
      "exp_en": "In the case of severe edema, pathological fluids have accumulated and threaten the interior of the body. The strategy is to increase the spleen and kidney functions of water metabolism while clearing the interior of pathological fluids. In the case of damp-heat diarrhea, warming herbs like bai zhu and gui zhi are removed and replaced with yin chen hao and jin yin hua. Yin chen hao is bitter to dry the dampness and only slightly cold which keeps it from being too damaging. Likewise, Jin yin hua is cold but also sweet (tonifying) which tempers its potential damaging effects. It clears damp-heat from the lower burner. Combining Yin chen hao and da huang makes the combination extremely bitter and da huang's cold would be more assaulting to the digestion since it is not tonifying. To remove fu ling and add yi yi ren does not change the function of the formula much. These herbs are similar with yi yi ren used more for bi syndromes than fu ling. Lian qiao is somewhat similar to jin yin hua and forms a dui yao pair to treat wei level wind-heat but is bitter and slightly acrid and therefore more potentially damaging in this situation. Mu dan pi is a bitter and acrid herb which clears heat but does not resolve dampness. Sheng di huang also cools the blood and nourishes yin but its cloying nature could arguably make the effects from dampness worse. Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pgs 312, 148, 235, 267, 275, 152, 126, 120; Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pgs 724-728",
      "exp_hant": "在嚴重水腫的情況下,病理性水液已經蓄積並威脅體內臟腑。此時的治療策略是加強脾腎的水液代謝功能,同時清除體內的病理性水液。若為濕熱腹瀉,則應去除溫燥藥物如白朮、桂枝,改以茵陳蒿與金銀花取代。茵陳蒿味苦以燥濕,性僅微寒,不致過於損傷正氣。同樣地,金銀花性寒但兼甘味(具滋養性),可緩和其潛在的損傷作用,並能清下焦濕熱。若將茵陳蒿與大黃合用,則組合過於苦寒,大黃之寒性因不具滋養作用,對脾胃的損傷會更大。去茯苓、加薏苡仁對方劑功效影響不大,兩藥性質相近,只是薏苡仁更常用於痹證,而茯苓則否。連翹與金銀花性質相近,兩者組成對藥治療衛分風熱,但其性偏苦、略帶辛散,在此情況下反而更易造成損傷。牡丹皮為苦辛之藥,能清熱但不能化濕。生地黃亦能涼血滋陰,但其滋膩之性可能反使濕邪加重。《中藥學》,Bensky著,2004年,第312、148、235、267、275、152、126、120頁;《方劑學》第二版,Bensky著,2009年,第724-728頁"
