      ],
      "exp_en": "This formula treats a mutually enforcing qi stagnation and phlegm pattern that can involve either or both of substantial and insubstantial phlegm. Sha ren is added to this formula due to its ability to move the qi, and transform damp. It also improves the spleen transformation and transportation which aids in the reestablishment of the proper middle jiao qi dynamic. Its aromatic quality both awakens the spleen and bursts through turbidity to remove obstruction causing distention. Mu xiang is a good herb to move qi in the middle jiao. It adjusts stagnation in the intestines and strengthens the spleen to aid it in removing obstruction. Its acrid and bitter properties help to disperse and drain down obstruction in the middle jiao causing distention. Together, these two herbs specifically target the middle and facilitate the free flow of qi by removing obstruction. Bai dou kou is similar to sha ren in function but it is not as strong. Hou po is already in the formula and yu jin is a blood invigorator which also clears heat in the blood. Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pg 530, 479, 610; Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pg 516-519",
      "exp_hant": "此方治療氣滯與痰互結之證,可涉及有形或無形之痰,或二者兼有。加入砂仁乃因其能行氣化濕,並能增強脾之運化功能,有助恢復中焦正常的氣機運行。其芳香之性既能醒脾,又能突破濁邪以消除阻滯所致的脹滿。木香為調理中焦氣機的良藥,能調理腸道氣滯,並健脾以助其消除阻滯。其辛苦之性有助疏散並瀉下中焦阻滯所致的脹滿。此二藥合用,專門作用於中焦,藉由消除阻滯而使氣機暢通。白豆蔻功效與砂仁相似,但力量較弱。厚朴已在方中,而鬱金為活血藥,兼能清血分之熱。《中藥學》,Bensky著,2004年,第530、479、610頁;《方劑學》第二版,Bensky著,2009年,第516-519頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 375,
      "question_en": "A 45 year old high school math instructor states he is suffering from hypoglycemia, He states that the diagnosis was made by a Naturopath, and he carries with him a sixty-page computer printout given to him by that practitioner which he says justifies his claim. He has also seen a nutritionist who told him he has had candida albicans due to the symptoms of recurrent burning stomach and high fever with oral thrush (he also exhibited hyperhidrosis). He has a disheveled appearance and finds it difficult to answer the questions without referring to the computer printout. His main complaint is fatigue, restlessness, memory loss and poor concentration. He also has periodic cravings for sugar and extreme mood swings throughout the day although he rarely eats because he cannot stomach the thought of actually eating without feeling nauseated and vomiting up the food. On the occasion when he does eat, he will have abdominal cramping followed by diarrhea. These symptoms make it difficult for him to do math and he has kept his current job only because his students are all too happy to have a math instructor who cannot do math. He has a pale yellowish complexion and his speech is rapid but scattered. His tongue is pale and thin with a thin, moist white coat and his pulse is fine and moderate. What does the former presence of the symptoms listed for candida and the current symptoms reflect as it relates to the six channels?",
      "question_hant": "一位45歲的高中數學教師表示自己患有低血糖症,他表示此診斷是由一位自然療法師所做,並隨身攜帶一份長達六十頁的電腦列印報告,他表示這份報告可以佐證他的說法。他也曾看過一位營養師,對方告訴他,根據他反覆出現的胃部灼熱、高熱伴口腔鵝口瘡等症狀(他還表現出多汗症),診斷他患有白色念珠菌感染。他外表邋遢,若不參照那份電腦列印報告便難以回答問題。他的主要主訴是疲勞、躁動不安、記憶力減退及注意力不集中。他也會週期性地渴望攝取糖分,並在一天之中出現劇烈的情緒波動,儘管他很少進食,因為他無法忍受進食的念頭,一想到就會感到噁心並嘔吐。在少數進食的場合,他會出現腹部絞痛,隨後腹瀉。這些症狀使他難以進行數學運算,他之所以能保住目前的工作,只因為學生們都很樂於擁有一位不會算數學的數學老師。他的面色呈淡黃色,說話速度快但語意散亂。舌淡而薄,苔薄白而濕,脈細緩。就六經而言,先前所描述的念珠菌症狀與目前的症狀反映出何種關係?",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "The Yin levels are easier to resolve than the Yang levels",
          "hant": "陰經階段比陽經階段更容易痊癒",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Yang Ming level always moves into the Tai Yin level when left untreated",
          "hant": "陽明階段若不治療,必然轉入太陰階段",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "The Yang levels take longer to resolve than the Yin levels",
          "hant": "陽經階段比陰經階段需要更長時間才能痊癒",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "A mutually convertible relationship between Yang Ming and Tai Yin levels",
          "hant": "陽明與太陰階段之間存在相互轉化的關係",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The Tai Yin level reflects pathology to the earth element it governs and in turn is damaged by dampness. Along with the Yang Ming level, these two levels manifest in digestive disorders as spleen/stomach pathologies govern. Whereas the yang ming level is an interior heat excess pattern, the tai yin level is an interior deficiency cold pattern for the most part. These have an almost opposite nature from each other and it is therefore said \"[if the condition is one of] repletion, it is yang brightness, [if one of] vacuity, it is greater yin.\" In this case, as the candida symptomology includes the high fever and big sweating with the digestive symptom of burning stomach, this places the level at yang ming. Over time as the middle jiao falls to deficiency, the level moves naturally from yang ming to tai yin. Although this is a natural progression, yang ming can transmute in many ways if left untreated depending on several factors including the patient's constitution. Due to the deficiency nature of the yin levels, it can be strongly argued that the yin levels are more difficult to treat than the yang levels where the right qi is still intact and able to fight against the pathogen to a greater extent. Likewise, often the yin levels where resolving the pathogen and tonifying the deficiency (dual strategy) is employed to treat a patient can take longer to resolve than the excess yang levels where expelling and resolving the pathogen is the main and sometimes sole focus. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs 451-452.",
      "exp_hant": "太陰階段反映其所主管的土行受損,其病變乃因濕邪所傷。連同陽明階段,此二階段皆表現為脾胃病變所主導的消化系統疾病。陽明階段大致為裡熱實證,而太陰階段則多屬裡虛寒證。此二者性質幾乎完全相反,因此有云:『[若病證屬]實者,為陽明;[若屬]虛者,為太陰。』本案中,由於念珠菌症狀包括高熱大汗與胃部灼熱之消化道症狀,故將此階段定為陽明。隨著時間推移,中焦轉為虛損,病位便自然由陽明轉入太陰。雖然這是一種自然的病程演變,但若不加以治療,陽明證依患者體質等多項因素的不同,可能有多種轉歸方式。由於陰經階段具有虛損的本質,可以有力地論證陰經階段較陽經階段更難治療,因為在陽經階段,正氣尚存,能較大程度地與病邪抗爭。同樣地,在陰經階段常須採用祛邪與扶正並行的雙重策略,治療所需時間往往長於單純以祛邪、解表為主要甚至唯一重點的陽經實證階段。《傷寒論》,Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel著,1999年,第451-452頁"
    },
