      "exp_en": "Though kidney yang deficiency is a common pattern for impotence, it takes sufficient yin and yang to solve the impotence riddle. Ba ji tian is a yang tonic but it is not overly drying of the yin and fluids. It also augments the essence which is an important factor in sexual function. Rou cong rong is a yang tonic which also nourishes both the blood and essence. The heat from the yang tonifying is offset with the tonifcation of the blood. Gou qi zi is a yin and blood tonic that mildly tonifies the yang. This helps to balance the actions of the other two yang tonics. Ren shen, on the other hand, by stoking the gate of vitality aids the fire and is thusly contraindicated for issues where yin deficiency is an issue despite its ability to nourish fluids and yin. Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pg 778, 773, 759, 710; Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pg 395-400",
      "exp_hant": "雖然腎陽虛是陽痿的常見證型,但要真正解決陽痿問題,須陰陽兼顧、皆須充足。巴戟天為補陽藥,但不會過度耗傷陰液,亦能益精,而精對於性功能是重要因素。肉蓯蓉為補陽藥,兼能養血益精。其溫補所生之熱可藉由養血而得以緩解。枸杞子為滋陰養血之藥,兼能溫和補陽,有助於平衡另外兩味補陽藥的作用。人參則不同,因其能助命門之火,故在陰虛為患的情況下屬禁忌,儘管它具有滋養津液與陰液的能力。《中藥學》,Bensky著,2004年,第778、773、759、710頁;《方劑學》第二版,Bensky著,2009年,第395-400頁"
