      "exp_en": "This formula derives from qu mai san and treats urinary dribbling disorders. Specifically, it treats hot, bloody, and painful urinary dribbling. In modern times, this formula, and many formulas developed based on this formula treat urinary tract infections. When there is cloudy and painful urination, two of the herbs from the formula to treat cloudy lin (Bi xie feng qin yin) are used. Bei xie is the major herb in the pharmacopeia to treat cloudy urination. It has the ability to separate the clear from the turbid. Shi chang pu is added for its ability to transform and expel turbid dampness. It also aids in the removal of obstruction and moves the qi. Mu tong is a good choice for the treatment of hot lin but not a major herb for cloudy lin syndrome. Hu po is a good herb to treat bloody lin syndrome. Bian xu can drain dampness but lacks the ability to transform turbid dampness. Fu ling is also a sweet and bland diuretic but does not transform turbidity like shi chang pu. Hua shi is in the formula to clear heat and unblock the dribbling. It would be a good choice for hot lin but not a premiere herb for cloudy lin. Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pgs 301, 954, 283, 921, 267; Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pgs 713-715",
      "exp_hant": "此方源自瞿麥散,治療小便淋瀝澀痛之證,特別是治療熱淋、血淋及石淋。現代此方及許多以此為基礎發展出的方劑皆用於治療泌尿道感染。當出現小便渾濁澀痛時,應加入萆薢分清飲中的兩味藥物,用以治療膏淋。萆薢是藥典中治療小便渾濁的主要藥物,能分清別濁。加入石菖蒲是因其能化濁祛濕,亦助於消除阻滯並行氣。木通是治療熱淋的良藥,但並非治療膏淋的主要藥物。琥珀是治療血淋的良藥。萹蓄能利濕,但缺乏化濁的能力。茯苓亦為甘淡利水藥,但不像石菖蒲能化濁。滑石在方中能清熱、通淋,對熱淋是良好選擇,但並非治療膏淋的首選藥物。《中藥學》,Bensky著,2004年,第301、954、283、921、267頁;《方劑學》第二版,Bensky著,2009年,第713-715頁"
