      ],
      "exp_en": "This formula was intended to treat women's emotional disorders but has been assigned to the disorder of zang zao (visceral agitation). This formula focuses on tonifying the ying qi while restraining the heart from the dispersal of its spiritual aspects. Ultimately, this manifests as an emotional condition characterized by worry, anxiety, or pensiveness. Sinus arrhythmias are variations in the heart rate related to vagal impulses to the sinoatrial node. They can be common and a benign condition. A choppy pulse is a sign of blood stasis or blood deficiency. This condition is caused by blood deficiency. The strategy is to tonify the spleen and lungs and nourish the blood. Dang shen is sweet and neutral to tonify both the spleen and lungs. These are two of the organs that are central in the blood creation mechanism. Hu po calms the spirit but neither tonifies qi nor blood. Long gu and mu li are a dui yao pair adept at anchoring the shen but do not tonify qi or blood. Di gu pi (cortex lycii radicis) eliminates deficiency heat from the blood. Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pgs 714, 748, 919, 1043, 921, 907, 911,752; Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pgs 471-474",
      "exp_hant": "此方原意在治療婦女的情志疾病,後被歸類為治療臟躁之證。此方著重於補益營氣,同時斂心以防其神志耗散。此證最終表現為以憂慮、焦慮或多思善慮為特徵的情志病證。竇性心律不整是與迷走神經衝動至竇房結有關的心率變化,通常屬常見且良性的病症。澀脈是血瘀或血虛的徵象。本病是由血虛引起。治療策略為補益脾肺、養血。黨參性味甘平,能補脾益肺,而脾肺正是生血機制中的兩個核心臟腑。琥珀能安神,但既不補氣也不補血。龍骨與牡蠣為擅長潛鎮心神的對藥,但無法補氣血。地骨皮則清血分虛熱。《中藥學》,Bensky著,2004年,第714、748、919、1043、921、907、911、752頁;《方劑學》第二版,Bensky著,2009年,第471-474頁"
