      "exp_en": "It is 15 to 30g for the fresh herb and 6 to 15g for the dried herb. The herb should be wrapped in cheese cloth prior to decoction to prevent the hair like parts from irritating the throat. When fried with honey it increases moistening action and becomes better for wheezing due to dry heat. The raw form treats nausea and vomiting while the honey-fried form dissolves phlegm and relieves cough. The herb dissolves phlegm, stops cough, harmonizes the stomach, and directs qi down. It is bitter and cool. It enters the lung and stomach. The herb is not suitable for cough due to cold or for nausea or vomiting due to a cold stomach. Chinese Medical Herbology,Chen and Chen, 2004, page 735",
      "exp_hant": "鮮品劑量為15至30克，乾品則為6至15克。煎煮前應以紗布包裹，以防其毛狀物刺激咽喉。蜜炙後可增強潤燥之效，更適用於燥熱所致之喘證。生品治噁心嘔吐，蜜炙品則化痰止咳。此藥能化痰止咳、和胃降氣，性苦涼，入肺、胃二經。寒咳或胃寒嘔吐者不宜使用。《中醫藥學》，Chen and Chen著，2004年，第735頁"
    },
