          "key": "B",
          "en": "yue ju wan (escape restraint pill)",
          "hant": "越鞠丸",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "wen jing tang (warm the menses decoction)",
          "hant": "溫經湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Xiao Yao San (Rambling Powder)",
          "hant": "逍遙散",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This condition is a combined pattern of blood stasis and qi stagnation. Although there are clear stasis signs in the purple blood color and clots, the tongue and pulse are more indicative of qi stagnation. Yue ju wan is the best choice for this condition as the xiang fu and chuan xiong treat the qi stagnation and blood stasis respectively. The pattern for this formula is liver qi stagnation but it addresses the five stagnations including blood stasis and this formula therefore most completely addresses this patient's condition. Gui zhi fu ling wan seems like a likely choice because of its ability to move the blood in the uterus and ability to break up masses and clots. This formula does not address the liver qi stagnation symptoms and therefore does not address the condition completely. Xiao yao san treats liver qi stagnation and tonifies the blood but does not move the blood to treat blood stasis. Again, this formula treats this condition but does not address both of the major patterns. Wen jing tang treats deficiency and cold in the chong and ren vessels causing blood stasis. With a rapid pulse and red tongue, this is not an appropriate choice for this case. Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs.583, 507, 120, 577",
      "exp_hant": "此證為血瘀與氣滯並見之複合證型。雖然經血色紫夾塊為明顯之血瘀徵象，然舌脈表現則更偏向氣滯。越鞠丸為此證之最佳選擇，方中香附、川芎分別治氣滯與血瘀。本方證型雖為肝氣鬱結，然其能兼治五鬱（含血鬱），故最能全面對治此患者之病證。桂枝茯苓丸看似合適之選擇，因其能活血化瘀、消癥散結，然此方未能處理肝氣鬱結之症狀，故無法全面對治此病證。逍遙散能疏肝解鬱、養血，然不能活血以治血瘀，同樣僅能治部分病證而非兩大主要病機。溫經湯治沖任虛寒所致之血瘀，然此患者脈數舌紅，並不適合使用此方。Bensky, Dan等著，《方劑學》，第583、507、120、577頁"
    },
