      "exp_en": "COMMON: Both herbs warm the Spleen and Kidney yang to treat diarrhea. DIFFERENCES: The herb Bu Gu Zhi is a stronger Kidney yang tonic and warms the yang. It is bitter, acrid, and very warm. It enters the Kidney and Spleen channels. The herb Yi Zhi Ren is stronger at warming the Spleen and retaining body fluids. It is acrid and warm. It enters the Kidney and Spleen channels. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: The herb Bu Gu Zhi is contraindicated with yin xu heat, constipation, nocturnal emissions, hematuria, cystitis, UTIs, red eyes, bitter mouth taste, or for long-term use. The herb Yi Zhi Ren is contraindicated with yin xu heat, vomiting due to qi stasis or heat, urinary incontinence due to heat, or diarrhea from qi xu or heat. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 974, 909, 912",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：兩藥皆能溫脾腎之陽以治瀉泄。差異：補骨脂補腎陽之力較強，能溫陽。其性苦、辛、大溫，入腎、脾二經。益智仁溫脾、固澀津液之力較強，其性辛溫，入腎、脾二經。禁忌／慎用：補骨脂於陰虛有熱、便秘、遺精、血尿、膀胱炎、尿路感染、目赤、口苦或需長期使用者禁用。益智仁於陰虛有熱、氣滯或熱所致之嘔吐、熱所致之小便失禁，或氣虛或熱所致之瀉泄者禁用。《中醫藥學》，Chen and Chen著，2004年，第974、909、912頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 445,
      "question_en": "Which herb clears Lung heat, stops coughing, and stops bleeding?",
      "question_hant": "何藥能清肺熱、止咳並止血？",
