      ],
      "exp_en": "COMMON: All four herbs disperse wind-heat, clear heat in the Liver, and brighten the eyes. DIFFERENCES: The herb Sang Ye clears Lung heat, stops coughing, and stops bleeding. It is bitter, sweet, and cold. It enters the Lung and Liver channels. The herb Ju Hua is stronger at clearing heat in the Liver and clears toxins. It calms Liver yang. It is acrid, sweet, bitter, and cool. It enters the Lung and Liver channels. The herb Man Jing Zi relieves headaches, dispels wind and relieves pain. It is acrid, bitter, and cool. It enters the Liver, Stomach, and Bladder channels. The herb Mu Zei stops bleeding. It is sweet, bitter, and cold. It enters the Lung, Liver, and Gallbladder channels. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: The herb Sang Ye is cold and should be used with caution with constitutional deficiency or cold. The herb Ju Hua should be cautiously used in patients with qi xu or cold in the Stomach (diarrhea, poor appetite). It is contraindicated in yang xu or deficiency and cold. The herb Man Jing Zi should be used cautiously for patients with Spleen/Stomach deficiency or yin empty heat or patients with blood xu headaches or dizziness. The herb Mu Zei should be used cautiously with deficiencies (qi, blood, yin or yang), during pregnancy. It should not be used with red eyes due to Liver yang. Avoid long term use. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 97, 74, 75, 77, 79",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：此四藥皆能疏散風熱、清肝熱、明目。差異：桑葉能清肺熱、止咳並止血，性苦甘寒，入肺、肝二經。菊花清肝熱、解毒之力較強，能平肝陽，性辛甘苦涼，入肺、肝二經。蔓荊子能止頭痛、袪風止痛，性辛苦涼，入肝、胃、膀胱三經。木賊能止血，性甘苦寒，入肺、肝、膽三經。禁忌／慎用：桑葉性寒，體質虛寒者慎用。菊花於氣虛或胃寒（腹瀉、食慾不振）者慎用，陽虛或虛寒者禁用。蔓荊子於脾胃虛弱、陰虛內熱，或血虛頭痛頭暈者慎用。木賊於氣血陰陽虛損者、孕婦慎用，肝陽所致之目赤者不宜使用，並應避免長期使用。《中醫藥學》，Chen and Chen著，2004年，第97、74、75、77、79頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 446,
      "question_en": "A 23 year-old male presents to your office 2 days ago with tremendous stabbing pain after being kicked in the groin by his girlfriend. He revealed that the kick was not the most painful strike but a subsequent punch to his lower abdominal area. His lower abdominal area is bruised and extremely painful to the touch. He reports difficulty urinating due to the pain. His pulse is rough and wiry and his tongue is dark. You prescribe the formula Shi Xiao San (Sudden Smile Powder) and he reports that it immediately diminished the stabbing pain and now he feels more of a dull pressure aching in his lower abdomen and groin. How would you modify his formula in light of his new presentation?",
      "question_hant": "一名23歲男性於2天前因遭女友踢中鼠蹊部而出現劇烈刺痛前來就診。他表示踢擊本身並非最痛之處，反而是隨後被拳擊小腹部位更為疼痛。其小腹部有瘀青，觸痛劇烈，並因疼痛而排尿困難。脈澀弦，舌質暗。醫者予以失笑散治療，患者表示服藥後刺痛立即緩解，現改為小腹及鼠蹊部悶脹隱痛。針對此新的病情表現，應如何調整處方？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Add Xiang Fu (Rhizoma Cyperi)",
          "hant": "加香附",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Add San Qi (radix notoginseng)",
          "hant": "加三七",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Add Pao Jiang (rhizome zingiberis preparatum) and Ai Ye (folium artemisiae argyi)",
          "hant": "加炮薑與艾葉",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Remove Wu Ling Zhi (faeces trogopterori) and add Wu Zhu Yu (fructus evodiae)and Ze Xie (rhizome alismatis)",
          "hant": "去五靈脂，加吳茱萸與澤瀉",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "After treating this young male with the blood invigorating and pain relieving formula Shi Xiao San, he is left with pain more indicative of qi stagnation than blood stasis. For this, the herb xiang fu is added. This herb has a strong affinity for the liver system which runs through the lower abdomen and groin and is a qi regulator and pain relieving herb. Adding san qi to the formula will help with the blood stasis but not treat pain due to qi stagnation. Removing wu ling zhi, which is in the formula to direct the formula to the liver system and clear the blood vessels, invigorate the blood and alleviate pain, will not help the formula with qi stagnation and reduce the formula's pain relieving effects. Additionally adding wu zhu yu, although clearing of stagnation of the liver system, is a very warming herb where there should be clear cold signs for its use. Ze xie would cool some of the heat from wu zhu yu but acts primarily to remove dampness obstruction to promote urination. This is not needed in this case. Adding pao jiang and ai ye to this formula is for cases where there are signs of concurrent coldness. There is not sufficient evidence of this and more likely there would be heat presenting in this patient's condition. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 591-592.",
      "exp_hant": "以活血止痛之失笑散治療此青年後，其疼痛表現已更偏向氣滯而非血瘀，故加入香附。此藥與循行於小腹及鼠蹊部之肝經關係密切，能理氣止痛。加入三七雖有助於血瘀，卻不能治氣滯所致之疼痛。去除五靈脂——此藥於方中原用以引藥入肝經、清利血脈、活血止痛——並無助於治療氣滯，反而會削弱本方之止痛效果。此外，加入吳茱萸雖能疏解肝經之鬱滯，然其為溫熱之藥，須有明顯寒象方可使用。澤瀉雖能稍緩吳茱萸之熱性，但其主要功效在於袪濕利尿，此證並不需要。加入炮薑與艾葉則適用於兼有寒象之情況，此患者並無充分證據顯示有寒象，反而更可能表現為熱證。《方劑學》第二版，第591-592頁"
    },
