      "exp_en": "ENERGETICS: sweet, sour, cool. ORGANS: Stomach, Spleen, Lung. ACTIONS: Clears heat, relieves agitation, relieves summer heat, generates body fluids, moistens the lungs, treats morning sickness, treats low blood sugar, relieves intoxication, stimulates the appetite, THERAPEUTICS: Treats hot symptoms (restlessness, thirst, hangover). CONTRAINDICATION: none. FOLK REMEDIES: For morning sickness, prepare 30-60g of fresh apple. Fry 30g rice until yellow. Mix together with apple peel and make tea. For low blood sugar, eat two peeled apples. For cough due to hot lungs and dry mouth, peel apples, remove seeds, crush and steam them with honey until soft like jelly. Take 2 teaspoons each time 3x per day. Tao of Nutrition, 3rd Edition, page 53; Chinese System of Food Cure, Lu, 1986, page 62",
