      "exp_en": "COMMON: All five herbs dissolve phlegm and arrest cough. DIFFERENCES: The herb Jie Geng ventilates the Lung, benefits the throat, and dispels pus. It is bitter, acrid, and neutral. It enters the Lung channel. The herb Xuan Fu Hua descends Lung and Stomach qi. It is bitter, acrid, salty, and slightly warm. It enters the Liver, Lung, Stomach, and Spleen channels. The herb Qian Hu disperses wind-heat. It is bitter, acrid, and cool. It enters the Lung channel. The herb Chuan Bei Mu arrests chronic cough and moistens the Lung. It is bitter, acrid, and cool. It enters the Heart and Lung channels. The herb Zhe Bei Mu clears heat, eliminates toxins, and disperses stagnation. It is bitter and cold. It enters the Heart and Lung channels. CAUTIONS/CONTRAS: The herb Jie Geng should be used with caution with chronic cough from yin xu or cough with blood streaked sputum. The herb Xuan Fu Hua should be used with caution with dry cough from yin xu or with loose stools due to Spleen xu. The herb Qian Hu does not have any listed. The herbs Chuan Bei Mu and Zhe Bei Mu are both contraindicated with phlegm due to cold and dampness. DRUG INTERACTIONS: The herb Xuan Fu Hua, though undocumented, may potentiate the effect of diuretics. The herb Qian Hu, though undocumented, should be used with caution with anticoagulant or antiplatelet drugs as it can increase the effect of the drugs. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 745, 696, 698, 699, 702, 703",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：此五藥皆能化痰止咳。差異：桔梗能宣肺、利咽、排膿，性苦辛平，入肺經。旋覆花能降肺胃之氣，性苦辛鹹微溫，入肝、肺、胃、脾四經。前胡能疏散風熱，性苦辛涼，入肺經。川貝母能止久咳並潤肺，性苦辛涼，入心、肺二經。浙貝母能清熱解毒、散結，性苦寒，入心、肺二經。禁忌／慎用：桔梗於陰虛久咳或痰中帶血者慎用。旋覆花於陰虛燥咳或脾虛便溏者慎用。前胡無特別禁忌記載。川貝母與浙貝母皆禁用於寒濕所致之痰證。藥物交互作用：旋覆花雖未有明確記載，然可能增強利尿劑之效果。前胡雖未有明確記載，然與抗凝血劑或抗血小板藥物合用時應謹慎，因其可能增強該類藥物之效果。《中醫藥學》，Chen and Chen著，2004年，第745、696、698、699、702、703頁"
