      ],
      "exp_en": "This patient's exterior condition has moved into the shao yang and lies between the shaoyang and tai yang stages as shown by the floating pulse and the continued fever and chills. Since the patient is reporting that the fever and chills are not occurring simultaneously but seem to be starting to alternate, with the reported symptoms, it is diagnosed that the pathogen is in the shao yang layer and xiao chai hu tang is the correct prescription. The pulse is not floating and rapid indicating wind-heat and therefore yin qiao san is not the correct formula for this condition. xiao cheng qi tang is for mild yang ming syndromes and this is not the appropriate presentation for this formula. Li zhong wan is for middle burner yang deficiency which would not show exterior symptoms and would exhibit symptoms such as diarrhea with watery stools. Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs. 104, 36, 66,257",
      "exp_hant": "此患者之表證已轉入少陽，介於少陽與太陽之間，此可由脈浮及持續之發熱惡寒得知。由於患者所述之發熱與惡寒並非同時出現，而似乎開始呈現寒熱往來之勢，加以其餘症狀，可診斷邪氣已入少陽，小柴胡湯為正確之處方。此脈非浮數，故非風熱之象，因此銀翹散並非此證之正確方劑。小承氣湯用於輕度陽明證，亦非此病情之適當表現。理中丸用於中焦陽虛，此證並無表證表現，而應以水瀉等症狀為主。Bensky, Dan等著，《方劑學》，第104、36、66、257頁"
