    {
      "number": 457,
      "question_en": "A patient is prescribed a combination of Bai Hu Tang (White Tiger Decoction) and Long Dan Xie Gan Tang (Gentiana Decoction to Drain the Liver) for a symptom complex that includes digestive upset, burning stomach, and urinary tract infection. The pulse was slippery, fast, and surging in the guan position, and slightly deficient in the chi position. After two weeks, the patient has stopped taking these formulas and you reassess the patient's condition. She reports the possibility that she is pregnant and has vomiting from morning sickness with a bad reaction to any intake of food, fullness in the epigastrium, severe vertex headache, salivation bringing on nausea and cold limbs. The pulse is slow, deep, thin and weak. The tongue is pale with a wet, white fur. What formula would you prescribe for her at this time?",
      "question_hant": "某患者因症見消化不良、胃部灼熱及尿路感染，醫者處以白虎湯合龍膽瀉肝湯治療。其脈滑數，關部脈湧盛，尺部略顯不足。兩週後，患者自行停藥，醫者重新評估其病情。她表示可能已懷孕，出現孕吐嘔吐、進食後反應不佳、胃脘脹滿、劇烈之巔頂頭痛、流涎並引發噁心，以及四肢冰冷。脈遲、沉、細、弱，舌淡、苔白而濕。此時應為她處方何種方劑？",
