        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "da jian zhong tang (major construct the middle decoction)",
          "hant": "大建中湯",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In this case, with the underlying deficiency in the original presentation, the cold and bitter herbs in the original prescriptions damaged the liver, spleen, and kidneys leading to the current presentation. The strategy to employ is to warm the center and harmonize the liver. There is evidence that there is also kidney yang deficiency caused by too much cold in the former treatment but herbs like Zhi Fu Zi should be avoided due to the potential toxicities with her report of possibly being pregnant. Zhen Wu Tang tonifies the ming men fire and shores up overflowing water due to kidney weakness, but this is not the appropriate presentation and is led by aconite. Si Ni Tang likewise warms the kidney yang and features aconite as its lead herb. One has to consider that if the patient is possibly pregnant, it is not only the heat of fu zi that must be avoided but also the fact that the main action of fu zi is that of mobilizing. The great movement factor of aconite is to be absolutely avoided in a condition like pregnancy. Da Jian Zhong Tang does not have the correct presentation where there would be more pronounced abdominal pain. This formula also would not sufficiently address the liver component of the pattern. Wu Zhu Yu Tang both warms and tonifies the liver and stomach while countering the rising cold in the liver channel causing the vertex headache. Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs. 744, 261, 268, 274",
      "exp_hant": "本案中，因原本體質即有虛損，前方所用之寒涼苦寒藥物損傷肝、脾、腎，導致目前之表現。治療策略應為溫中和肝。雖有證據顯示先前治療過用寒涼已導致腎陽虛損，然因患者可能懷孕，應避免使用如製附子等具潛在毒性之藥物。真武湯能溫補命門之火並制水，然此並非此案之正確表現，且此方以附子為主藥。四逆湯同樣以附子為主藥以溫補腎陽。須考量若患者可能懷孕，不僅須避免附子之熱性，更須注意附子之主要作用在於推動氣血運行——此種強烈之推動作用於妊娠期間應絕對避免。大建中湯之表現並不相符，該證應有更明顯之腹痛，且此方亦不足以兼顧肝之病機。吳茱萸湯既能溫補肝胃，又能對治肝經寒氣上逆所致之巔頂頭痛。Bensky, Dan等著，《方劑學》，第744、261、268、274頁"
