      "exp_en": "COMMON: All five herbs dissolve food and strengthen the Stomach. DIFFERENCES: The herb Shan Zha digests meat and disperses blood stagnation. In combination with other herbs, it can treat cardiovascular disorders. It is sweet, sour, and slightly warm. It enters the Liver, Spleen, and Stomach channels. The herb Shen Qu breaks down hard to digest foods and protects the Stomach. It is sweet, acrid, and warm. It enters the Spleen and Stomach channels. The herb Mai Ya digests starch and inhibits lactation. It is sweet and neutral. It enters the Liver, Spleen, and Stomach. The herb Lai Fu Zi digests starch and is best for weak patients. It is acrid, sweet, and neutral. It enters the Spleen, Stomach, and Lung channels. It relieves fullness and distention, descends Lung qi and dispels phlegm. The herb Gu ya reduces food Stagnation, promotes digestion, strengthens and descends Qi, opens the Stomach and harmonizes the center. It is sweet-neutral and enters the Spleen and Stomoach. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: The herb Shan Zha should be used with caution with Spleen and Stomach deficiency and with peptic ulcers (herb can stimulate gastric acid secretion). It should not be used long term. The herb Shen Qu should be used with caution during pregnancy. The herb Mai Ya should be used with caution in patients without food stagnation. Prolonged use may injure qi. It is contraindicated in large dosages in nursing mothers. The herb Lai Fu Zi is contraindicated with qi and blood xu or in patients without food stagnation. Prolonged use or large doses can consume the qi. DRUG INTERACTIONS: The herb Shan Zha interacts with digoxin (Lanoxin) to have a cardiotonic effect. Its use should be monitored to avoid side effects. The herb Mai Ya interacts with antidiabetic drugs as it can lower blood sugar levels. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 535, 523, 526, 529, 531",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：此五藥皆能消食並健脾胃。差異：山楂能消肉食、散血瘀，與其他藥物配伍可治心血管疾病，性甘酸微溫，入肝、脾、胃三經。神麴能消化難消之食物並顧護胃氣，性甘辛溫，入脾、胃二經。麥芽能消澱粉類食物並回乳，性甘平，入肝、脾、胃三經。萊菔子能消澱粉類食物，最適合體弱之患者，性辛甘平，入脾、胃、肺三經，能除脹滿、降肺氣並袪痰。穀芽能消食化積、健胃降氣、開胃和中，性甘平，入脾、胃二經。禁忌／慎用：山楂於脾胃虛弱及消化性潰瘍（此藥可刺激胃酸分泌）患者慎用，不宜長期使用。神麴孕婦慎用。麥芽於無食積者慎用，長期使用可能耗氣，哺乳婦女大劑量使用者禁用。萊菔子於氣血兩虛或無食積者禁用，長期使用或大劑量使用可能耗氣。藥物交互作用：山楂與地高辛（Digoxin，商品名Lanoxin）交互作用可產生強心效果，使用時應監測以避免副作用。麥芽與降血糖藥物交互作用，因其可降低血糖濃度。《中醫藥學》，Chen and Chen著，2004年，第535、523、526、529、531頁"
    },
