    {
      "number": 469,
      "question_en": "A patient presents with edema all over her body including significant facial edema (puffy face and eyelids). She also reported abnormally cold hands and feet, painful abdomen, vertigo, shortness of breath, and fatigue. Her tongue was dark and wet, and her pulse was thin and weak. The patient was prescribed Shi Pi Yin (Bolster the Spleen Decoction) which reduced the edema temporarily but soon thereafter became ineffective. Which of the following formulas would be the best new formula to prescribe to treat the condition?",
      "question_hant": "某患者全身水腫，包括明顯之顏面水腫（面部及眼瞼浮腫）。她亦訴說手足異常冰冷、腹痛、頭暈、氣短及疲倦。舌質暗而濕潤，脈細弱。醫者予以實脾飲治療，水腫暫時減輕，但隨後即失效。下列何方最適合作為新的治療處方？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Wu Zhu Yu Tang (Evodiae Decoction)",
          "hant": "吳茱萸湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Wu Ling San (Five Ingredient Formula with Poria)",
          "hant": "五苓散",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Zhen Wu Tang (True Warrior Decoction)",
          "hant": "真武湯",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "zhu ling tang (polyporus decoction)",
          "hant": "豬苓湯",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Edema is caused by disorders of the lungs, spleen, and kidneys. Very often the strategies focus on the lungs and spleen but when there is a kidney deficiency, it must be addressed to have any long-lasting effect in the treatment of the edema. In this case, the wet tongue coat and deficiency pulse indicates that the kidneys are impaired and the formula needs to nourish the kidney water metabolism effort (kidney yang) to be able to clear the edema. The original formula worked to some degree for a short period of time as it works effectively to discharge water although it ignored the root cause of the water collection in the first place. Zhen wu tang utilizes zhi fu zi to activate the kidney yang while maintaining the discharging qualities of fu ling and bai zhu. Wu ling san is a very good formula to treat spleen deficiency edema. This would likely have similar results as the originally prescribed formula. Wu Zhu Yu Tang treats cold striking the middle burner and liver. This is not the pattern of this patient's condition. Zhu Ling Tang treats a shao yin heat syndrome. Clearing heat in this case of shao yin stage cold disease would not be advised. The Clinical Application of Shang Han Lun Formulas, Chen, Rui-Chun, 2009, pgs. 183-184.",
      "exp_hant": "水腫乃因肺、脾、腎三臟功能失調所致。治療策略常著重於肺脾，然若兼有腎虛，則必須加以處理方能使水腫治療獲得長久之效。此案例中，舌苔濕潤與脈虛弱顯示腎已受損，處方須能溫養腎之水液代謝功能（腎陽），方能消除水腫。原方在短期內確有一定療效，因其能有效利水，然卻忽略了水液停聚之根本病因。真武湯以製附子激發腎陽，同時保留茯苓、白朮之利水之效。五苓散為治脾虛水腫之良方，然其效果可能與原處方相似。吳茱萸湯治中焦與肝經受寒，此非本案之證型。豬苓湯治少陰熱化證，此案屬少陰寒化，清熱並不適宜。《傷寒論方劑臨床應用》，Chen, Rui-Chun著，2009年，第183-184頁。"
    },
    {
      "number": 470,
      "question_en": "A 16 year old male patient arrives at your office complaining that his dentist has asked him to seek treatment for his teeth grinding. He was given a mouthpiece to wear but finds it uncomfortable and does not use it. His dentist fears that he will wear out his teeth. The young man is a relatively healthy student who reports that his roommates have complained of the noise he makes grinding his teeth at night. Upon a full inquiry and examination, it was revealed that he has a bitter taste in his mouth and a dry throat. He reported being tired and in slightly low spirits but attributed it to his upcoming semester exams. His tongue was light red and his pulse was strong and moderate. What formula would you use as the base formula for this young man?",
      "question_hant": "一名16歲男性患者前來就診，主訴其牙醫要求他為磨牙問題就醫治療。他曾配戴牙套，但覺得不舒服而未持續使用。牙醫擔心他會因磨牙而磨損牙齒。這名青少年是一位相對健康的學生，他表示室友抱怨他夜間磨牙的聲音。經詳細問診與檢查後，發現他有口苦與咽乾之症狀。他自述感到疲倦、精神略顯低落，但將此歸因於即將到來的期末考試。舌質淡紅，脈強而緩。此青年應以何方作為基礎方劑？",
