      "exp_en": "The formula zhu ye shi gao tang (lophatherus and gypsum decoction) treats qi-level heat lingering in the Lungs and Stomach where the heat injures the qi and fluids. This formula treats the recovery stage of the aftermath of a febrile disorder. The more pronounced heat has lessened but low-grade fever with sweating remains. This formula clears heat, generates fluids, augments qi, and harmonizes the Stomach. This formula has the ability to clear lurking heat and tonfy qi deficiency. INGREDIENTS: dan zhu ye (herba lophatheri gracilis), shi gao (gypsum), mai men dong (tuber ophiopogonis japonici), ban xia (rhizoma pinelliae ternatae), ren shen (radix ginseng), jing mi (nonglutinous rice), gan cao (radix glycyrrhizae uralensis). The chief herb is shi gao whose cold nature clears heat from the Lungs and Stomach. Its acrid nature vents pathogenic heat to the exterior. Its sweet nature generates fluid to stop thirst. The formula has three deputies. The herb dan zhu ye is sweet-bland-cold and enters the Heart, Lung, and Stomach channels. The herb dan zhu clears lingering heat through urination and vents the upper jiao. The other two deputies are ren shen and mai men dong which work together to moisten the Lungs, nourish the yin, benefit the Stomach, generate fluids, and clear Heart heat to eliminate irritability. The assistant herb is zhi ban xia which directs rebellious qi down to stop nausea and vomiting. The herb zhi ban xia is warm-acrid and can be seen as a wrong herb to include in the formula. However, when zhi ban xia is combined with herbs that clear heat and generate fluids, it strengthens Spleen qi and reduces the cloying and stagnating effects of the herb mai men dong. The envoy herbs are zhi gan cao and jing mi assist ren shen in tonifying the qi and harmonizing the middle jiao to protect the Stomach from being injured by shi gao. CONTRAINDICATION: Febrile disorder with abundant normal and pathogenic qi, when the Fever remains high or when there is no damage to qi and yin. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 155",
      "exp_hant": "竹葉石膏湯治肺胃氣分餘熱未清，其熱耗傷氣津。本方治熱病後期恢復階段之餘證，明顯之高熱已減退，然低熱兼汗出仍存。本方能清熱、生津、益氣並和胃，具有清餘熱兼補氣虛之效。組成：淡竹葉、石膏、麥門冬、半夏、人參、粳米、甘草。君藥為石膏，其寒性能清肺胃之熱，辛味能透邪外達，甘味能生津止渴。方中有三味臣藥：淡竹葉性甘淡寒，入心、肺、胃三經，能經由利尿清除餘熱並透散上焦。另兩味臣藥為人參與麥門冬，二者合用能潤肺、養陰、益胃生津，並清心熱以除煩。佐藥為製半夏，能降逆氣以止噁心嘔吐。製半夏性溫辛，看似與本方不合，然與清熱生津之藥配伍後，能健脾氣並減輕麥門冬滋膩留滯之弊。使藥為炙甘草與粳米，輔助人參益氣並和中，以保護胃氣不受石膏所傷。禁忌：熱病正邪俱盛、高熱不退，或氣陰尚未受損之情況不宜使用。《方劑學》第二版，Bensky著，第155頁"
