      "exp_en": "Sylvia is clearly suffering from Yin deficiency with flourishing fire. Although both da bu yin wan and liu wei di huang wan treat symptoms of Yin deficiency, the former focuses more on quelling fire, whereas liu wei di huang wan is best for treating Yin deficiency with turbid Yin. The focus of da bu yin wan is to conserve water in order to quell excess fire. Symptoms of fire can include tidal fever, burning pain in the knees or low back, and irritability. Forcefulness in the rear position of the pulse shows intense heat affecting the Kidneys. By contrast, liu wei di huang wan nourishes Kidney Yin by regulating the Qi dynamic and eliminating pathogenic water. It can therefore be used to treat Yin deficiency accompanied by phlegm or other types of water excess. The formula jia wei xiao yao san can treat night sweats, but it is best used for a background of Liver Qi stagnation with Blood deficiency, Spleen Qi deficiency, and deficiency heat. In this pattern, Liver Qi constraint damages the Blood, which in turn leads to heat. The pulse in this case would likely be rapid but wiry. Although suan zao ren tang also treats night sweats and irritability, its hallmark indication is insomnia. This pattern is due to Blood deficiency of the Liver and Heart. In this case, heat would likely cause a dry throat and mouth, and the pulse would be either wiry or thready and rapid. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 124, 365, 375, and 466",
      "exp_hant": "Sylvia明顯患有陰虛火旺之證。雖然大補陰丸與六味地黃丸皆能治陰虛之症狀，然前者較著重於降火，後者則更適合治療陰虛兼水濁之證。大補陰丸之重點在於滋水以制盛火，火旺之症狀可包括潮熱、膝部或腰部灼痛及心煩易怒。尺部脈有力顯示腎部熱邪熾盛。相對地，六味地黃丸則透過調節氣機、袪除病理水液以滋養腎陰，故可用於治療兼有痰濁或其他水液過剩之陰虛證。加味逍遙散雖能治盜汗，然最適合用於肝氣鬱結兼血虛、脾氣虛及虛熱之背景證型。此證型中，肝氣鬱滯損傷血分，進而化熱，其脈象可能表現為數而弦。酸棗仁湯雖亦能治盜汗與心煩，然其主要指徵為失眠，此證乃因肝心血虛所致，此情況下之熱象可能導致咽乾口燥，脈象則可能為弦或細數。《方劑學》第二版，Bensky著，第124、365、375、466頁"
