      "exp_en": "The main actions of the formula are to enrich the yin, drain fire, stabilize the exterior, and stop sweating. The night sweats are caused by internal fire arising from a deficiency of yin and blood. The Heart is yang, associated with the Fire element, and resides in the upper jiao. The Kidneys are yin, are associated with the Water element, and reside in the lower jiao. In this pattern there is a deficiency of the Water element below which is then unable to control the Fire element above. This results in the blazing Fire above consuming the Water below. When a person sleeps, the wei qi enters the ying qi. However, when the yin is deficient, the yin is unable to restrain the yang in the exterior which becomes unstable. The uncontrolled yang and the inner Fire results in the opening of the pores and the pushing out of the yin fluids. This produces night sweating and fever. When the person wakes up, the wei qi leaves the ying qi, returns to the exterior, and sweating stops. When the unanchored Fire blazes up there can be a red face, dry mouth, and parched lips. As sweat is a Heart fluid, chronic sweating can eventually injure the Heart yin and cause irritability and restlessness. The dry stool and dark-scanty urine are the result of deficiency fire. The tongue is red from the deficiency heat and dry from the deficiency of yin. The pulse is rapid from the deficiency heat. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 218",
      "exp_hant": "本方主要功用為滋陰瀉火、固表止汗。盜汗乃因陰血虧虛所生之內火所致。心屬陽，應火行，居於上焦；腎屬陰，應水行，居於下焦。此證中，下焦水之不足，使其無法制約上焦之火，導致上炎之火耗傷下焦之水。人於入睡時，衛氣入於營氣，然陰虛則陰不能斂陽，致使肌表之陽氣浮動不穩。失於制約之陽氣與內火迫使腠理開泄，逼迫陰液外出，因而產生盜汗與發熱。醒後衛氣離營返表，汗出隨即停止。失於潛藏之火上炎，可致面赤、口乾、唇燥。因汗為心之液，久汗可終致心陰受損，而生心煩不安。大便乾結與小便量少色深皆為虛火所致之結果。舌紅乃因虛熱，舌乾則因陰虛。脈促則因虛熱所致。《方劑學》第二版，Bensky著，第218頁"
