      "exp_en": "The Chief herb is dang gui. The Deputy herbs are chuan xiong and tao ren. The Assistant herbs are pao jiang and yellow wine. The Envoy herb is zhi gan cao. The main actions of the formula are to invigorate the blood, transform and dispel blood stasis, warm the menses, and alleviate pain. During the time just after childbirth the nutritive qi and blood can be deficient. This requires tonification. There can also be abdominal pain due to blood stagnation. The strategy requires tonification with dispersion. The chief herb dang gui is used in large dose (24g) to tonify and move the blood, transform blood stagnation, and produce new blood. When blood is abundant the blood vessels will be full which aids in the circulation and smooth movement of blood. This promotes transformation of blood stasis. The deputy herbs are chuan xiong, which invigorates blood and promotes qi movement, and tao ren, which invigorates blood and dispels stagnation. One of the assistant hers is pao jiang which enters the blood, dispels cold, warms the menses, and alleviates pain. The herb pao jiang assists chuan xiong and tao ren in warming and unblocking blood stagnation. The other assistant is yellow wine with which the formula is prepared with. The wine warms and dispels cold. The envoy zhi gan cao relates the other herbs. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 581",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為當歸。臣藥為川芎、桃仁。佐藥為炮薑、黃酒。使藥為炙甘草。此方主要功效為活血化瘀、溫經止痛。產後營血多有不足，須予以補養；同時亦常因血瘀而生腹痛，故治法須補中兼散。君藥當歸重用（24克）以補血行血、化瘀生新。血充則脈道充盈，有助血行通暢，並促進瘀血之化解。臣藥川芎活血行氣，桃仁活血祛瘀。佐藥之一炮薑入血分，祛寒、溫經止痛，協助川芎、桃仁溫通血瘀。另一佐藥為黃酒，方以此酒為引，取其溫通散寒之性。使藥炙甘草調和諸藥。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第581頁"
    },
