      "exp_en": "The Chief herbs are bai he, sheng di huang, and shu di huang. The Deputy herbs are mai men dong and xuan shen. The Assistant herbs are chuan bie mu, dang gui, and bai shao. The Envoy herb is gan cao. This formula nourishes the yin, moistens the Lungs, transforms phlegm, and stops coughing. This formula enriches yin and controls deficiency heat. It generates metal and water to enrich the yin. The chief herb bai he moistens and nourishes dryness in the Lungs and clears heat. The other chief herb sheng di huang enriches yin, tonifies the Kidneys, and cools the blood to stop bleeding. The third chief herb is shu di huang which strongly tonifes the Liver and Kidney yin. The deputy herb mai men dong tonifies yin particularly in the upper jiao. It also assists bai he to assist the Lungs and tonify the yin. The other deputy herb xuan shen helps the Kidney water to rise to the Lung to clear deficiency fire and treat steaming bones. The assistant herb chuan bie mu moistens the Lungs, transforms phlegm, and stops coughing. The other assistant herbs dang gui and bai shao nourish the blood to support the yin. The envoy herb gan cao harmonizes the actions of the other herbs. When gan cao is combined with jie geng, together they benefit the throat. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 384",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為百合、生地黃、熟地黃。臣藥為麥門冬、玄參。佐藥為川貝母、當歸、白芍。使藥為甘草。此方滋陰潤肺、化痰止咳，滋陰而制虛熱，生金生水以養陰。君藥百合潤肺養陰、清熱；另一君藥生地黃滋陰補腎、涼血止血；第三味君藥熟地黃則力補肝腎之陰。臣藥麥門冬滋養上焦之陰，並助百合潤肺養陰；另一臣藥玄參助腎水上濟於肺，清虛火、退骨蒸。佐藥川貝母潤肺化痰止咳，另二佐藥當歸、白芍養血以助陰。使藥甘草調和諸藥，與桔梗同用則能利咽。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第384頁"
