      "exp_en": "The Chief herbs are zhi ban xia and hou po. The Deputy herbs are fu ling and zi su ye . The Assistant herb is si sheng jiang. The main actions of the formula are to promote qi movement, dissipate lumps, direct rebellious qi down, and transform phlegm. This formula treats patterns where qi stasis and phlegm mutually reinforce each other. When qi is stagnant, the phlegm cannot be resolved. If the phlegm is not transformed, the qi will not be moved. This formula opens the qi movement (primary action) and at the same time transform phlegm (secondary action). The two chief herbs are zhi ban xia and hou po. The herb zhi ban xia transforms phlegm, dissipates clumps, redirects rebellious qi down, and harmonises the Stomach. The herb hou po eliminates the stifling sensation and assists zhi ban xia in redirected rebellious qi. The first deputy herb is fu ling which leaches out dampness and assists zhi ban xia in transforming phlegm. The second deputy is zi su ye which is acrid-light-warm-dispersing and reinforces the action of hou po to regulate qi and break stagnation. The herb hou po enters the Lungs which govern the throat and treats the symptoms of feeling something stuck in the throat. The herb hou po helps focus the action of the formula on the Lung channel and to relieve cough, should the symptom manifest. The assistant herb si sheng jiang which helps the chief herbs harmonize the Stomach and stop vomiting. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 516",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為制半夏、厚朴。臣藥為茯苓、紫蘇葉。佐藥為生薑。此方主要功效為行氣散結、降逆化痰。此方治氣滯與痰凝互結之證：氣滯則痰難化，痰不化則氣難行。此方一方面開通氣機（為主要作用），一方面化痰（為次要作用）。二君藥為制半夏與厚朴：制半夏化痰散結、降逆和胃；厚朴消除胸悶感，並助制半夏降逆。臣藥之一茯苓滲利水濕，助制半夏化痰；另一臣藥紫蘇葉辛香輕散，加強厚朴理氣散結之力。厚朴入肺經，肺主咽喉，故能治咽中如有異物梗阻之症。厚朴使此方作用集中於肺經，若兼見咳嗽亦可緩解。佐藥生薑助君藥和胃止嘔。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第516頁"
