      "exp_en": "The Chief herb is gan jiang. The Deputy herb is ren shen. The Assistant herb is bai zhu. The Envoy herb is zhi gan cao. The formula warms the middle burner and strengthens the Spleen and Stomach. The formula specializes in treating cold xu in the middle jiao. The formula combines the treatment principle of both warming the interior cold and at the same time dispelling the cold. The formula tonifies the qi of the Stomach and Spleen. The chief herb is gan jiang which warm the Spleen and Stomach yang and gets rid of internal cold. The deputy herb ren shen tonifies the source qi which results in strengthening the yang and normalizing the ascending and descending functions of the middle jiao. When the Spleen is weak, it does not adequately transform and transport body fluids which can lead to water stasis and accumulation of dampness. The assistant herb bai zhu helps the deputy herb ren shen in tonifying the Spleen but also strengthens the Spleen and dries up dampness. The envoy herb zhi gan cao tonifies the qi of the middle jiao and harmonizes the other herbs in the formula. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 257",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為乾薑。臣藥為人參。佐藥為白朮。使藥為炙甘草。此方溫中健脾，專治中焦虛寒之證，同時兼顧溫裡與散寒之治則，並補益脾胃之氣。君藥乾薑溫脾胃之陽、祛除內寒。臣藥人參補益元氣，使陽氣得以強健，並使中焦升降功能恢復正常。脾氣虛弱則不能正常運化輸布水液，易致水停濕聚。佐藥白朮助臣藥人參補脾，同時健脾燥濕。使藥炙甘草補益中焦之氣，並調和諸藥。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第257頁"
