      "exp_en": "The formula bai tou weng tang (pulsatilla decoction) treats jue yin stage damp-heat disorders with diarrhea. This formula clears heat, resolves toxicity, cools the blood, and alleviates dysenteric disorders. In classical texts, thirst and a wiry pulse with toxic damp-heat are key signs that the presence of the pathogen has entered jue yin. The chief herb is bai tou weng which treats dysenteric disorders by clearing damp-heat and fire toxins from the Large Intestine and especially from the blood level. The two deputy herbs are huang lian and huang bai. The herb huang lian is bitter-cold and clears damp-heat, particularly in the Stomach and Intestines. huang bai clears lower jiao damp-heat. The deputies assist the chief herb in clearing damp-heat to relive dysenteric disorders and diarrhea. The assistant herb qin pi is cold-bitter and astringent. Qin pi restrains diarrhea and helps the actions of the other herbs in the formula. CONTRAINDICATION: Spleen yang deficiency or long-term use. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 210",
