      "exp_en": "The formula zhen wu tang (true warrior decoction) treats shao yin stage deficient cold with difficult urination. The formula focuses on shao yin patterns with yang deficiency and water flooding. The shao yin stage has fatigue and lethargy with a faint-thin pulse that indicates the yang qi is failing to transform the yin. This formula warms the yang and promotes urination. The formula treats the root of the pattern which is Kidney yang xu by strengthening and warming the gate of fire. The chief herb is zhi fu zi which is very hot, tonifies fire, and restores Kidney yang. These actions activate the Kidney function of transforming water. The deputy herbs are bai zhu and poria which tonfiy the Spleen and promote urination. fu ling also drains pathogenic dampness through urination. The assistant herb sheng jiang warms and dispels pathogenic dampness which assists the actions of the deputy herbs. sheng jiang also disseminates Lung qi and warms the Stomach. Bai zhu and fu ling tonify Earth to control Water. The other assistant herb is shao yao which preserve yin and alleviates pain. shao yao also prevents the dry-hot herbs that promote urination from injuring the yin. CONTRAINDICATION: Bensky does not list any contraindication. Chen and Chen lists water accumulation caused by an excess disorder as a contraindication. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 744; Chinese Herbal Formulas, Chen and Chen, page 1136",
      "exp_hant": "真武湯治少陰病陽虛寒盛、小便不利之證。此方著重於少陰病陽虛水泛之證，少陰病見神疲乏力、脈微細，示陽氣不足以化陰。此方溫陽利水，治其本——腎陽虛，透過溫壯命門之火以治之。君藥製附子大辛大熱，溫補真火、恢復腎陽，能激發腎主水之功能。臣藥白朮與茯苓健脾利水，茯苓亦能滲利邪濕。佐藥生薑溫散水濕，助臣藥之功，並宣肺、溫胃。白朮與茯苓合用健脾（培土）以制水。另一佐藥白芍斂陰止痛，並防諸利水藥之燥性傷陰。禁忌：Bensky未載明禁忌；Chen and Chen則指出水飲屬實證者為禁忌。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第744頁；《中醫方劑學》，Chen and Chen，第1136頁"
