      "exp_en": "The formula xiang su san (cyperus and perilla leaf powder) is used to treat tai yang stage with wind-cold occurring in conjunction with qi constraint in the interior. Exterior wind-cold obstructs Lung qi which in turn obstructs the Stomach and Spleen qi. The formula treats wind-cold with interior qi stasis. Wind-cold symptoms (aversion to cold, fever, headache, lack of sweating) are combined with qi stasis in the middle burner (chest fullness, poor appetite). The herb xiang fu activates qi circulation to relieve qi stasis. The herb zi su ye dispels the exterior wind-cold and relieves chest congestion. It is often selected to treat digestive disorder such as with the stomach fu by harmonizing the middle burner. The herb chen pi assists xiang fu to regulate the qi flow and harmonize the middle burner. The herb zhi gan cao harmonizes the herbs and strengthens the middle burner. CONTRAINDICATION: None listed. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 29",
      "exp_hant": "香蘇散用於治療太陽病風寒外襲，兼裡氣鬱滯之證。外感風寒鬱阻肺氣，肺氣不宣進而影響脾胃之氣。此方治風寒兼內部氣滯之證：風寒表證（惡寒、發熱、頭痛、無汗）與中焦氣滯（胸悶、納呆）並見。香附行氣以解氣滯；紫蘇葉解表散風寒、寬胸，亦常用於治療兼有胃腸不適之證，能和中焦。陳皮助香附理氣、和中。炙甘草調和諸藥，並健脾。禁忌：未載明。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第29頁"
