      "exp_en": "E TCM term \"consumptive deficiency\" refers to middle burner deficiency cold. The formula xiao jian zhong tang (minor construct the middle decoction) treats tai yin stage with mild deficient cold and abdominal pain by warming the middle burner. The formula warms and tonifies the middle burner and moderates spasmodic abdominal pain. This formula strengthens the middle qi and regulates yin and yang. INGREDIENTS: yi tang (maltosum), gui zhi (rammulus cinnamomi), bai shao (radix peoniae), sheng jiang (rhizoma zingiberis), da zao (fructus jujubae). The chief herb yi tang is sweet which is associated with earth. It tonifies both qi and blood, generates fluids, relieves thirst, and moderates abdominal spasms. The deputy herbs are bai shao and gui zhi. The herb gui zhi warms the middle burner and disperses cold while bai shao which is sweet-sour benefits the yin. The protective qi is yang which requires tonification and warming. The nutritive qi is yin which requires sweet herbs. The assistant herbs sheng jiang and da zao combine these functions while at the same time tonifying the middle burner. The envoy herb zhi gan cao helps the deputy herbs to stop the spasmodic abdominal pain and also harmonizes the action of the other herbs. The sweet warming herbs of the formula tonify the deficient cold while the acrid-sour herbs harmonize the protective and nutritive qi. The acrid-sweet herbs facilitate yang transformation while the sour-sweet herbs facilitate yin transformation. CONTRAINDICATION: Heat with yin xu. Modify the formula with vomiting or with abdominal distention.-. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 264",
      "exp_hant": "中醫術語「虛勞」在此指中焦虛寒。小建中湯治太陰病輕度虛寒兼腹痛之證，功能溫補中焦，方法為溫養中焦。此方能強壯中氣，調和陰陽。組成：飴糖、桂枝、白芍、生薑、大棗。君藥飴糖味甘，甘屬土，能補氣血、生津止渴，並緩解腹部拘急疼痛。臣藥為白芍與桂枝：桂枝溫中散寒，白芍甘酸而能益陰。衛氣屬陽，需溫補；營氣屬陰，需甘藥以養之。佐藥生薑與大棗兼具此二功能，同時亦補益中焦。使藥炙甘草助臣藥緩解腹部拘攣疼痛，並調和諸藥。方中甘溫之藥溫補虛寒，辛酸之藥調和營衛；辛甘之藥助陽化，酸甘之藥助陰化。禁忌：熱證兼陰虛者忌用；若見嘔吐或腹脹則需加減使用。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第264頁"
