      "exp_en": "The formula yin chen hao tang (artemisia yinchenhao decoction) in \"Discussion of Cold Damage\" treats jaundice arising due to a strong tai yang protective reaction that generates heat that then combines with clumps of internal dampness already present in tai yin. This formula clears heat, resolves dampness, and reduces jaundice. Heat and dampness clump and accumulate in the interior to form \"stasis heat\". This formula treats internal clumping of heat and dampness that steams to the skin to produce yang jaundice yellowing of the skin. INGREDIENTS: yin chen hao (herba artemisiae yinchenhao), zhi zi (fructus gardeniae jasminoidis), da huang (radix et rhizoma rhei). The chief herb yin chen treats all the different types of jaundice, especially the yang type due to damp-heat. A large dose to increase its action. The deputy zhi zi clears heat from the three jiaos, especially dampness through the lower jiao through urination.The assistant herb da huang purges heat, removes stagnation heat, and has a downward directing movement. da huang expels retained pathogenic toxins generated by the clogging of the qi by damp-heat. The three herbs work together to drain damp-heat and clear out the jaundice. CAUTION: Modify formula with yin jaundice. Use with extreme caution during pregnancy. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 710",
      "exp_hant": "《傷寒論》中的茵陳蒿湯治因太陽衛氣抗邪強烈而生熱，此熱復與太陰原有內濕相合而致之黃疸。此方清熱、利濕、退黃。濕熱互結蘊於內，形成所謂「瘀熱」，此方治濕熱內結、蒸於肌表而發為陽黃之證。組成：茵陳蒿、梔子、大黃。君藥茵陳蒿善治各類黃疸，尤以濕熱所致之陽黃為主，重用以增強其效。臣藥梔子清瀉三焦之熱，尤能通過利小便清除下焦濕邪。佐藥大黃瀉熱、除積，性主下行，能驅除因濕熱阻遏氣機而蓄積之邪毒。三藥合用，共奏清利濕熱、退黃之效。注意：陰黃須加減使用；孕婦應極其慎用。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第710頁"
    },
