    {
      "number": 512,
      "question_en": "A patient was treated in your clinic for high fever with sweating and thirst after traveling for business across the country and feeling sick for the last week. He also complained about nausea and constipation at that time. You prescribed Da Cheng Qi tang (Major Order the Qi Decoction) for three days. The patient now reports to your office with a swollen throat, intermittent nosebleed, and a slight fever that has not fully resolved. He reports that his nausea and abdominal tenderness has subsided although he still does not regularly move his bowels (he has a history of regular bowel movements). How would you modify his formula to match his current state?",
      "question_hant": "某病人因出差跨州旅行、勞累染病一週，於診所就診，見高熱汗出、口渴，並訴噁心與便秘。您予以大承氣湯服用三日。病人現回診，主訴咽喉腫痛、間歇性鼻衄，並仍有輕微未盡之發熱。其噁心與腹部壓痛已消退，但仍未能規律排便（其素有規律排便之病史）。應如何調整其方劑以符合其目前病情？",
      "image": null,
