          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "No modification to the original formula is needed at this time",
          "hant": "目前無需調整原方",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Da Cheng Qi Tang has four ingredients (da huang, mang xiao, hou po, and zhi shi). This is to treat a yang ming organ syndrome with the four greatnesses and constipation from dessicated intestines due to the great heat. By removing the hou po and zhi shi and adding gan cao, the formula created in Tiao Wei Cheng Qi Tang (Regulate the Stomach and Order the Qi Decoction) which is for yang ming organ syndrome but is the mildest of the laxative cheng qi tang formulas with no apparent discomfort of the abdominal region or with abdominal palpation. The removal of hou po and zhi shi suggests that the constipation is so mild that there is not much qi regulation needed from the obstruction caused by constipation. Removing mang xiao from da cheng qi tang creates xiao cheng qi tang which is a formula for mild heat in the yang ming organ level. In this level, there is constipation and stagnation which can be cleared through the purging action of the da huang (the extra purging and softening actions of the mang xiao are not needed here) and the qi regulation actions of the hou po and zhi shi. Removing da huang and adding huang qi and rou gui would not be beneficial for this patient. The purging actions of the da huang is needed to remove the obstruction trapping the heat in the yang ming and adding a hot herb like rou gui would exacerbate the heat symptoms and likely further injure the yin. Huang qi would be good in the case of qi and blood deficiency underlying but not in this case. Keeping da cheng qi tang for the patient's current presentation would be too strong as the patient's strongly excess symptoms have subsided. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 327-331.",
      "exp_hant": "大承氣湯由四味藥組成（大黃、芒硝、厚朴、枳實），用以治陽明腑實證，具「四大」之候，並因大熱灼傷腸道津液而致燥屎內結、便秘。若去厚朴、枳實而加甘草，則成調胃承氣湯，同治陽明腑實證，但為承氣類方中最輕之瀉下方，腹部並無明顯不適或按壓疼痛。去厚朴、枳實提示便秘程度極輕，不需太多因便秘阻滯氣機而生之理氣藥。若由大承氣湯去芒硝，則成小承氣湯，治陽明腑輕度熱結之證：此階段仍有便秘與積滯，可藉大黃之瀉下作用清除（芒硝額外之瀉下軟堅之力於此已非必要），並輔以枳實、厚朴之理氣功能。對此病人而言，去大黃而加黃耆、肉桂並無助益：大黃之瀉下作用乃為去除困陽明之熱結所必需，而加入肉桂此類熱藥將加重熱象，並可能進一步傷陰。黃耆適用於氣血兩虛之證，非此病人所宜。若維持原方大承氣湯不變，則對此病人目前之病情而言藥力過強，因其原本強烈之實證已消退。《傷寒論：寒傷論》，Mitchell, Craig; Ye, Feng; Wiseman, Nigel著，1999年，第327至331頁。"
