      ],
      "exp_en": "The formula huang lian e jiao tang (coptis and ass hide gelatin decoction) treats shao yin stage disorders of the heart and kidney. The shao yin corresponds to the Kidneys (control fluids, store essence) and the Heart (controls blood vessel, stores shen). The result is excess heat at the qi level where the heat enters yang ming combined with xu yin and blood. The main actions of the formula are to enrich yin, cause fire to descend, eliminate irritability, and calm the spirit. The formula treats excess heat and blood xu. The blood xu symptoms mainly show in the Heart symptoms. What the formula does is direct fire down by using bitter-cooling herbs while at the same time using sweet-salty-sour herbs to nourish blood and yin. The chief herb is huang lian which clears heat in the Heart and thus calms the mind. The other chief herb is e jiao which helps to control Heart fire by nourishing the blood. These two chief herbs manifest an interaction between water and fire to treat both the root and branch. The deputy herbs are the bitter-cooling huang qin which drains heat from the upper jiao and from the Intestines. The herb huang qin helps huang liang in directing fire down. The other deputy herb is shao yao which sour-cooling and helps e jiao to enrich yin. The assistant herb and envoy is egg yolk (ji zi huang) which enters the Heart and Kidneys, tonifies yin and blood, and clears toxic heat. It helps the herbs which drain heat while protecting from their drying nature. It also works with the blood and yin tonifying herbs. CONTRAINDICATION: None listed. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 469",
      "exp_hant": "黃連阿膠湯治少陰病心腎不交之證。少陰對應腎（司水液、藏精）與心（主血脈、藏神）。其病機為邪熱盛於氣分，熱邪傳入陽明，兼陰血之虛。此方主要功效為滋陰、降火、除煩、安神，治熱盛兼血虛之證，血虛之症狀主要表現於心。此方之法乃以苦寒之藥引火下行，同時以甘鹹酸之藥滋養陰血。君藥黃連清心火以安神；另一君藥阿膠滋養陰血以制心火。此二君藥呈現水火相濟之作用，標本兼治。臣藥黃芩苦寒，清瀉上焦與腸道之熱，助黃連引火下行。另一臣藥白芍酸寒，助阿膠滋養其陰。佐使藥雞子黃入心腎二經，滋養陰血，並清解熱毒，既助清熱藥而不傷其燥性，又能配合養血滋陰之藥發揮作用。禁忌：未載明。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第469頁"
    },
