      "exp_en": "The formula tao he cheng qi tang (peach pit decoction to order the qi) treats tai yang bowel disease with blood stasis in the lower burner (blood buildup). Source texts say that the disorder is due to the transmission of an external pathogenic factor entering the lower burner and transforming into heat and obstructing the blood. The pathogenic factor can enter either the water level or the blood level. Both water and blood can build up. In this pattern it is the blood that builds up. If the exterior has been released but there is still acute clumping and pain in the lower abdomen then the strategy is to purge with this formula. The blood build up disturbs the lower burner and cause acute lower abdominal pain but does not disturb the Bladder qi (urination is normal). There is fever at night, an unclear spirit (delirious talk, irritability, restlessness), thirst, and possible mania. The main actions of the formula are to drain heat and break up blood stasis. This formula is derived from modifying tiao wei cheng qi tang (regulate the stomach and order the qi decoction) with the addition of tao ren and gui zhi. The addition of these two herbs changes tiao wei cheng qi tang from a formula which purges clumping of heat and stools to a formula which breaks up blood stasis. The chief herb is tao ren which eliminate blood stasis and da huang which purges accumulations and clears pathogenic heat. The formula works by guiding blood stasis out which leaves the heat unable to attach to anything and is thus more easily cleansed. The deputy herb gui zhi warms the sinews, unblocks the vessels, and dispels retained blood from the lower jiao. The herb gui zhi unblocks the circulation of blood in the vessels and assists tao ren in breaking up blood stasis. The assistant herb mang xiao softens hardness and expels accumulation. which helps da huang in moving the stool, draining heat, and eliminating blood stagnation. The herb zhi gan cao acts an assistant and envoy to protect the Stomach and calm the middle jiao through moderating the harsh nature of the other herbs. Taking this formula should cause loose stools or mild diarrhea which are signs indicating the elimination of pathogenic heat. CONTRAINDICATION: Pregnancy. IF there are still exterior symptoms, release the exterior before prescribing the formula. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 559",
      "exp_hant": "桃核承氣湯治太陽腑證下焦蓄血之證。古籍記載此證乃因外邪傳入下焦、化熱而阻遏血分所致。邪氣可入水分或血分，水與血皆可蓄積；此證則屬蓄血。若表證已解，但少腹仍有急結疼痛，則治則為攻下，此方即為攻逐蓄血而設。蓄血擾及下焦，致少腹急痛，但不影響膀胱之氣化功能（小便自利）。可見夜間發熱、神志不清（譫語、心煩、躁動不安）、口渴，甚或發狂。此方主要功效為瀉熱、破血逐瘀。此方乃調胃承氣湯加桃仁、桂枝化裁而成；加入此二藥後，方義由原本瀉熱結、通大便，轉為破血逐瘀。君藥桃仁破血逐瘀，大黃瀉熱結、清瀉邪熱。此方藉引導蓄血外出，使熱邪無所依附而更易清除。臣藥桂枝溫通經脈、通利血脈，並祛除下焦蓄留之瘀血，能通利血中之循環，助桃仁破瘀。佐藥芒硝軟堅散結，助大黃通便瀉熱，並消散瘀血。炙甘草兼具佐使之功，保護脾胃、緩和中焦，並緩解諸藥之峻烈之性。服此方後宜見大便溏薄或輕度腹瀉，此為邪熱得以排出之徵象。禁忌：孕婦忌用。若仍有表證，應先解表，再議攻下。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第559頁"
