      "exp_en": "The main actions of the formula are to invigorate blood, dispel blood stasis, warms the menses, and alleviates pain. The formula is a combination of tao hong si wu tang (four substance decoction with safflower and peach pit) and shi xiao san (sudden smile powder). The formula is indicated for cold due deficiency that leads to blood stagnation. The formula will have not only cold symptoms but also blood stagnation symptoms. The herbs dang gui, chuan xiong, and chi shao nourish blood, invigorate blood circulation, and eliminate blood stagnation. The ingredient dry fried wu ling zhi disperses blood stagnation to stop pain. The herb pu huang regulates blood, The herbs yan hu suo and mo yao activate qi and blood to stop pain. The herb gan jiang warms the menses and dispels cold. The herbs xiao hui xing and rou gui warm the lower jiao to alleviate pain. The combination of rou gui with dang gui and chuan xiong treat dysmenorrhea, postpartum abdominal pain or amenorrhea arising from xu cold in the the chong mai and ren mai. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 567; Chen and Chen, page 889",
      "exp_hant": "此方主要功效為活血逐瘀、溫經止痛。此方為桃紅四物湯與失笑散之合方，適用於虛寒導致血瘀之證，故臨床上既見寒象，亦見血瘀之象。方中當歸、川芎、赤芍養血活血、化瘀。炒五靈脂散瘀止痛。蒲黃調血。延胡索、沒藥行氣活血止痛。乾薑溫經散寒。小茴香與肉桂溫暖下焦以止痛。肉桂與當歸、川芎合用，可治因沖任虛寒所致之痛經、產後腹痛或閉經。《方劑學》，Bensky，第二版，第567頁；Chen and Chen著，第889頁"
