      "exp_en": "Xi xian cao dispels wind dampness and unblocks the channels and collateral to treat pain in the joints, cramping and weakness in the legs. Wei ling xian dispels wind dampness, unblocks the channels, and alleviates pain. This herb is often combined with directional herbs like qiang huo for the upper, and niu xi for the lower, to treat wind damp bi syndrome in specific areas of the body. For wind heat body aches, herbs like ge gen or bo he would be more useful. Gout is typically blood stasis due to internal damp heat. The fact that it is worse with internal cold means that herbs that warm the interior should be used. An herb like zhi fu zi could be helpful in this situation. Qi stagnation causing pain in the arms is best served by using herbs that move qi rather than herbs that treat wind damp. Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pgs 357, 326",
      "exp_hant": "豨薟草祛風濕、通經絡，可治關節疼痛、下肢拘攣痿弱；威靈仙祛風濕、通經絡、止痛。此二藥常配合具引經作用之藥物，如上肢用羌活、下肢用牛膝，以治療特定部位之風濕痹證。若為風熱身痛，則葛根或薄荷更為適宜。痛風多因內有濕熱、血瘀所致；若兼內寒偏盛，則應使用溫裡藥，如製附子較為合適。氣滯所致手臂疼痛，宜用行氣藥而非祛風濕藥。Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pgs 357, 326"
