      "exp_en": "This formula was created by Zhang Zhongjing to treat kidney deficiency patterns with symptoms of water metabolism malfunction and wasting and thirsting. This serves as the basis of the famous yin tonifying formula liu wei di huang wan. When cold due to deficiency of the kidney yang sinks down and settles in the lower burner causing painful urination, Lu rong and chen xiang are paired to treat this occurrence. Lu rong strongly tonifies and warms the kidney yang with its sweet, salty, and warm nature while chen xiang warms both the spleen and the kidneys (the two organs responsible for water metabolism), and moves the qi to alleviate pain. Chen xiang also has a downwards nature that solidifies the qi dynamic of the lower burner. Gui zhi is in the formula to benefit the joints, warm the channels, promote qi transformation in the bladder, and unblock the vessels. To increase these functions on the surface does not seem to be a bad thing for this condition but it leaves out the spleen which is also partially responsible for the metabolism of water. Chen xiang is also bitter which strongly moves downwards which is lost by increasing gui zhi. Zhi fu zi is in the formula as the chief herb to warm the source qi, dispel cold, and eliminate dampness. Although fu zi strongly promotes movement, it is not bitter and therefore the movement is not specifically directed downwards. Zhi fu zi also warms all three burners while this condition is concentrated on the lower burner. Sheng jiang has a light and airy quality which tends to float upwards (particularly when used in larger doses). This herb is primarily a middle jiao herb but also treats the lungs in the upper burner. This pathology is located in the lower burner. Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pgs 764, 536, 30; Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pgs 395-400",
      "exp_hant": "此方為張仲景所創，用以治療腎虛所致水液代謝失常及消渴之證，亦為著名滋陰方六味地黃丸之基礎方。若腎陽虛寒下沉於下焦而致小便疼痛，則配伍鹿茸與沈香以治之。鹿茸味甘鹹性溫，能強力溫補腎陽；沈香則能溫脾腎（此二臟共主水液代謝），並行氣止痛，其沉降之性亦能穩定下焦之氣機。桂枝於方中能利關節、溫通經脈、助膀胱氣化、通利血脈；若僅增加其表位之作用，雖非壞事，卻遺漏了同司水液代謝之脾臟；且沈香味苦而沉降之性，若僅增桂枝亦無法取代。製附子為方中君藥，能溫補元陽、散寒除濕；雖附子行氣力強，然其性不苦，故其行散並非專主下行；且附子能溫通三焦，而此證病位集中於下焦。生薑輕浮上揚（尤其用量較大時更甚），主要作用於中焦，兼治上焦之肺，與此病位在下焦者不符。Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, Bensky, 2004, pgs 764, 536, 30; Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pgs 395-400"
