      "exp_en": "Huai Hua San treats rectal bleeding due to heat. Huang lian and huang bai are both cold herbs that drain heat from the Large Intestine. Adding these two herbs to Huai Hua San will increase the formula's ability to clear heat and stop rectal bleeding. Da huang and mang xiao are more appropriate for heat in the Large Intestine leading to severe constipation. Jue ming zi and dang gui also move the bowels, but without addressing the severe heat. Add di yu and huang qin to the formula for treating bleeding hemorrhoids. Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, 3rd Edition, Bensky, Clavey, and Stoger, pages 111, 134, 138, 235, 240, and 748; Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Scheid, Bensky, Ellis, and Barolet, pages 605 and 606",
