      "exp_en": "COMMON: All of these herbs calm the Liver and sedate yang. DIFFERENCES: The herb Shi Jue Ming clears the Liver and brightens the eyes and clears Stomach Fire. It is salty and cold. It enters the Liver channel. The herb Mu Li softens hardness, reduces nodules, and consolidates jing. It is salty, astringent, and cool. It enters the Liver and Kidney channels. The herb Dai Zhe Shi cools blood, stops bleeding, and reverses rebellious Stomach qi. It is bitter and cold. It enters the Heart and Liver channels. The herb Bai Ji Li disperses Liver qi stagnation, dispels wind to brighten the eyes, and relieves itching. It is bitter, acrid, and neutral. It enters the Liver channel. The herb jue ming zi clears the Liver fire, clears the vision and benefits the eyes, calms the Liver and anchors Liver Yang. It is bitter, sweet, and slightly cold. It enters the Liver and Kidney channels. CAUTIONS/CONTRAS: The herb Shi Jue Ming is contraindicated with Spleen and Stomach deficiency-cold or with poor appetite and loose stools. The herb Mu Li is contraindicated with damp-heat or excess patterns. The herb Dai Zhe Shi should be used with caution during pregnancy or with cold conditions. The herb Bai Ji Li should be used with caution with blood deficiency. It is contraindicated during pregnancy. The herb jue ming zi is contraindicated in diarrhea due to Spleen xu and during pregnancy. DRUG INTERACTIONS: The herbs Bai Ji Li and Jue Ming Zi, though undocumented, may increase the effect of diuretic drugs. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 809, 796, 797, 799, 801, 803",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：以上諸藥皆能平肝潛陽。差異：石決明能清肝明目，並清胃火；性鹹寒，入肝經。牡蠣能軟堅散結、固澀腎精；性鹹澀而涼，入肝、腎二經。代赭石能涼血止血、降逆胃氣；性苦寒，入心、肝二經。白蒺藜能疏肝解鬱、祛風明目、止癢；性苦辛而平，入肝經。決明子能清肝火、明目益眼、平肝潛陽；性苦甘微寒，入肝、腎二經。禁忌：石決明忌用於脾胃虛寒或食慾不振、大便溏瀉者。牡蠣忌用於濕熱或實證。代赭石孕婦及寒證患者慎用。白蒺藜血虛者慎用，孕婦忌用。決明子脾虛泄瀉者及孕婦忌用。藥物交互作用：白蒺藜與決明子雖無明確記載，然可能增強利尿藥之藥效。Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 809, 796, 797, 799, 801, 803"
    },
