      "exp_en": "The formula si wu tang is formulated according to the principles of the four seasons. The dang gui is sweet, warm, and acrid. It represents the genesis of Blood, similar to the sun in the Spring. The herb chuan xiong is acrid, warm, and dispersing. It represents the growth of Summer. The herb bai shao is sour and astringent. It represents the harvest in the season of autumn. The herb shu di huang is rich and tonifying. It represents the storing of Blood in winter. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: Due to the stagnating nature of the herb shu di huang, the formula should be used with caution in cases of deficiency of the Spleen and Stomach. It should be used with caution during pregnancy. The formula is contraindicated in the treatment of blood or qi collapse, yin xu heat, and with middle burner deficiency with diarrhea. Chinese Herbal Formulas and Applications, Chen and Chen, 2009, page 569",
      "exp_hant": "四物湯之組成乃依四季之理而設。當歸味甘、性溫、味辛，象徵血之生發，猶如春日之陽氣初生。川芎辛溫發散，象徵夏季之生長。白芍酸澀收斂，象徵秋季之收穫。熟地黃質潤而滋補，象徵冬季血之閉藏。禁忌：因熟地黃滋膩易礙脾胃，本方於脾胃虛弱者宜謹慎使用，孕婦亦應慎用。本方禁用於氣血暴脫、陰虛內熱及中焦虛寒兼腹瀉者。Chinese Herbal Formulas and Applications, Chen and Chen, 2009, page 569"
