      "exp_en": "COMMON: All four herbs promote diuresis, treat edema, and dysuria syndrome. DIFFERENCES: The herb Fu Ling harmonizes the Stomach, and promotes digestion. It is sweet, bland, and neutral. It enters the Heart, Spleen, and Kidney channels. The herb Zhu Ling exerts a stronger diuretic function than the other three herbs. It is sweet, bland, and neutral. It enters the Kidney and Bladder channels. The herb Ze Xie strongly promotes diuresis, treats vertigo and dizziness caused by damp accumulation, and clears empty Kidney fire. It is sweet, bland, and cold. It enters the Kidney and Bladder channels. The herb Yi Yi Ren strengthens the Spleen, treats painful obstruction syndrome due to dampness, and clears heat to expel pus. It is sweet, bland, and cool. It enters the Spleen, Stomach, and Lung channels. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: The herb Fu Ling should be used with caution with yin deficiency and/or spermatorrhea. The herb Zhu Ling is contraindicated for patients with dizziness due to yin xu or patients with thirst and dampness. The herb Ze Xie does not list a caution or contra. The herb Yi Yi Ren should be used with caution in patients with spermatorrhea and polyuria. It is contraindicated during pregnancy. DRUG INTERACTIONS: The herb Fu Ling, Zhu Ling, and Ze Xie, though not documented, may increase the effect of diuretic drugs. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 428, 383, 385, 387, 389",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：四藥皆能利水滲濕，治水腫及淋證。差異：茯苓能和胃、助消化；性甘淡而平，入心、脾、腎三經。豬苓利水滲濕之力較其餘三藥更強；性甘淡而平，入腎、膀胱二經。澤瀉能強力利水滲濕，治濕邪內停所致眩暈、頭暈，並清虛火；性甘淡而寒，入腎、膀胱二經。薏苡仁健脾、治濕邪痹阻之痹證，並清熱排膿；性甘淡而涼，入脾、胃、肺三經。禁忌：茯苓陰虛及遺精者宜慎用。豬苓禁用於陰虛眩暈或口渴兼濕盛之患者。澤瀉無特別記載之禁忌。薏苡仁遺精及多尿患者宜慎用；孕婦禁用。藥物交互作用：茯苓、豬苓與澤瀉雖未有明確記載，然可能增強利尿藥之藥效。Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 428, 383, 385, 387, 389"
