      ],
      "exp_en": "COMMON: All three herbs tonify the Spleen and help to harmonize herbal formulas. DIFFERENCES: The herb Gan Cao tonifies Heart qi, moistens the Lung, sedates fire, and detoxifies. It is sweet and neutral. It enters the Spleen, Stomach, Lung, and Heart channels. The herb Da Zao tonifes blood. It is sweet and warm. It enters the Spleen and Stomach channels. The herb Yi Tang reduces pain and relieves cough. It is sweet and warm. It enters the Spleen, Stomach, and Lung channels. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: The herb Gan Cao can create dampness and is contraindicated with nausea/vomiting, chest and abdominal fullness due to damp excess. The herb Da Zao is contraindicated in excess damp, excess heat, or hot phlegm as the herb can create dampness. The herb Yi Tang should be used with caution with middle burner dampness or with vomiting due to stasis. It is contraindicated with cough due to hot phlegm. DRUG INTERACTIONS: The herb Gan Cao may alter the therapeutic effect of corticosteroids such as prednisone. It should be used with caution with cardiac drugs such as digoxin. The herb Gan Cao can treat overdosages of cocaine, caffeine, nicotine, and barbiturates. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 972, 866, 872, 87",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：三藥皆能補脾益氣，並能調和諸藥。差異：甘草能補心氣、潤肺、瀉火解毒；性甘平，入脾、胃、肺、心四經。大棗能補血；性甘溫，入脾、胃二經。飴糖能緩急止痛、止咳；性甘溫，入脾、胃、肺三經。禁忌：甘草易助濕，忌用於噁心嘔吐、胸腹脹滿等濕邪偏盛之證。大棗禁用於濕邪偏盛、實熱或痰熱之證，因其能助濕生痰。飴糖於中焦濕盛或瘀血所致嘔吐者宜慎用；禁用於痰熱咳嗽者。藥物交互作用：甘草可能改變皮質類固醇（如強體松）之療效；與強心類藥物（如毛地黃）併用時應謹慎。甘草可用於治療古柯鹼、咖啡因、尼古丁與巴比妥類藥物之中毒。Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 972, 866, 872, 87"
    },
