      ],
      "exp_en": "Both formulas nourish yin and blood to treat palpitations, anxiety, insomnia, and dry stools. The zhi gan cao tang treats blood xu failing to nourish the Heart. When qi is weak, the yang is weak and fails to generate the pulse resulting in intermittent pulse. The formula uses herbs that tonify and warm the qi combined with herbs that nourish yin and blood. The formula tian wang bu xin dan treats disorders due to Heart yin and blood xu with an excess Heart yang flaring, There is anxiety, reduced sleep, palpitations, a depressed shen, and nervousness due to a failure of nourishing the shen. This formula uses nourishing herbs and shen calming herbs. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: The formula tian wang bu xin dan is contraindicated with Spleen and Stomach xu with loose stools and disorders with phlegm-damp stagnation. Do not take long term. The formula zhi gan cao tang is contraindicated with yin xu heat or with severe diarrhea. Chinese Herbal Formulas and Applications, Chen and Chen, 2009, page 592",
      "exp_hant": "二方皆能滋陰養血，以治療心悸、焦慮、失眠及大便乾燥。炙甘草湯治血虛而無以養心；若氣虛則陽氣亦虛，無以鼓動脈搏，因而出現結代脈。本方使用補氣溫陽之藥，配合滋陰養血之品。天王補心丹則治心陰血虛而心陽偏亢之證，症見焦慮、睡眠減少、心悸、神志抑鬱及煩躁不安，乃因心神失養所致。本方使用滋養與安神之藥物。禁忌：天王補心丹禁用於脾胃虛弱兼大便溏瀉，及痰濕停滯之證，不宜久服。炙甘草湯禁用於陰虛內熱或嚴重腹瀉者。Chinese Herbal Formulas and Applications, Chen and Chen, 2009, page 592"
