      "exp_en": "COMMON: All four herbs disperse wind-heat, clear heat in the Liver, and brighten the eyes. DIFFERENCES: The herb Sang Ye clears Lung heat, stops coughing, and stops bleeding. It is bitter, sweet, and cold. It enters the Lung and Liver channels. The herb Ju Hua is stronger at clearing heat in the Liver and clears toxins. It calms Liver yang. It is acrid, sweet, bitter, and cool. It enters the Lung and Liver channels. The herb Man Jing Zi relieves headaches, dispels wind and relieves pain. It is acrid, bitter, and cool. It enters the Liver, Stomach, and Bladder channels. The herb Mu Zei stops bleeding. It is sweet, bitter, and neutral. It enters the Lung, Liver, and Gallbladder channels. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: The herb Sang Ye is cold and should be used with caution with constitutional deficiency or cold. The herb Ju Hua shuld be cautiously used in patients with qi xu or cold in the Stomach (diarrhea, poor appetite). It is contraindicated in yang xu or deficiency and cold. The herb Man Jing Zi should be used cautiously for patients with Spleen/Stomach deficiency or yin empty heat or patients with blood xu headaches or dizziness. The herb Mu Zei should be used cautiously with deficiencies (qi, blood, yin or yang), during pregnancy. It should not be used with red eyes due to Liver yang rising. Avoid long term use. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 97, 74, 75, 77, 79",
      "exp_hant": "共同點：四藥皆能疏散風熱、清肝熱、明目。差異：桑葉能清肺熱、止咳、止血；性苦甘而寒，入肺、肝二經。菊花清肝熱之力較強，並能清熱解毒，兼能平肝陽；性辛甘苦而涼，入肺、肝二經。蔓荊子能治頭痛、祛風止痛；性辛苦而涼，入肝、胃、膀胱三經。木賊能止血；性甘苦而平，入肺、肝、膽三經。禁忌：桑葉性寒，體質虛弱或偏寒者宜慎用。菊花於氣虛或胃寒（腹瀉、食慾不振）患者宜慎用；陽虛寒證者禁用。蔓荊子於脾胃虛弱、陰虛內熱，或血虛頭痛、頭暈者宜慎用。木賊於氣、血、陰、陽諸虛及孕婦宜慎用；肝陽上亢所致目赤者不宜使用；避免長期使用。Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 97, 74, 75, 77, 79"
