      "exp_en": "Both formulas include the herbs in si wu tang (four substance decoction) to tonify blood. The formula tai shan pan shi san is a qi and blood tonic that can stabilize the fetus. The clinical picture includes a restless fetus or a threatened miscarriage, pale complexion, poor appetite, fatigue, a pale tongue, and a slippery-weak or deep-weak pulse. The formula shi quan da bu tang is a warm tonic that nourishes qi and blood. The chief symptoms are chronic cough, poor appetite, weak knees and back, and chronic uterine bleeding due to qi and blood xu. CAUTIONS/CONTRA: With tai shan pan shi san avoid excessive emotions, alcohol and sour, spicy and hot foods. The formula shi quan da bu tang is contraindicated with heat or excess disorders. DRUG INTERACTIONS: The formula shi quan da bu tang may have a marked protective effect against chemotherapy- and radiation-induced toxicities. Chinese Herbal Formulas and Applications, Chen and Chen, 2009, page 620",
      "exp_hant": "二方皆含四物湯之藥味以補血。泰山磐石散為氣血雙補之劑，能安胎。其臨床表現包括胎動不安或先兆流產、面色蒼白、食慾不振、疲倦、舌淡、脈滑弱或沉弱。十全大補湯為溫補氣血之劑，主治慢性咳嗽、食慾不振、腰膝痠軟及氣血兩虛所致之慢性崩漏。禁忌：服用泰山磐石散期間應避免情緒過激、飲酒及酸辣燥熱之食物。十全大補湯禁用於熱證或實證。藥物交互作用：十全大補湯可能對化療及放療所致之毒性具有明顯保護作用。Chinese Herbal Formulas and Applications, Chen and Chen, 2009, page 620"
