      "exp_en": "This is a yin deficiency pattern which requires yin tonifying foods that are neutral-sweet and refreshing-sweet. Grains or beans that tonify yin include barley (cool-sweet-salty, moistens dryness, nourishes yin), rice (neutral-sweet, tonifies qi and blood, produces body fluids), wheat (cool-sweet, nourishes heart yin, builds qi and blood, clears heat, tonfies spleen and kidneys), and black soybeans (neutral-sweet, tonifies spleen and kidneys, nourishes kidney yin, dispels wind and damp). Fish that tonify yin include oysters (cool-sweet-salty, tonifies liver, kidneys, blood, and yin), octopus (cool-sweet-salty, tonifies qi, blood, yin), crab (cold-sweet, tonifies yin), caviar (cold-salty, tonifies kidney yin), and carp (neutral-sweet-salty, tonifies qi and blood). Meats that tonify yin include pork (cool-sweet, tonifies blood and yin) and duck (cool-sweet-salty, tonifies qi, blood, and yin). Fruits that tonify yin include Asian pears (cold-sweet, tonifies body fluids, moistens, stops cough), blueberries (warm-sweet-sour, tonifies kidneys, nourishes blood, anti-aging), and avocado (cool-sweet, nourishes yin and blood, moistens lungs and intestines). Seeds that tonify yin include white sesame seeds (cool-sweet, tonifies body fluids and blood) and sunflower seeds (neutral-sweet, nourishes yin and moistens). Dairy products that tonify yin include butter (cool-sweet, tonifies qi and blood, moistens), sour cream (cool-sour-sweet, nourishes yin), and yogurt (cool-sour-sweet, nourishes yin and cools intestines). Small amounts of eggs, pork and cheese can tonify yin but should not be overdone as they can stimulate the Liver into heat. In yin deficiency, energetically warm bitter-hot or acrid-hot foods are to be avoided as well as coffee, red wine, and tobacco. The food choices in the other answers are energetically warm foods which should be restricted. Healing with Whole Foods, Paul Pitchford, 3rd Edition page 357; Chinese Nutrition Therapy, Kastner, 2004, page 87",
      "exp_hant": "此為陰虛證候，須選用性平甘或涼甘、能滋陰之食物。能滋陰之穀類或豆類包括大麥（涼、甘鹹，潤燥滋陰）、稻米（平、甘，補氣血、生津）、小麥（涼、甘，養心陰、益氣血、清熱、補脾腎）及黑豆（平、甘，補脾腎、滋腎陰、祛風濕）。能滋陰之魚貝類包括牡蠣（涼、甘鹹，補肝腎、益血滋陰）、章魚（涼、甘鹹，補氣血、滋陰）、螃蟹（寒、甘，滋陰）、魚子醬（寒、鹹，滋腎陰）及鯉魚（平、甘鹹，補氣血）。能滋陰之肉類包括豬肉（涼、甘，補血滋陰）與鴨肉（涼、甘鹹，補氣血滋陰）。能滋陰之水果包括亞洲梨（寒、甘，生津潤燥止咳）、藍莓（溫、甘酸，補腎養血、抗老）及酪梨（涼、甘，滋陰養血、潤肺腸）。能滋陰之種子類包括白芝麻（涼、甘，生津養血）與葵花子（平、甘，滋陰潤燥）。能滋陰之乳製品包括奶油（涼、甘，補氣血、潤燥）、酸奶油（涼、酸甘，滋陰）及優格（涼、酸甘，滋陰清腸）。少量蛋類、豬肉及乳酪亦能滋陰，惟不宜過量，以免助長肝熱。陰虛證候應避免性溫之苦熱或辛熱食物，亦應避免咖啡、紅酒與菸草。其餘選項中之食物皆屬性溫之品，應予節制。Healing with Whole Foods, Paul Pitchford, 3rd Edition page 357; Chinese Nutrition Therapy, Kastner, 2004, page 87"
