    {
      "number": 635,
      "question_en": "A patient comes in with poor digestion, fatigue, lack of appetite, and loose stools. He also reports difficulty falling asleep, muscle burning, and melancholy. You prescribe them Gui Pi Tang (Restore the Spleen Decoction) for one week but he returns the next day saying that he seems to be having some kind of reaction to the formula. He asks for a different formula and you decide to prescribe Si Jun Zi Tang (Four-Gentlemen Decoction) instead to hopefully avoid any reaction. He returns the next day saying that he reacted to this formula as well and now is feeling warmer than usual. What would be the best choice of formulas for this patient to hopefully avoid a reaction?",
      "question_hant": "一名患者主訴消化不良、疲倦、食慾不振及大便溏瀉。他還提及入睡困難、肌肉灼熱感及情緒低落。您為其處方歸脾湯，服用一週後，患者隔日回診表示對此方似乎產生某種反應。他要求更換處方，於是您改開四君子湯，希望能避免反應。他隔日再度回診，表示對此方亦產生反應，且現在感覺比平常更燥熱。為使此患者盡量避免產生反應，下列何方最為適當？",
