      "question_en": "A patient with gouty arthritis presents with a headache after hiking in the windy rock canyons in Utah. You prescribe Chuan Xiong Cha Tiao San (Chuanxiong Powder to be Taken with Green Tea) to treat the patient's headache which resolves within a day and a half. The patient returns to your office with visibly red and swollen knees, with achiness and heaviness of the lower legs. The tongue has a greasy, yellow coat and the pulse is slippery and slightly rapid. What formula would you prescribe for this patient?",
      "question_hant": "一名患有痛風性關節炎的患者，在猶他州多風的岩石峽谷健行後出現頭痛。您處方川芎茶調散治療患者的頭痛，一天半後頭痛緩解。患者再度回診，膝關節明顯紅腫，並伴有下肢痠痛沉重感。舌苔黃膩，脈滑略數。您會為此患者處方何種方劑？",
      "image": null,
