      ],
      "exp_en": "The Chief herbs are bie jia and qing hao. The Deputy herbs are sheng di huang and zhi mu. The Assistant herb is mu dan pi. This formula nourishes yin and vents heat, two things that should not be done by itself when a hot pathogenic factor settles in the body. One should not just nourish the yin because the cloying nature of the herbs can trap the heat internally. One should not just use bitter-cold herbs to drain fire because these herbs are drying and can injure the yin. What needs to be done is to simultaneously nourish the yin and vent the pathogenic heat. The herb bie jia is salty-cold and nourishes the yin to reduce empty heat from deficiency. Unlike other yin nourishing herbs, bie jia enters the collaterals to track the pathogen and clears heat from the yin. bie jia is combined with the aromatic-acrid herb qing hao that vents and expels heat. These two herbs, which are the chief herbs in the formula, work together to accomplish the task of nourishing yin and venting heat. The deputy herbs are sheng di huang and zhi mu, both of which assist bie jia, in nourishing yin and clearing heat. The assistant herb is mu dan pi which drains heat from the yin and helps qing hao in venting heat. The five herbs in the formula work together to nourish, clear, and vent. The formula treats both the root and branch. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 212",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為鱉甲與青蒿。臣藥為生地黃與知母。佐藥為牡丹皮。此方能滋陰、透熱，此二者在熱邪深伏體內時不可單獨施行。不可僅滋陰，因滋膩之品可能將熱邪內閉；亦不可僅用苦寒藥物瀉火，因這類藥物性燥，可能傷陰。應同時滋陰與透散伏熱。鱉甲鹹寒，能滋陰以退虛熱。與其他滋陰藥不同，鱉甲能入絡搜邪，清透陰分伏熱。鱉甲與辛香的青蒿合用，青蒿能透散、驅除熱邪。這兩味藥為方中君藥，共同完成滋陰透熱之任務。臣藥生地黃與知母皆助鱉甲滋陰清熱。佐藥牡丹皮能瀉陰分伏熱，並助青蒿透熱外出。方中五味藥協同作用，兼顧滋、清、透三法。此方標本兼治。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 212"
    },
