      "exp_en": "In cold damage cases where there is an increase in retching, precipitation cannot be used even when there are signs that the pernicious has moved into the yang ming. Generally, bitter purging is utilized in a case like this but the vomiting is a sign that the heat evil is not bound in the intestines and instead rises and insults the stomach and diaphragm region. When there is evil in the stomach causing counterflow, the strategy employed by da cheng qi tang cannot be used without causing vomiting and damaging the right qi. With the damage caused to the right qi, the evil descends deeper in the body and the condition worsens. It is important in these cases to differentiate the retching that can occur in shao disease as well. In Shao yang case retching, other signs indicating the shao yang stage will likely be present. This case does not show evidence of the evil moving into the tai yin. Although this is an atypical progression of disease and reaction to da cheng qi tang with the presenting symptoms, this does not appear to be a serious disease that needs immediate hospitalization. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgss. 363-364.",
      "exp_hant": "在傷寒病證中，若乾嘔症狀加劇，即使有邪入陽明之徵象，亦不可使用攻下法。此類病例一般會使用苦寒攻下之法，但嘔吐正顯示熱邪並未結於腸道，而是上逆侵犯胃與膈的部位。當邪氣在胃導致氣機上逆時，大承氣湯的治法若貿然使用，必會導致嘔吐並損傷正氣。正氣受損後，邪氣會更深入體內，病情因而加重。此類病例中，亦須注意辨別少陽病中亦可能出現的乾嘔症狀。少陽病乾嘔則通常伴有其他顯示少陽階段的徵象。此病例並無邪傳太陰之證據。雖然此病程進展及對大承氣湯的反應並非典型表現，但就目前所呈現的症狀而言，並不屬於需要立即住院治療的嚴重疾病。Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgss. 363-364."
