      "exp_en": "In the book \"Discussion of Cold Damage\" the formula ling gui zhu gan tang (poria, cinnamom twig, atractylodes, and licorice decoction) is selected to treat injury due to cold that is caused by the improper use of purgatives. The wrong treatment results in chest fullness and hypochondriac fullness combined with vertigo. The book \"Essentials from the Gold Cabinet\" prescribes this formula for thin mucus in the epigastric area that is resolved via urination. In TCM the term \"thin mucus\" refers to both a set of symptoms and as a disease causing factor. This formula is indicated for the deficient type of thin mucus arising from Spleen and Kidney yang xu. The formula however does not focus on treating the deficiency in the Spleen and Kidneys zang organs but rather focuses on harmonizing the fluids and qi dynamic. Harmonizing implies regulating yin and yang, water and fire. This formula warms and transforms phlegm and thin mucus, strengthens the Spleen, and resolves dampness. INGREDIENTS: fu ling (poria), gui zhi (ramulus cinnamomi), bai zhu (rhizoma atractylodi), zhi gan cao (radix glycyrrhizae). The chief herb fu ling tonifies the Spleen and drains dampness. It transforms thin mucus by treating the root which is the transportation and transformation of fluids, the metabolism of fluids. The deputy herb gui zhi warms yang and strengthens the transforming power of qi. The combination of fu ling and gui zhi work together to increase the circulation of fluids while warming the qi flow. The assistant herb bai zhu tonfies the transforming and transporting functions of the Spleen to dry dampness. The herb bai zhu combined with gui zhi has a stronger effect on tonifying Spleen yang to transform excess dampness. The envoy herb is zhi gan cao augments the qi of the middle jiao. zhi gan cao can cause mild stagnation but fu ling counteracts that. CONTRAINDICATION: thin mucus arising from damp-heat patterns with yin xu and hyper yang. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 735-737",
      "exp_hant": "《傷寒論》選用苓桂朮甘湯來治療因誤用攻下法所致的傷寒。誤治導致胸滿、脇滿並兼眩暈。《金匱要略》則以此方治療經由利小便而解的心下痰飲。中醫「痰飲」一詞，既指一組症狀，亦指一種致病因素。此方適用於因脾腎陽虛所致的虛證痰飲。然而此方並不著重於直接治療脾腎兩臟之虛，而是著重於調和津液與氣機。所謂調和，即調節陰陽、水火。此方能溫化痰飲，健脾利濕。組成：茯苓、桂枝、白朮、炙甘草。君藥茯苓能補脾滲濕，透過治療水液運化輸布失常之根本，即水液代謝，以化痰飲。臣藥桂枝能溫陽，增強氣化之力。茯苓與桂枝合用，能在溫通氣機的同時增進津液循環。佐藥白朮能補益脾臟運化輸布之功能以燥濕。白朮與桂枝合用，能加強溫補脾陽以化除水濕過盛，效果更強。使藥炙甘草能補益中焦之氣。炙甘草雖可能略微造成氣機壅滯，但茯苓能抵消此作用。禁忌：因濕熱兼陰虛陽亢所致之痰飲證不宜使用。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 735-737"
    },
