      "exp_en": "The burning anus is a clue that there is damp-heat in the condition and the prescription of Yin Chen Hao Tang (containing yin chen hao, zhi zi, and da huang) suggests that the liver and gallbladder is involved. If damp-heat attacks the liver and gallbladder, then there is a good chance that jaundice will develop and a formula like yin chen hao tang will be needed to remedy the condition. Yang Ming heat returning to the exterior is a very uncommon path however, if it were to return to the tai yang and block the pores, a formula like Ma Huang Tang would likely be needed to treat the condition. Fire rising to scorch the lungs leading to lung dryness can be treated with formulas like sheng mai san (if the lung qi also has been injured), sha shen mai men dong tang, or bei mu gua lou san (if there is also concurrent phlegm). If yang ming heat dessicates the blood causing blood stasis, formulas like di dang tang or tao he cheng qi tang can be used to treat the condition. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 369-370.",
      "exp_hant": "肛門灼熱是體內存在濕熱的線索，而處方茵陳蒿湯（由茵陳蒿、梔子、大黃組成）則顯示病位涉及肝膽。若濕熱侵犯肝膽，則極有可能發展為黃疸，此時需要如茵陳蒿湯這類方劑來治療。陽明熱邪還表是相當少見的傳變途徑，然而若邪熱還至太陽並阻閉毛竅，則可能需要如麻黃湯這類方劑來治療。火邪上炎灼肺導致肺燥，可用生脈散（若肺氣亦受損）、沙參麥門冬湯，或貝母瓜蔞散（若兼有痰證）等方劑治療。若陽明熱邪灼傷血分導致血瘀，則可使用抵當湯或桃核承氣湯等方劑治療。Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 369-370."
