      "exp_en": "This question examines which pre-existing condition would lead to the most serious case of a jue yin syndrome. The first patient shows a history of an exterior contraction and a tai yang syndrome moving into a jue yin syndrome. As an exterior and excess case syndrome, the body's resources are not severely injured prior to arriving at jue yin. Patient 2 exhibits symptoms of a shao yang syndrome leading to a jue yin syndrome. This path is a common one. With the shao yang being an excess syndrome, although the shao yang can damage the body's resources significantly, it would not be to the level of patient 3 who is coming from a shao yin syndrome. The shao yin syndrome is a deficiency of kidney yang with internal cold. The shao yin syndrome itself is a very serious and dangerous stage for a patient to be in. Patient 4 has a history of yang ming organ syndrome moving into jue yin. Although this is a very dramatic and symptomatic stage, this is still an excess syndrome where the body's resources are not yet exhausted as in the shao yin syndrome. Moving into a jue yin from a shao yin is clearly the most serious of the conditions and patient 3 needs to be treated first. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 534-535.",
      "exp_hant": "此題考察何種既有病史會導致最嚴重的厥陰病表現。第一位患者的病史顯示為外感邪氣，由太陽病傳入厥陰病。此為表證兼實證，因此在傳入厥陰之前，身體的正氣尚未受到嚴重損傷。第二位患者的症狀顯示由少陽病傳入厥陰病，此為常見的傳變途徑。少陽病雖為實證，雖可能明顯耗傷正氣，但程度仍不及第三位患者由少陰病傳來的情況。少陰病為腎陽虛兼內寒之證，少陰病本身即為患者所處階段中極為嚴重且危險的階段。第四位患者的病史為陽明腑證傳入厥陰。雖然此階段表現劇烈且症狀明顯，但仍屬實證，正氣尚未如少陰病那般耗竭。由少陰病傳入厥陰病顯然是所有病情中最為嚴重者，因此第3位患者須優先治療。Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 534-535."
    },
    {
      "number": 681,
      "question_en": "A patient presents with a high fever and a red, wet face and head. He mumbles and explains to you that he returned from a Boy Scouts winter camping trip a week ago in which his sleeping bag was unable to keep him warm during the extremely cold nights. For days after the trip, he felt abnormally cold and would suffer from chills until two days ago when he started warming up. His mother gave him colloidal silver, which she said was a natural antibiotic on day 2 of the chills but he was unable to say whether it helped or not. Currently, he complains of feeling \"too warm\" and has slight abdominal pain. He cringes when his abdomen is palpated with medium pressure. His pulse is surging and his tongue is red with a thick yellow coating. Which of the following formulas would be the most appropriate choice for this patient at this time?",
      "question_hant": "一名患者出現高熱，面部與頭部潮紅且濕潤。他喃喃自語，向您說明他一週前剛結束童軍冬令露營活動，露營期間睡袋無法在極寒的夜晚為他保暖。返家後數日，他感到異常畏寒並持續惡寒，直到兩天前才開始感覺回暖。他的母親在惡寒的第二天給他服用了膠體銀，並表示這是「天然抗生素」，但他無法確定是否有效。目前他主訴感覺「過於燥熱」，並有輕微腹痛。以中等力道按壓其腹部時他會畏縮。脈象洪大，舌紅苔厚黃。此時下列何方對此患者最為適當？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
