      ],
      "exp_en": "This patient was struck with an external issue during his camping trip with the extreme cold weather likely interfering with the body's yang function of protecting the body from evils. After the first few days, as his chills diminished and his fever increased, the external evil moved inwards into the yang ming stage. The case study identifies three of four of the \"Si Da\" symptoms (big fever, big pulse, big sweat). When a clinician can clearly identify three of the four \"big\" symptoms, a diagnosis of yang ming disorder can be established. Further, this patient's condition is in the organ stage with the abdominal pain reflecting the constipation that has occurred due to the heat dessicating the intestines. With the excess pulse and uncomfortable abdomen with palpation, Da Cheng Qi Tang is the best choice. If there was no discomfort with palpation of the abdomen, a milder formula like Xiao Cheng Qi Tang could be the best choice. Bai Hu Tang is the appropriate formula to use when the heat evil is still in the channel stage. This stage is characterized by the four great symptoms without the constipation. Bai Hu Jia Ren Shen Tang is used for yang ming syndrome with a concurrent qi deficiency. The surging pulse suggests that there is not a current state of qi deficiency. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 336-351.",
      "exp_hant": "此患者在露營期間因極端寒冷天氣而感受外邪，此天候可能干擾了身體衛陽袪邪護體的功能。最初幾天，隨著惡寒逐漸減輕、發熱逐漸加重，外邪已由表傳入陽明階段。此病例呈現出四大症狀（大熱、大脈、大汗、大渴）中的三項。當臨床醫師能清楚辨識出四大症狀中的三項時，即可確立陽明病之診斷。此外，此患者的病情已進入腑證階段，腹痛正反映出因熱邪灼傷腸道津液所致的便秘。結合實脈與按壓腹部不適之表現，大承氣湯為最佳選擇。若按壓腹部並無不適，則較為和緩的小承氣湯可能為最佳選擇。白虎湯適用於熱邪仍在經證階段時使用，此階段的特徵為四大症狀而無便秘。白虎加人參湯則用於陽明病兼氣虛之證。此患者脈洪大，顯示目前並無氣虛之狀態。Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 336-351."
    },
