      ],
      "exp_en": "Classically, there are three types of inversion: 1) emotional disorders with qi rushing upward from the abdomen to the chest. 2) sudden fainting. 3) extreme cold in the extremities. The formula si ni tang (frigid extremities decoction) treats the last one which can be selected in shao yin disorders to rescue the yang of the Kidneys, in tai yin to warm the cold within the Spleen, and in jue yin with devastated yang. It can also treat greater yang with inversion where the wrong use of a formula produced excess sweating which has devastated the yang. In brief, the formula si ni tang is usually selected to treat shao yin stage deficient cold. The formula rescues devastated yang, warms the middle burner, and stops diarrhea. When the yang is debilitated the yin flourishes. Treatment requires the use of strong warming-acrid herbs to break through the yin and rescue the yang. The chief herb zhi fu zi warms and stimulates the fire at the gate of vitality which gets disseminated throughout the whole body to reach the limbs. The deputy herb gan jiang warms the middle jiao and eliminates cold. As a result, the transformation-transportation functions of the Spleen are strengthened. The chief herb zhi fu zi and the deputy herb gan jiang work together in tonifying the middle jiao yang qi. The chief herb zhi fu zi warms the whole body by entering all twelve channels while the deputy herb gan jiang mainly focuses warming the Spleen, Stomach, and Lungs. The assistant herb zhi gan cao augments qi, tonifies the Spleen, reduces the toxicity of the chief herb, and moderates the drying nature of both the chief and deputy herbs. Because zhi gan cao is sweet, it can provide the matrix to which the acrid-hot nature of zhi fu zi to attach to in order to achieve its action without merely dissipating. CONTRAINDICATION: True heat and false cold with cold limbs, thirst with desire to drink cold liquids, dark urine, and a red tongue with yellow coating. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, pages 265-267",
      "exp_hant": "古典文獻中，「厥」分為三種類型：一為情志失調，氣自腹部上衝於胸；二為突然昏厥；三為四肢極度厥冷。四逆湯治療的是最後一種，可用於少陰病以回陽救逆，用於太陰病以溫散脾中之寒，用於厥陰病以救治陽氣衰敗。此方亦可治療太陽病誤治導致過度發汗而使陽氣衰敗的厥證。簡言之，四逆湯通常用於治療少陰病虛寒之證。此方能回陽救逆、溫中、止瀉。當陽氣衰微時，陰寒便會偏盛。治療須使用峻猛的溫辛藥物以破陰回陽。君藥製附子能溫壯命門之火，並將此火布散全身直達四肢。臣藥乾薑能溫中散寒，藉此增強脾之運化輸布功能。君藥製附子與臣藥乾薑相輔相成，共同補益中焦陽氣。君藥製附子能通行十二經以溫煦全身，臣藥乾薑則主要著重於溫煦脾、胃、肺。佐藥炙甘草能益氣補脾，降低君藥之毒性，並緩和君藥與臣藥的燥烈之性。因炙甘草味甘，能作為載體使製附子辛熱之性得以附著發揮作用，而非僅是耗散消失。禁忌：真熱假寒證，症見四肢厥冷、口渴欲飲冷、小便色深，舌紅苔黃者禁用。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, pages 265-267"
    },
    {
      "number": 683,
      "question_en": "Which formula treats tai yang warp disorder with an external pathogen at the surface and an internal water accumulation?",
      "question_hant": "何方治療太陽經證，表有外邪兼裡有蓄水之證？",
      "image": null,
