      "exp_en": "The formula wu ling san (five ingredient powder with poria) treats tai yang with accumulation or build up of water. Both water and blood can build up. They are the result of pathogenic factors entering tai yang organ, the bladder. In this pattern it is the water that builds up. Water buildup occurs when the pathogen enters the Bladder qi level which then fails to transform fluids. This causes urinary problems with either diarrhea or normal bowel movements. That is, this formula treats internal water accumulation when a pathogen remains in the exterior. The TCM diagnosis 1) water build--up, 2) Spleen xu, 3) retention of thin mucus in the lower jiao. This formula promotes urination, drains dampness, strengthens the Spleen, warms the yang, and promotes the transformative functions of qi. The formula combines herbs that drain dampness with herbs that promote the qi dynamic to resolve the exterior. INGREDIENTS: fu ling (sclerotium poriae cocos), ze xie (rhizoma alismatis orientalis), zhu ling (sclerotium polypori umbellati), bai zhu (rhizoma atractylodis), gui zhi (ramulus cinnamomi). The chief ingredient is ze xie which is sweet-bland-cold. ze xie leaches out dampness through promoting urination. The cold aspect of ze xie also eliminates the heat constraint that is generated by water accumulation or thin mucous blocking the ascent of yang qi. The deputy herb fu ling also leaches out dampness by promoting urination, tonifies the Spleen, and assist the yang. The other deputy herb is zhu ling also eliminates dampness and promotes urination. The chief and deputy herbs work together to drain dampness, regulate urination, and drain Bladder heat. The assistant herb bai zhu strengthens the Spleen function of transforming and transporting fluids to help resolve excess dampness. The ingredient gui zhi acts as both and assistant and as an envoy. gui zhi warms the gate of fire to assist the Bladder in transforming and facilitating urine. gui zhi also helps the Spleen qi raise the clear yang to facilitate the steaming fluids by Kidney yang, thus acting as an envoy. As an assistant ingredient, gui zhi helps to release the exterior part of the tai-yang disorder. The herbs work in pairs. fu ling and zhu ling promote urination. fu ling and bai zhu tonify the Spleen and promote urination. gui zhi and fu ling warm and transform body fluids, unblock the yang, and promote urination. CONTRAINDICATION: Limit dosage with Spleen and Kidney xu or avoid with thirst from excess heat or yin xu. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 724",
      "exp_hant": "五苓散治療太陽病兼水液蓄積之證。水與血皆可能發生蓄積，此為邪氣入侵太陽腑（膀胱）所致。此證型中蓄積者為水。當邪氣進入膀胱氣分，導致氣化不利，水液無法正常運化時，即會發生蓄水，造成小便異常，同時大便可能腹瀉或正常。也就是說，此方治療邪氣仍在表而體內卻發生蓄水之證。中醫診斷為：一、蓄水；二、脾虛；三、下焦痰飲停聚。此方能利小便、滲濕、健脾、溫陽，並促進氣化功能。此方結合滲濕藥物與行氣解表藥物，以達到解表之效。組成：茯苓、澤瀉、豬苓、白朮、桂枝。君藥澤瀉性甘、淡、寒。澤瀉能利水滲濕。其寒性亦能消除因水濕痰飲阻遏陽氣升發所生之鬱熱。臣藥茯苓同樣能利水滲濕、補脾、助陽。另一臣藥豬苓亦能滲濕利尿。君藥與臣藥相輔相成，共同滲濕、利尿並清膀胱之熱。佐藥白朮能強化脾臟運化輸布津液的功能，協助化解過盛的水濕。桂枝兼具佐藥與使藥之作用。桂枝能溫命門之火以助膀胱氣化利尿。桂枝亦能助脾氣升發清陽，以助腎陽蒸騰津液，因此發揮使藥之作用。作為佐藥時，桂枝有助於解除太陽病表證的部分。方中藥物成對配伍：茯苓與豬苓合用以利尿；茯苓與白朮合用以健脾利尿；桂枝與茯苓合用以溫化津液、通陽利水。禁忌：脾腎兩虛者應限制劑量，因熱盛或陰虛所致口渴者忌用。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 724"
    },
    {
