      "exp_en": "The formula gui zhi tang (cinnamon twig decoction) treats tai yang with exterior-cold-deficiency. The most important symptom for using this formula is sweating in an exterior pathogen invasion. Cold is a yin pathogen that attaches itself to nutritive yin. Nutritive yin becomes contracted and slowed which then reduces its ability to control the protective yang or wei qi. This results in excess outward and upward movement of wei qi manifesting as increased sweating and fever. This formula harmonizes the nutritive and protective qi. It both disperses excess external wind-cold at the wei qi level and also restores the normal flow of the nutritive qi. INGREDIENTS: gui zhi (ramulus cinnamomi), bai shao (radix paeoniae), sheng jiang (rhizoma zingiberis), da zao (fructus zizyphi), zhi gan cao (radix glycyrrhizae). The chief herb is gui zhi which releases external wind-cold from the muscle layer. The deputy herb is bai shao which benefits yin and contains weak nutritive qi. Acting together, gui zhi and bai shao strengthen the wei qi to expel the pathogenic factor while at the same time fortifying the nutritive qi. The assistant herb sheng jiang assists gui zhi to release the exterior and to also treat nausea-vomiting by directing qi downward while at the same time warming the middle jiao. da zao assists the deputy, bai shao, to nourish-harmonize the blood and nutritive qi. The herb zhi gan cao, the envoy, harmonizes the action of the herbs. zhi gan cao, gui zhi, and sheng jiang transform the yang nature of the disorder. The herb bai shao and da zao transform the yin nature of the disorder. CONTRAINDICATION: Exterior cold with interior heat. With internal heat it can result in epistaxis. Do not use with damp-heat. CAUTION: Use cautiously during the summer or during hot weather. NOTE: If this formula is incorrectly prescribed or the dosage is too much it can produce high fever, severe thirst, palpitations, and irritability. To counteract, prescribe bai hu jia ren shen tang (white tiger plus ginseng decoction). . Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 13, 14",
      "exp_hant": "桂枝湯治療太陽病表虛兼寒之證。使用此方最重要的症狀為外邪侵襲時出現的自汗。寒為陰邪，容易依附於營陰。營陰因而收斂遲滯，導致其約束衛陽（衛氣）的能力減弱。此結果造成衛氣過度向外、向上運行，表現為汗出增多與發熱。此方能調和營衛。既能疏散衛氣層面過盛的外感風寒，亦能恢復營氣的正常運行。組成：桂枝、白芍、生薑、大棗、炙甘草。君藥桂枝能解肌散除外感風寒。臣藥白芍能益陰，並涵養較弱的營氣。桂枝與白芍合用，能增強衛氣以袪除邪氣，同時亦能扶助營氣。佐藥生薑協助桂枝解表，並透過降氣及溫中以治療噁心嘔吐。大棗協助臣藥白芍以滋養調和血分與營氣。使藥炙甘草能調和諸藥。炙甘草、桂枝與生薑能轉化此證屬陽的部分。白芍與大棗則能轉化此證屬陰的部分。禁忌：表寒兼裡熱者忌用。若體內有熱，服用此方可能導致鼻衄。濕熱證忌用。注意事項：夏季或炎熱天氣使用時應謹慎。備註：若此方誤用或劑量過大，可能導致高熱、劇渴、心悸及煩躁。此時可處方白虎加人參湯以糾正。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 13, 14"
    },
