      "exp_en": "There are typically two pathomechanisms for a Tai Yin level disease. The first is when a patient has a constitutional weakness in the spleen yang and contracts a wind-cold or has internal damage which engenders cold. The second pathomechanism is when damage to the spleen occurs after a condition is improperly treated or not treated at all leading to a disease shift to the Tai Yin. This is a case of the latter. Tai Yin patterns are characterized by abdominal distention with periodic pain, lack of appetite, lack of thirst, nausea/vomiting and a moderate pulse. Since the pulse is not floating, this would not be characterized as a Tai Yang and there is no evidence of a constitutional spleen yang deficiency followed by an external contraction. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs 451-452.",
      "exp_hant": "太陰病通常有兩種致病機轉。第一種是患者素體脾陽不足，感受風寒，或因內傷而生寒。第二種致病機轉則是病情經誤治或未經治療，導致脾臟受損而使病情傳入太陰。本病例屬於後者。太陰病證型的特徵為腹脹兼陣發性疼痛、食慾不振、口不渴、噁心嘔吐及脈緩。由於脈象並非浮脈，因此不應歸類為太陽病，且亦無證據顯示患者素體脾陽虛而後感受外邪。Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs 451-452."
