      "exp_en": "The current state the patient is a shaoyang disorder evidenced by the alternating fever and chills, bitter taste in his mouth and wiry quality pulse. The weak pulse indicates how the shaoyang disorder appeared suddenly with a direct strike to the level due to the patient's deficient state. When a patient is weak, pernicious influences can attack deeper as the resistance to keep it on the exterior is weak. Pernicious attacks and immediately moves into the shao yang depth level. The report by the patient that he felt normal prior to being suddenly stricken with the shao yang symptoms indicates that this is not a tai yang disease moving into the shao yang. There is no evidence of a manifest yang ming stage. The presence of the chills indicates that the exterior has not fully resolved and both yang ming and tai yin are purely interior stages. Some of the symptoms presenting could be attributed to the jue yin stage. however the presence of fever and chills indicates that this would not be a solely interior disease. Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 415-416.",
      "exp_hant": "此患者目前的病情為少陽病，可從往來寒熱、口苦及弦脈得到印證。弱脈顯示此少陽病是因患者體虛，邪氣直中此層次而突然發病。當患者體質虛弱時，邪氣抵禦於表的能力薄弱，邪氣便可深入侵犯。邪氣直接侵襲並立即傳入少陽這一較深的層次。患者自述在突然出現少陽症狀之前感覺正常，顯示此並非太陽病傳入少陽病。亦無明顯的陽明病證據。惡寒的存在顯示表證尚未完全解除，而陽明與太陰皆屬純粹的裡證階段。部分症狀表現或可歸因於厥陰階段，然而發熱與惡寒並存則顯示此並非單純的裡證。Shang Han Lun: On Cold Damage, Mitchell, Craig, Ye, Feng, Wiseman, Nigel, 1999, pgs. 415-416."
