      "exp_en": "Bitter foods are yin and cooling in nature. They contract the qi and move the qi down. The bitter taste acts as sedation in an excess patient (loud voice, red face, robust body, thick tongue coating, excess pulse, etc). The bitter flavor clears heat, clears mucoid deposits (cholesterol) and can lower blood pressure. The bitter taste also lowers fever and drains dampness. The bitter taste helps with infections, inflammations, and conditions which has an excess of dampness. Patients who are slow, overweight, and lethargic can benefit from the bitter flavor. Patients who are deficient, weak, cold, thin, and dry should limit the bitter flavor in their diet. Healing with Whole Foods, Paul Pitchford, 3rd Edition page 314",
      "exp_hant": "苦味食物性屬陰而寒涼。它能收斂氣機並使氣下行。苦味對實證患者（聲音洪亮、面赤、體格壯實、舌苔厚、脈實等）具有鎮靜作用。苦味能清熱，清除濕濁黏膩沉積物（膽固醇），並能降血壓。苦味亦能退熱、瀉濕。苦味有助於感染、發炎及濕邪偏盛的病症。動作遲緩、體型肥胖、倦怠嗜睡的患者可從苦味中獲益。虛弱、體寒、形瘦、津液不足的患者則應限制飲食中苦味的攝取。Healing with Whole Foods, Paul Pitchford, 3rd Edition page 314"
