      "exp_en": "Excess eating under stress can lead to Liver invading the Stomach. Excess eating of red meat can lead to Liver Fire. Excess eating of fried foods can lead to Liver Damp-Heat. Deficient eating of meat can lead to Deficient Liver Blood. Stagnant Cold in Liver Channel arises from an invasion of external Cold. Eating under stress, in a hurry, while working, eating with anger can lead to Rebellious Liver Qi invading the Spleen/Stomach or Liver Yang Rising. Not eating enough nourishing foods such as meat and grains can weaken the Spleen function of producing sufficient Blood to be stored in the Liver and cause Liver Blood Xu, Liver Yin Xu or Liver and Heart Blood Xu. Excess eating of dairy or greasy foods or fried foods can generate Damp-Heat in the Liver. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 531;2005 Edition, page 503; 1989, Edition, 216",
      "exp_hant": "壓力下過食可導致肝犯胃。過食紅肉可導致肝火。過食煎炸食物可導致肝濕熱。肉食攝取不足可導致肝血虛。肝經寒滯多因外寒侵襲所致。在壓力下進食、匆忙進食、邊工作邊進食、帶著怒氣進食，皆可導致肝氣上逆犯脾胃或肝陽上亢。未能攝取足夠的滋養性食物（如肉類與穀類）會削弱脾臟化生足夠血液以藏於肝的功能，進而導致肝血虛、肝陰虛或肝心血虛。過食乳製品、油膩食物或煎炸食物可產生肝濕熱。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 531;2005 Edition, page 503; 1989, Edition, 216"
