        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "fu zi (aconiti radix lateralis preparata)",
          "hant": "附子",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Ionotropic means it affects muscle contraction and chronotropic means it affects heart rate. An arrhythmia is an abnormal heartbeat which causes the heart to beat too fast or too slow. Different types of fast arrhythmias include atrial fibrillation, atrial flutter, supraventricular tachycardia, ventricular tachycardia and premature heartbeats. Antiarrhythmic medications are used only to treat rapid heart rhythms. Slow arrhythmias, called bradycardia, are treated with a pacemaker. The herb fu zi should be taken with extreme caution with patients on antiarrhythmic drugs. This herb restores devastated yang and rescues from rebellion, warms Ming Men Fire and assists Heart, Kidney and Spleen yang, disperses Cold and Dampness, and warms the channels and stops pain. There are four main types of antiarrhythmic medications: 1) Sodium channel blockers block the sodium channel of the heart muscle cells which then decreases the speed of electrical conduction. Examples include procainamide (Procan SR), quinidine (Quinidex), and disopyramide (Norpace). 2) Beta blockers slow down heart rate during an episode of an abnormally fast heart rhythm. Example include metoprolol or Toprol XL. This type of medication is primarily used to control the heart rate during an arrhythmic episode and may also reduce the number of episodes experienced. 3) Potassium channel blockers block the potassium channel in the heart muscle cell and help prevent arrhythmias by lengthening the time of the electrical impulse between heartbeats. Examples include sotalol (Betapace) and dofetilide (Tikosyn). 4) Calcium channel blockers slow the heart rate in the presence of an abnormal heart rhythm. These drugs also treat hypertension. Examples of calcium channel blockers include diltiazem (Cardizem, Cartia) and verapamil (Tiazac, Calan). Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 162",
      "exp_hant": "Ionotropic（肌力性）是指影響肌肉收縮，chronotropic（變時性）是指影響心率。心律不整是指異常的心跳，會使心跳過快或過慢。快速性心律不整的類型包括心房顫動、心房撲動、室上性心搏過速、室性心搏過速及早發性心跳。抗心律不整藥物僅用於治療快速性心律。緩慢性心律不整（心搏過緩）則以心律調節器治療。附子這味藥對於服用抗心律不整藥物的患者應極為謹慎使用。此藥能回陽救逆，溫命門之火並助心、腎、脾之陽，散寒祛濕，溫通經脈止痛。抗心律不整藥物主要有四類：1）鈉離子通道阻斷劑會阻斷心肌細胞的鈉離子通道，進而減慢電傳導速度，例如普魯卡因胺（Procan SR）、奎尼丁（Quinidex）及丙吡胺（Norpace）。2）乙型阻斷劑於心律異常快速發作時可減慢心率，例如美托洛爾或 Toprol XL，此類藥物主要用於控制心律不整發作期間的心率，亦可能減少發作次數。3）鉀離子通道阻斷劑會阻斷心肌細胞的鉀離子通道，藉由延長心跳間的電衝動時間以預防心律不整，例如索他洛爾（Betapace）及多非利特（Tikosyn）。4）鈣離子通道阻斷劑可於心律異常時減慢心率，此類藥物亦可治療高血壓，例如地爾硫卓（Cardizem、Cartia）及維拉帕米（Tiazac、Calan）。Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 162"
    },
