      "exp_en": "The herb gan cao may alter the therapeutic effects of steroids such as cortisone, prednisone (Orasone), dexamethasone (Decadron), hydrocortisone (Cortef) and methoprednisolone (Medrol). Steroids can be used as the main treatment for certain inflammatory disorders, such as systemic vasculitis (inflammation of blood vessels) and myositis (inflammation of muscle). They may also be used selectively to treat inflammatory conditions such as rheumatoid arthritis, lupus, and asthma. The herb bai zhu interacts with diuretics and anti-coagulants. The herb hou po interacts with anti-coagulants. The herb sang zhi is not known to have any drug interactions. Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 866",
      "exp_hant": "甘草可能改變類固醇的療效，例如可體松、潑尼松（Orasone）、地塞米松（Decadron）、氫化可體松（Cortef）及甲基潑尼龍（Medrol）。類固醇可作為某些發炎性疾病的主要治療藥物，例如全身性血管炎（血管發炎）及肌炎（肌肉發炎）。亦可選擇性用於治療類風濕性關節炎、紅斑性狼瘡及氣喘等發炎性病症。白朮與利尿劑及抗凝血劑產生交互作用。厚朴與抗凝血劑產生交互作用。桑枝則未知有任何藥物交互作用。Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology, Chen and Chen, 2004, page 866"
