      "exp_en": "DMARDs are prescribed to reduce or prevent joint damage by rheumatoid arthritis (RA). From a TCM perspective, they can be posited to be attacking-draining medicinals with an emphasis on blood-quickening. In TCM bony deformation in advanced RA can be attributed to as caused mainly by stasis of Blood leading to an insufficient nourishment of the sinews-bones. The side effects of DMARDs include hematuria, chronic diarrhea, tongue inflammation, hair loss, anemia, hypokalemia (muscle weakness, irregular heart rhythm, cramping, flaccid paralysis, strong thirst, frequent urination, confusion). Some of these side effects can be classified as qi vacuity (hematuria, muscle weakness, frequent urination, chronic diarrhea) and Blood vacuity (anemia, cramping, hair loss, irregular heart rhythm). Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 375",
      "exp_hant": "DMARDs 用於減少或預防類風濕性關節炎（RA）所致的關節損傷。從中醫角度而言，可將其視為以活血為主的攻邪瀉法藥物。中醫認為，晚期類風濕性關節炎所出現的骨骼變形，主要是由血瘀導致筋骨失於濡養所致。DMARDs 的副作用包括血尿、慢性腹瀉、舌炎、落髮、貧血、低血鉀（肌肉無力、心律不整、抽筋、弛緩性癱瘓、劇渴、頻尿、意識混亂）。這些副作用中，部分可歸類為氣虛（血尿、肌肉無力、頻尿、慢性腹瀉），部分可歸類為血虛（貧血、抽筋、落髮、心律不整）。Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 375"
