      "exp_en": "Diuretics are used to promote urination to help treat hypertension, edema. Diuretics are posited to be drugs that drain Dampness and induce a free-flow of urination. The side effects of diuretics include lack of strength, fatigue, muscle cramps, headache, palpitations (arrhythmias), and orthostatic hypotension. During urination it is the qi that moves fluids out of the body. Each time we urinate we also lose that qi that is moving the fluids. The excess urination caused by the diuretics also cause qi vacuity (fatigue, weakness, hypotension). Body Fluids and Blood have a common source. When there is fluid desertion there can also be Blood vacuity (headache, muscle cramps). Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 358",
      "exp_hant": "利尿劑用於促進排尿，以協助治療高血壓、水腫。利尿劑可被視為能瀉濕並使小便通利的藥物。利尿劑的副作用包括乏力、疲倦、肌肉抽筋、頭痛、心悸（心律不整）及姿勢性低血壓。排尿過程是由氣推動體液排出體外，每次排尿也會耗損推動體液的氣。利尿劑所致的過度排尿也會造成氣虛（疲倦、乏力、低血壓）。津液與血同源，津液耗脫時亦可見血虛（頭痛、肌肉抽筋）。Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 358"
