      "exp_en": "Garlic can act as a cholesterol lowering agent, as a anticoagulant, and may lower plasma glucose levels. Anticoagulant: The sulfur compounds in garlic (ajoene, allicin) have an ability to block the aggregation of platelets and prevent the formation of clots. Atherosclerosis: garlic powder supplement such as Allicor taken twice daily for 24 months seems to reduce how much hardening of the arteries progresses. Diabetes: garlic may reduce pre-meal blood sugar levels in patients with or without diabetes. It works best in patients with diabetes, especially if it is taken for 3 or more months. Hypertension: garlic seems to reduce systolic blood pressure (top number) by about 7-9 points and diastolic blood pressure (bottom number) by about 4-6 ponts in patients with high blood pressure.The other three food items (walnut, ginger, turmeric) have only an anticoagulant effect but do not lower blood sugar levels. Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, pages 147, 187, 199",
      "exp_hant": "大蒜可作為降膽固醇藥物、抗凝血劑，並可能降低血漿葡萄糖濃度。抗凝血作用：大蒜中的硫化物（如蒜烯、大蒜素）能抑制血小板聚集並阻止血栓形成。動脈粥狀硬化：如 Allicor 等大蒜粉補充品，每日兩次連續服用24個月，似乎可減緩動脈硬化的進展。糖尿病：大蒜可能降低有無糖尿病患者的餐前血糖，對糖尿病患者效果最佳，尤其連續服用3個月以上時。高血壓：大蒜似乎可使高血壓患者的收縮壓（上壓）降低約7至9點，舒張壓（下壓）降低約4至6點。其餘三項食材（核桃、生薑、薑黃）僅具抗凝血作用，並無降血糖效果。Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, pages 147, 187, 199"
    },
    {
      "number": 723,
      "question_en": "A 79 year female patient comes to your office for the treatment of hypertension and early congestive heart failure. She is currently on Lasix plus Metoprolol from her doctor. What herb might be a problem for this patient because it is an aldosterone agonist?",
      "question_hant": "一位79歲女性患者至你的診所治療高血壓及早期充血性心衰竭。她目前由醫師處方服用Lasix及Metoprolol。何種中藥因具有醛固酮促效作用而可能對此患者造成問題？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "gan Cao (licorice)",
          "hant": "甘草",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "gui zhi (ramulus cinnamomi), gan jiang (rhizoma zingiberis officinalis)",
          "hant": "桂枝、乾薑",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "huang qi (radix astragalus)",
          "hant": "黃耆",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "fu ling (poria)",
          "hant": "茯苓",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Gan Cao (licorice) has known pseudoaldosterone effects, and can increase potassium loss, especially when co-administered with Loop diuretics such as Lasix that are also potassium depleting. Licorice specifically inhibits 11beta-hydroxysteroid dehyhydrogenase, that normally serves to protect local mineral-corticoid receptors from activation by cortisol via metabolism of the endogenous glucocorticoid locally into its inactive form. When this process is inhibited, the resulting excess cortisol stimulates the glucocorticoid and the unprotected renal mineral-corticoid receptors, promoting potassium loss. Left unchecked, this can lead to sodium retention and hypokalemia with possible hypertension, myopathy, arrhythmias, rhabdomyolysis and potential renal failure. These adverse event case studies are usually found in the public who are consuming licorice-containing candies to excess of 6-15g licorice daily. Patients prescribed potassium-depleting diuretics should be warned to avoid any licorice products except the DGL (Deglycyrrhizinated) form. Herb, Nutrient, and Drug Interactions: Clinical Implications and Therapeutic Strategies, Stargrove, Treasure, McKee, 2008, Page 115-121.",
      "exp_hant": "甘草已知具有類似醛固酮的作用，可能增加鉀離子流失，尤其當與同樣會導致鉀流失的環利尿劑（如Lasix）併用時更為明顯。甘草特異性抑制11β-羥類固醇去氫酶，此酶原本能保護局部礦皮質激素受體，使其不受皮質醇活化，其機轉為將內源性糖皮質激素在局部代謝為無活性形式。當此過程受到抑制時，過多的皮質醇會刺激糖皮質激素受體及未受保護的腎臟礦皮質激素受體，導致鉀流失。若未加以控制，可能導致鈉滯留及低血鉀，並伴隨高血壓、肌病、心律不整、橫紋肌溶解及潛在腎衰竭。此類不良事件案例通常見於每日食用超過6至15克含甘草糖果的一般民眾。建議服用排鉀性利尿劑的病患，除去甘草酸（DGL）形式的產品外，應避免使用任何甘草製品。Herb, Nutrient, and Drug Interactions: Clinical Implications and Therapeutic Strategies, Stargrove, Treasure, McKee, 2008, Page 115-121."
    },
