      "exp_en": "This class of drugs treat mainly depression. Tricyclic anti-depressants are posited to be acrid, windy, and qi-rectifying medicinals. The side effects of these western drugs can include blurred vision, dry-scratchy eyes, urinary retention, constipation, fatigue, somnolence, epilepsy, orthostatic hypotension, palpitations, tachycardia (rapid pulse), and weight gain. These side effects are explained by the patterns of qi vacuity or yin-Blood-fluid vacuity. The qi vacuity side effects include fatigue, somnolence, orthostatic hypotension, and lack of strength. As the Spleen is involved in qi formation, tricyclic anti-depressants can damage the Spleen resulting in weight gain. The yin-Blood-fluid vacuity side effects include blurry vision, dry-scratchy eyes, constipation, palpitations. Yin vacuity can fail to control the yang resulting in 1) heat vacuity (rapid pulse) or 2) internal Wind (epilepsy). Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 354",
      "exp_hant": "此類藥物主要用於治療憂鬱症。三環類抗憂鬱藥可被視為辛味、風性及理氣的藥性分類。此類西藥的副作用可能包括視力模糊、眼乾澀、尿滯留、便秘、疲倦、嗜睡、癲癇、姿勢性低血壓、心悸、心搏過速（脈快）及體重增加。這些副作用可以氣虛或陰血津液虛的證候加以解釋。氣虛的副作用包括疲倦、嗜睡、姿勢性低血壓及乏力。由於脾與氣的生成有關，三環類抗憂鬱藥可損傷脾臟，導致體重增加。陰血津液虛的副作用包括視力模糊、眼乾澀、便秘、心悸。陰虛不能制陽，可導致1）虛熱（脈快）或2）內風（癲癇）。Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 354"
