      "exp_en": "SSRIs drugs are used to treat depression, anxiety disorders (general anxiety, social anxiety, panic disorder), premenstrual dysphoric disorder, and OCD (obsessive-compulsive disorder). SSRIs are posited to be attacking and draining medicinals that rectify the qi that treat Liver depression and Spleen vacuity leading to the Heart not being nourished. As such they can also damage and consume the qi. The side effects of this class of western drugs include nausea, vomiting, headache, decreased sex drive, and inability or delayed ejaculation. These side effects indicate that they affect the Spleen and Stomach (nausea, vomiting) and the Spleen's relationship to the Kidneys (reduced libido, delayed ejaculation). Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 355",
