      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Drugs with the suffix -glitazone refer to drugs that treat diabetes. QUINOLONE (-floxacin) antibiotics such as ciprofloxacin (Cipro), levofloxacin, and moxifloxacin (Avelox) and TETRACYCLINE (-cycline) antibiotics such as doxycycline (Vibramycin) and minocycline (Minocin) have an interaction with dairy products (milk, cheese, yogurt, butter, ice cream). These antibiotics may bind to the calcium in milk, forming an insoluble substance in the stomach and upper small intestine that the body is unable to absorb. This can decrease the effectiveness of these drugs in treating an infection. The recommendation is to take quinolone and tetracycline drugs at least two hours before or two hours after eating or drinking dairy products. webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。字尾為 -glitazone 的藥物是指用於治療糖尿病的藥物。喹諾酮類（-floxacin）抗生素，如環丙沙星（Cipro）、左氧氟沙星及莫西沙星（Avelox），以及四環素類（-cycline）抗生素，如去氧羥四環素（Vibramycin）及米諾環素（Minocin），會與乳製品（牛奶、起司、優格、奶油、冰淇淋）產生交互作用。這些抗生素可能與牛奶中的鈣結合，在胃及小腸上段形成人體無法吸收的不溶性物質，進而降低這些藥物治療感染的效果。建議在服用喹諾酮類及四環素類藥物前後至少兩小時內，避免食用或飲用乳製品。webmd.com"
