      "exp_en": "Tian ma gou teng yin is a modern formula constructed to treat the western disease of hypertension. The formula treats hyperactive liver yang leading to the internal stirring of liver wind. In addition, the formula invigorates the blood and tonifies the liver and kidneys. This is the appropriate formula for this case. Ban xia bai zhu tian ma tang treats wind phlegm by strengthening the spleen and drying dampness while transforming phlegm and extinguishing wind. This patient's pattern revolves around the liver making this spleen centered formula inappropriate for this patient. Wen dan tang treats disharmony of the stomach and gallbladder with phlegm heat disrupting the qi dynamic. This is not the correct choice for the presentation of this patient. Gan mai da zao tang treats a condition called zang zao or restless organ syndrome. This syndrome typically manifests as an emotional disorder due to excessive worrying. This is not the correct formula for this patient at this time. Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs.647, 811, 786, 471.",
      "exp_hant": "天麻鉤藤飲是為治療西醫所稱高血壓病而創立的現代方劑。此方治療肝陽上亢導致內風妄動。此外，此方亦能活血並補益肝腎。此方適用於本病例。半夏白朮天麻湯治療風痰證，以健脾燥濕、化痰息風為法。此患者的證候以肝為核心，使得這個以脾為主的方劑並不適合此患者。溫膽湯治療胃膽不和兼痰熱擾亂氣機。此方並非此患者表現的正確選擇。甘麥大棗湯治療名為「臟躁」的病症。此病症通常表現為因過度憂思所致的情志失調病症。此方並非此時此患者的正確選擇。Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs.647, 811, 786, 471."
    },
    {
      "number": 739,
      "question_en": "A 37 year-old female returned from a trip to Italy with her boyfriend and reported having severe bouts of vertigo. They had gone on a foodie tour�� visiting several historical cities and indulging in their fine cuisine. She felt chest oppression and had significant nausea, particularly during the bouts of vertigo. She reported blowing her nose \"constantly\" and having copious amounts of thick and white phlegm. Her pulse was slippery and slightly wiry and her tongue had a greasy tongue coating. You prescribed the formula Ban Xia Bai Zhu Tian Ma Tang (Pinellia, White Atractylodes, and Gastrodia Decoction) for 2 days. She has returned after the two days and reports feeling better but not entirely better yet. She reported the warm sun being one of the only things that brought comfort for the two days during the attacks. She reported spending a significant time on the beach for the last two days where the sunny 90 degree weather \"felt good\". She reported that the vertigo bouts were coming less frequently, were not as severe, and were accompanied by a sensation of heat rushing to her head. She noticed that today, the sun did not feel as comfortable and that the sun bothered her vision in particular. Her tongue is now red and her pulse is slightly thin and wiry. She did not sleep well last night. What formula would you prescribe for her current condition?",
      "question_hant": "一位37歲女性與男友從義大利旅行返回後，主訴出現嚴重陣發性眩暈。他們進行了一趟美食之旅，走訪多個歷史古城並大快朵頤當地美食。她感到胸悶，並在眩暈發作時伴有明顯噁心感。她表示鼻塞「不停」流出大量濃稠白色鼻涕。脈滑略弦，舌苔膩。你開立半夏白朮天麻湯治療兩天。兩天後她回診，表示感覺好轉但尚未完全康復。她提到，這兩天發作期間，唯一能帶來舒緩的是溫暖的陽光。她表示過去兩天大部分時間都待在海灘，享受華氏90度（約攝氏32度）的晴朗天氣，感覺「很舒服」。她表示眩暈發作的頻率降低、程度減輕，且伴隨一股熱氣衝向頭部的感覺。她注意到今天陽光已不再讓她感到舒適，反而刺激視力。她的舌頭現在轉紅，脈略細而弦。她昨晚也睡得不好。你會為她目前的病情開立何方？",
