    {
      "number": 742,
      "question_en": "A 35 year-old male patient with no history of digestive problems presents with stomach pain for 3 days, since overeating meat. His pain is worse with pressure, and there is also abdominal distention. His bowel movements are foul-smelling and stickier than normal. His tongue is pale red with a yellow greasy fur. His herbalist prescribes the formula Bao He Wan (Preserve Harmony Pill) for his condition. Which of the following modifications is the most appropriate for this patient's current presentation?",
      "question_hant": "一位35歲男性患者素無消化系統病史，因暴食肉類後出現胃痛已三天。其疼痛按壓加劇，並伴有腹脹。大便氣味惡臭且較平常黏膩。舌淡紅苔黃膩。其中醫師為其開立保和丸治療此病情。針對此患者目前的表現，下列何項加減最為恰當？",
