    },
    {
      "number": 743,
      "question_en": "A 35 year-old male presents with severe intermittent hypochondriac pain for two months. The pain feels distending and pressured, and is worsened by his stress and depression. He also reports frequent sighing. His pulse is wiry and his tongue is dark with a thin white coating. The practitioner decides to modify the formula Chai Hu Shu Gan San (Bupleurum Powder to Spread the Liver) for this patient. Which of the following modifications would be most appropriate at this time?",
      "question_hant": "一位35歲男性因兩個月來反覆發作的嚴重脅痛前來就診。疼痛呈脹痛且有壓迫感，因壓力與情緒低落而加重。他也常有嘆氣的情形。脈弦，舌暗苔薄白。醫師決定加減柴胡疏肝散治療此患者。此時下列何項加減最為恰當？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Add Chuan Lian Zi (Melia Toosendan Fructus) and Yan Hu Suo (Corydalis Rhizoma)",
          "hant": "加川楝子、延胡索",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Add Zhi Zi (Gardeniae Fructus) and Suan Zao Ren (Ziziphi Spinosae Semen)",
          "hant": "加梔子、酸棗仁",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
