          "en": "Add Ban Xia (Pinelliae Rhizoma Preparatum) and Xuan Fu Hua (Inulae Flos)",
          "hant": "加半夏、旋覆花",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Delete Xiang Fu (Cyperi Rhizoma) and Chai Hu (Bupleuri Radix)",
          "hant": "去香附、柴胡",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The signs and symptoms of this case point to pronounced liver qi stagnation leading to severe pain likely through blood stasis evidenced through the dark tongue. To aid in the treatment of the liver qi stagnation, chuan lian zi is added which also stops pain. Furthermore, to move the blood and alleviate pain, yan hu suo is added which is an herb specifically used to alleviate blood stasis pain. Deleting xiang fu and chai hu takes out two of the herbs which are key in the treatment of liver qi stagnation which would not be beneficial in this case. Ban xia is not indicated in this case since there are no signs of phlegm-damp. Xuan fu hua is particularly good to remove phlegm in the lungs and subduing rebellious qi. This is not a necessary strategy in this case. Zhi zi removes heat and fire from the three burners and there is no evidence of heat in this case. Suan zao ren clears fire and nourishes the blood neither of which is necessary according to the signs and symptoms of this patient. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 512-513.",
      "exp_hant": "此病例的徵象顯示明顯的肝氣鬱結，導致嚴重疼痛，且舌暗提示可能兼有血瘀。為協助治療肝氣鬱結，加入川楝子，此藥亦能止痛。此外，為活血止痛，加入延胡索，此藥專用於緩解血瘀所致疼痛。去除香附與柴胡會移除治療肝氣鬱結的兩味關鍵藥物，這對本病例並無益處。此病例並無痰濕徵象，故不適用半夏。旋覆花特別擅長袪除肺中痰邪並降逆氣，此策略在本病例中並非必要。梔子能瀉三焦之熱與火，本病例並無熱象證據。酸棗仁清火養血，根據此患者的徵候皆非必要。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 512-513."
    },
    {
      "number": 744,
      "question_en": "A 59-year old female patient was prescribed Liu Wei Di Huang Wan (Six Ingredient Pill with Rehmannia) for her hot flashes and has been consistently taking the formula for six months. The hot flashes have not disappeared, but have reduced in both severity and frequency. She reports noticing that over the last two weeks she has developed Raynaud's disease, complaining of cold fingers and toes, feelings of irritability, and fullness of the chest. Her tongue is red with a slightly yellow coat and her pulse is wiry. Which formula is indicated?",
      "question_hant": "一位59歲女性患者因潮熱被開立六味地黃丸治療，並持續服用此方六個月。潮熱雖未消失，但嚴重程度與發作頻率皆已減輕。她表示過去兩週注意到自己出現雷諾氏症，主訴手指與腳趾冰冷、易怒感及胸悶。舌紅苔微黃，脈弦。此時應選用何方？",
