      "exp_en": "Taking liu wei di huang wan to treat deficiency heat not due to lack of kidney water can sometimes lead to an alleviation of symptoms, but side effects such as qi stagnation. In this patient's case, liver qi stagnation has led to the development of Raynaud's frigid extremities and si ni san is the correct formula. Si ni tang treats frigid extremities due to kidney yang deficiency which is not this case. Xiao chai hu tang treats shao yang syndrome. Many of the symptoms that are in this case are possible in a shao yang pattern but there is no clear history of an external contraction nor are there any alternating fever and chills. Xiao yao san treats liver qi stagnation and blood deficiency. Although this formula may work to alleviate some of the symptoms associated with this case, there is no clear blood deficiency and this formula is not the best choice with si ni san being a better option. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 274-277; 116-120; 104-109; 120-123",
      "exp_hant": "以六味地黃丸治療並非因腎水不足所致的虛熱，有時可使症狀緩解，但也可能產生氣滯等副作用。就本病例而言，肝氣鬱結導致雷諾氏症的四肢厥冷發展，四逆散為正確之方。四逆湯治療腎陽虛所致的四肢厥冷，並非本病例的情況。小柴胡湯治療少陽病證。本病例中的許多症狀在少陽證中皆有可能出現，但並無明確的外感病史，也無寒熱往來的表現。逍遙散治療肝氣鬱結兼血虛。雖然此方或可緩解本病例的部分症狀，但並無明確的血虛證據，相較之下四逆散為更佳選擇。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 274-277; 116-120; 104-109; 120-123"
    },
    {
      "number": 745,
      "question_en": "Two weeks ago, a pregnant patient of yours reportedly went to another herbalist while out of town and was mistakenly prescribed Yin Qiao San (Honeysuckle and Forsythia Powder) for her sore throat. Her throat has gotten worse and in addition she has had an abrupt onset of edema, beginning with the eyelids and face and gradually spreading to the limbs and entire body. She is 20-years-old. She also had sensitivity to drafts, fever, heavy aching limbs, difficult urination, and a sore, red, swollen throat. Her tongue is red and pulse is rapid, slippery, and floating. Which is the correct prescription for this condition?",
      "question_hant": "兩週前，你的一位孕期患者據稱在外地出差時，因喉嚨痛被另一位中醫師誤診並開立銀翹散治療。她的喉嚨症狀已惡化，此外她出現急性水腫，最初從眼瞼與面部開始，逐漸擴散至四肢及全身。她現年20歲。她同時有畏風、發熱、肢體沉重痠痛、排尿困難，以及喉嚨紅腫疼痛的症狀。舌紅，脈浮滑數。何者為此病情的正確處方？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "er chen tang (two cured decoction)",
          "hant": "二陳湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Zhen Wu Tang (True Warrior Decoction)",
          "hant": "真武湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "ma zi ren wan (hemp seed pill)",
          "hant": "麻子仁丸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Wu Pi San (Five Peel Powder)",
          "hant": "五皮散",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The incorrect prescribing of yin qiao san for what was likely an internally caused sore throat has caused a weakness at the exterior possibly by weakening the kidneys. This has allowed for the invasion of wind disrupting the lungs function leading to the edema. In this case and for this presentation, wu pi san is the correct choice. This formula resolves dampness and edema, regulates the qi and strengthens the spleen. This formula also is used in contemporary practice to treat edema during pregnancy. Zhen wu tang would likely be avoided due to the aconite in the prescription and the possible toxicity and complications to the pregnancy. Furthermore, this would be more appropriate if there were more kidney deficiency signs. The floating pulse indicates that this is an exterior wind invasion and the tonification of the kidneys would be a secondary strategy. Ma zi ren wan treats constipation due to dryness of the intestines. This is not appropriate for this patient at this time. Er chen tang treats dampness and strengthens the spleen but does not address the re-establishment of the lung qi dynamic through the usage of acrid dispersing herbs. Wu pi san is the better choice for this patient. Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs.732, 744, 81, 775",
      "exp_hant": "誤用銀翹散治療原本很可能是內因所致的喉嚨痛，導致表虛，可能因而損及腎氣。這使得風邪得以入侵並擾亂肺的功能，進而導致水腫。就此病情與表現而言，五皮散為正確之選。此方能利水消腫、理氣並健脾。此方在現代臨床上亦用於治療妊娠水腫。真武湯因方中含有附子，可能因其毒性及對妊娠可能造成的併發症而不宜使用。此外，若腎虛徵象更為明顯，此方會更為合適。浮脈顯示此為外感風邪，補腎則應為次要策略。麻子仁丸治療因腸燥所致的便秘，並不適用於此患者目前的狀況。二陳湯能祛濕健脾，但並未透過辛散藥物重建肺氣的運行功能。就此患者而言，五皮散為更佳選擇。Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs.732, 744, 81, 775"
    },
    {
      "number": 746,
      "question_en": "An 18 year-old comes to you to treat his cough which he claims to be getting better. Three weeks ago, he was diagnosed with bronchitis by his western physician and had a loud hacking cough that is now dry and can cause the spitting of blood occasionally. He has a history of bronchial asthma and has had some difficulty breathing. Additionally, he has suffered heat in the soles and palms and a cyclical fever that worsens throughout the day then sedates before rising again through the night. His pulse is weak, thin, and rapid. Which of the following would be the most appropriate modification of Mai Men Dong Tang (Ophiopogonis Decoction) for this patient's condition?",
      "question_hant": "一位18歲青少年前來就診，主訴咳嗽正逐漸好轉。三週前，他被西醫診斷為支氣管炎，當時咳嗽聲響劇烈，現已轉為乾咳，偶爾會咳出血絲。他有支氣管性氣喘病史，並曾出現呼吸困難。此外，他有手足心熱及日輕夜重、往復發作的週期性發熱。脈弱細而數。針對此患者的病情，下列何項對麥門冬湯的加減最為恰當？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Add chuan bei mu (bulbus fritillariae cirrhosae) and gua lou ren (semen trichosanthis)",
          "hant": "加川貝母、瓜蔞仁",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Remove ren shen (radix ginseng)",
          "hant": "去人參",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Add di gu pi (cortex lycii)",
          "hant": "加地骨皮",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Remove mai men dong (radix ophiopogonis) and add sheng di huang (radix rehmanniae)",
          "hant": "去麥門冬，加生地黃",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The formula mai men dong tang treats a condition called fei wei (lung atrophy) characterized by heat induced damage to the lungs and stomach. Primarily, damage to the stomach yin causes heat from deficiency to rise which damages the lungs to the extent in which it begins to atrophy over time. In this particular case, the patient is suffering from a cyclical tidal fever for which the formula is modified with di gu pi which clears deficiency heat. Chuan bei mu and gua lou ren are added to the formula in cases where there is a severe cough. In this case, the coughing is reportedly getting better. Removing ren shen does not make sense as it is one of the primary herbs in nourishing the fluids and tonifying the center which is the root cause of this condition. Mai men dong is an essential herb in this case as it targets nourishment of the fluids to the lungs and stomach while also being somewhat undervalued for its ability to clear heat. Sheng di huang nourishes the yin and clears heat in the kidneys and the current condition has not reached that level at this time. Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 670-672",
      "exp_hant": "麥門冬湯治療一種名為「肺痿」的病症，其特徵為熱邪損傷肺胃。主要是胃陰受損導致虛熱上炎，進而損傷肺臟，久之甚至造成肺臟萎縮。就本病例而言，患者出現週期性潮熱，故以地骨皮加減此方，用以清虛熱。川貝母與瓜蔞仁則用於咳嗽嚴重的情況下加入本方。本病例中患者的咳嗽據稱正在好轉。去除人參並不合理，因其為滋養津液並補益中焦的主藥之一，而這正是此病情的根本原因。麥門冬是此病例中不可或缺的藥物，因其能滋養肺胃之津，同時其清熱之效亦常被低估。生地黃能滋陰清腎熱，而目前的病情尚未發展到此程度。Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 670-672"
    },
    {
      "number": 747,
      "question_en": "A male patient complains of chronic low back pain that is worse with exertion and better with warmth and pressure, a cold sensation in the lower limbs and urinary difficulty with mild edema. His tongue is pale and swollen with a glossy coat, and his pulse is deep weak and slow. He is prescribed the formula Shen Qi Wan (Kidney Qi Pill). He later confesses that he also suffers from impotence which is a major concern. Which of the following modifications to the base formula is most appropriate at this time?",
      "question_hant": "一位男性患者主訴慢性腰痛，勞累加重、溫按則減，下肢有寒冷感，並有排尿困難兼輕度水腫。舌淡胖有滑苔，脈沉弱而遲。醫師為其開立腎氣丸治療。他後來坦承自己也患有陽痿，這是他相當在意的問題。此時對基礎方的何種加減最為恰當？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Keep Shen Qi Wan (Kidney Qi Pill) as is",
          "hant": "維持原方腎氣丸不變",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Switch the formula to Xiao Huo Luo Dan (Minor Invigorate the Collaterals Pill)",
          "hant": "改用小活絡丹",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Remove ze xie (rhizome alismatis) and add wu wei zi (fructus schisandrae)",
          "hant": "去澤瀉，加五味子",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Add ba ji tian (radix morindae), rou cong rong (herba cistanches), suo yang (herba cynomorii), and gou qi zi (fructus lycii)",
          "hant": "加巴戟天、肉蓯蓉、鎖陽、枸杞子",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Xiao huo luo dan is a formula that treats windstroke and removes obstruction of the channels due to wind-cold-damp, blood stasis, and phlegm. Removing ze xie and adding wu wei zi to the base formula are for cases where there is incontinence or turbid urine from overuse of bitter and cold herbs. Ba ji tian is correct because of its ability to tonify the kidneys and strengthen the yang (specifically for issues like impotence). Similarly, rou cong rong tonifies the kidneys, yang, and benefits the essence which helps to treat a condition like impotence while addressing the core pattern of kidney deficiency. Suo yang is also a kidney yang tonic which benefits the essence, marrow, and blood and can be of benefit to kidney yang deficiency impotence. Lastly, gou qi zi addresses the yin and blood aspect of impotence through its nourishing function and also benefits the essence. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 395-400.",
      "exp_hant": "小活絡丹用於治療中風，並袪除風寒濕、血瘀及痰邪所致的經絡阻滯。去除澤瀉並加入五味子適用於因過用苦寒藥物所致的尿失禁或尿濁的情況。巴戟天正確之處在於其能補腎壯陽（特別針對陽痿等問題）。同樣地，肉蓯蓉能補腎壯陽並益精，有助於治療陽痿此類病症，同時針對腎虛的根本證候。鎖陽亦為補腎陽之藥，能益精、髓、血，對腎陽虛所致陽痿有益。最後，枸杞子透過其滋養功能針對陽痿的陰血層面，亦能益精。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 395-400."
    },
    {
      "number": 748,
      "question_en": "A 34 year-old female seeks treatment from you because she has palpitations and a feeling of oppression in her chest. Through your interview and examination, you discover that she has mental restlessness, insomnia, dream disturbed sleep, a propensity to be startled, poor memory, anxiety, \"uneasiness\", malar flush, night sweating, and a dry mouth and throat. Her tongue is red with no coating with a crack down the middle, and her pulse is thready and rapid. You prescribe the formula Tian Wang Bu Xin Dan (Emperor of Heaven's Special Pill to Tonify the Heart). She calls you the next day and says that last night she could not sleep at all and her skin feels warm to the touch which is unusual for her. You decide to modify her original prescription with:",
      "question_hant": "一位34歲女性因心悸及胸悶前來就診。透過問診與檢查，你發現她有精神煩躁、失眠、多夢易醒、易受驚、健忘、焦慮、「不安」感、顴紅、盜汗，以及口乾咽燥。舌紅無苔且舌中有裂紋，脈細數。你開立天王補心丹治療。隔天她致電表示昨晚完全無法入睡，且皮膚摸起來發熱，這對她而言是不尋常的情形。你決定如何調整她原本的處方？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Add the herb Ci Shi (magnetitum)",
          "hant": "加磁石",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Remove ren shen (radix ginseng)",
          "hant": "去人參",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Remove Sheng Di Huang (radix rehmanniae) and add Gui Zhi (ramulus cinnamomi)",
          "hant": "去生地黃，加桂枝",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Add Chuan Xiong (rhizoma chuanxiong) and Bai Zhi (radix angelicae dahuricae)",
          "hant": "加川芎、白芷",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This patient suffers from a yin and blood deficiency leading to restlessness and mental unease. The yin deficiency leads the heart shen to become unstable in its position within the heart blood. As it rises, sleep is difficult and the lack of controlled burning of the heart fire causes disturbed sleep. To anchor the yang away from the surface causing the skin warmth and the shen back into the heart blood, the anchoring herb ci shi is added. One can also combine ci shi with the herb long chi These herbs will also clear any present heat due to yin deficiency. Removing sheng di huang is not a good idea as this is the chief herb responsible for nourishing the yin and clearing heat. These are the two main actions of the formula from a physiological perspective. Adding gui zhi will lead the yang back out towards the surface and add heat to a yin deficient system. Chuan xiong and bai zhi are added to the formula in instances where there is dizziness and vertigo for their abilities to regulate the blood and expel wind. Ren shen appears in the formula to assist the heart qi which is an important aspect of the formula. Removing this would leave this task up to fu ling which may be too much for the single herb. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 459-461.",
      "exp_hant": "此患者屬陰血兩虛導致精神不寧、心神不安。陰虛使心神在心血中無法安定其位。心神上擾則難以入眠，而心火失於制約則導致睡眠不安穩。為將浮越於外之陽氣（造成皮膚發熱）及心神引回心血之中，加入具有潛鎮作用的磁石。磁石亦可與龍齒合用。這些藥物亦能清除因陰虛所生之熱。去除生地黃並非良策，因其為滋陰清熱的主藥，這正是本方從生理角度而言的兩大主要作用。加入桂枝會將陽氣引回體表，並對本已陰虛之體增添熱象。川芎與白芷則於出現頭暈目眩時加入本方，取其活血袪風之效。人參於方中用以扶助心氣，這是本方重要的一環。若將其去除，此重任將全落於茯苓一味身上，恐難以獨力承擔。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 459-461."
    },
    {
      "number": 749,
      "question_en": "A 40 year-old female presents with an acute onset of fever last night, aversion to cold, headache, nausea and vomiting, diarrhea, heaviness in the body, and a stifling sensation in her chest. Her tongue has a white greasy coat and her pulse is floating and slippery. You decide to prescribe the formula Huo Xiang Zheng Qi San (Agastache Powder to Rectify the Qi). Before she leaves, she suddenly remembers and reports that she has also been suffering from brief and scanty urination that has a slight burning feeling. How would you modify your original prescription in light of this new information?",
      "question_hant": "一位40歲女性主訴昨夜突然發熱、惡寒、頭痛、噁心嘔吐、腹瀉、身體沉重感，以及胸悶感。舌苔白膩，脈浮滑。你決定開立藿香正氣散治療。在她離開前，她突然想起並告知你，她也一直有小便短少且略有灼熱感的情形。根據這項新資訊，你會如何調整原本的處方？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Add Mu Xiang (radix auklandiae) and Yan Hu Suo (rhizome corydalis)",
          "hant": "加木香、延胡索",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Add Mu Tong (caulis akebiae) and Ze Xie (rhizome alismatis)",
          "hant": "加木通、澤瀉",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "The original prescription is the best treatment of this condition and does not need modification",
          "hant": "原方即為此病情的最佳治療，無須調整",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Add Cang Zhu (rhizoma attractylodis) and Bai Zhu (rhizoma attractylodis macrocephalae)",
          "hant": "加蒼朮、白朮",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "For brief and scanty urination, mu tong is added for its ability to promote urination and bitterness which can dry dampness. Ze xie is added for its bland draining of dampness. In this case stagnation has occurred in the lower jiao which has begun to depress into heat and block the urination. These two herbs are cooling to offset the heat in this condition. Cang zhu and bai zhu would be added to the original prescription in cases where there is severe dampness. In these cases there would be a very thick and greasy tongue coat. Mu xiang and yan hu suo would be added in cases where there is pronounced qi stagnation with abdominal distention and pain. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 691-694.",
      "exp_hant": "針對小便短少，加入木通以利尿，其苦味亦能燥濕。加入澤瀉以淡滲利濕。此病例中，鬱滯已於下焦形成，並開始化熱阻礙排尿。此二藥性寒，可用以抵銷此病情中的熱象。蒼朮與白朮則於原處方中濕邪嚴重時加入，此類情況下舌苔會非常厚膩。木香與延胡索則於氣滯明顯、伴有腹脹腹痛時加入。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 691-694."
    },
    {
      "number": 750,
      "question_en": "A 62 year-old woman presents with constipation for six months. She reports difficult bowel movements that are dry and hard, along with frequent, clear, and pale urination. She also reports low back pain that is better with warmth and pressure and prefers warm environments and beverages. Her pulse is slow, deep and weak, and her tongue is pale with a thin white coat. The herbalist decides to prescribe a modification of the formula Fu Zi Li Zhong Wan (Prepared Aconite Pill to Regulate the Middle) for this patient. How well does this prescription match the patient's presentation?",
      "question_hant": "一位62歲女性因便秘六個月前來就診。她表示排便困難，大便乾硬，並伴有頻尿、尿清而量多。她也主訴腰痛，溫按則減，並偏好溫暖的環境與飲品。脈遲沉弱，舌淡苔薄白。醫師決定以附子理中丸的加減方治療此患者。此處方與患者的表現相符程度為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "It matches the patient's presentation and is the correct prescription at this time.",
          "hant": "此方與病情相符，為此時的正確處方",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Si Shen Wan (Four-Miracle Pill) matches the patient's presentation more accurately.",
          "hant": "四神丸與此患者的表現更為相符",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Ji Chuan Jian (Benefit the River Flow Decoction) matches the patient's presentation more accurately.",
          "hant": "濟川煎與此患者的表現更為相符",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Jin Gui Shen Qi Wan (Kidney Qi Pill from the Golden Cabinet) matches the patient's presentation more accurately.",
          "hant": "金匱腎氣丸與此患者的表現更為相符",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Firstly, a clue as to the appropriate formula is the combination of the chief complaint (constipation) and the patient's age (62). Constitutionally, as we age into the senior age range the body's resources are in decline. Constipation is common due to the decline of the kidney energies. As we see the symptoms of dry stools with copious urination and empty cold low back pain, kidney yang deficiency seems the logical pattern for this patient. Fu zi li zhong wan treats yang and spleen deficiency with abdominal pain due to cold. This formula is not indicated for kidney deficiency constipation. Ji chuan jian is the formula typically described for kidney deficiency constipation and is a common prescription for the senior population who suffer from constipation due to kidney deficiency. Jin gui shen qi wan is for kidney yang deficiency but where ji chuan jian also employs the strategy of moistening the intestines with dang gui and moving the qi with zhi ke, shen qi wan does not. Si shen wan is indicated for spleen and kidney yang deficiency cock's crow diarrhea by binding the intestines and tonifying the kidneys and spleen. This binding action would be inappropriate in this case of constipation. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 261, 84-85, 395-400, 429-431.",
      "exp_hant": "首先，判斷適當處方的線索在於主訴（便秘）與患者年齡（62歲）的結合。從體質角度而言，隨著邁入老年階段，人體資源逐漸衰退。便秘常因腎氣衰退所致。由於出現大便乾燥兼小便清長，以及虛寒腰痛的症狀，腎陽虛似乎是此患者的合理證候。附子理中丸治療脾陽虛兼寒邪所致腹痛。此方並不適用於腎虛便秘。濟川煎則是專為腎虛便秘所設之方，是老年族群因腎虛所致便秘的常用處方。金匱腎氣丸適用於腎陽虛，但濟川煎另以當歸潤腸、枳殼理氣，而腎氣丸則無此配伍。四神丸適用於脾腎陽虛所致五更瀉，透過澀腸與補益腎脾來治療。此收澀作用在本病例便秘的情況下並不適合。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 261, 84-85, 395-400, 429-431."
    },
    {
      "number": 751,
      "question_en": "A 37-year-old man arrives at your office with a main complaint of seminal emission not related to sexual activity. He suffers from frequent and spontaneous seminal discharge accompanied by cold extremities, an achy low back and knees, a receding hairline, and thinning head hair. His tongue is pale with toothmarks and excess saliva. His pulse is deep and weak. You prescribe Jin Suo Gu Jing Wan (Metal Lock Pill to Stabilize the Essence) for his condition. After three weeks on the formula, the spontaneous seminal emission resolves. The patient reports persistence of the accompanying symptoms, however, and his tongue and pulse have not changed. How would you modify the treatment given this development?",
      "question_hant": "一位37歲男性至你的診所就診，主訴與性行為無關的遺精。他有頻繁且自發性的遺精，伴有四肢冰冷、腰膝痠痛、髮際線後退及頭髮稀疏。舌淡有齒痕且口水過多。脈沉弱。你為其開立金鎖固精丸治療。服用此方三週後，自發性遺精獲得改善。然而患者表示伴隨症狀仍持續存在，且其舌象與脈象均未改變。針對此情況，你會如何調整治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Replace the original formula with Si Shen Wan (Four-Miracle Pill).",
          "hant": "改用四神丸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Replace the original formula with Zuo Jin Wan (Left Metal Pill).",
          "hant": "改用左金丸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Replace the original formula with Bu Zhong Yi Qi Tang (Tonify the Middle and Augment the Qi Decoction).",
          "hant": "改用補中益氣湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Replace the original formula with You Gui Wan (Restore the Right (Kidney) Pill).",
          "hant": "改用右歸丸",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This condition is known in Chinese Medicine as yi jing (seminal emission). The initial pattern symptom complex was one of Kidney yang deficiency with failure to seal and store. Jin Suo Gu Jing W a n (Metal Lock Pill to Stabilize the Essence) is an astringent formula that consolidates the Kidneys and stops seminal emission, acting to supplement Kidney yang and secure essence. It focuses on the branch symptom rather than the Kidney yang and qi deficiency at the root. As such, it should be combined with a tonic formula in chronic conditions or replaced by a tonic formula once the branch symptom of seminal emission has subsided. Upon the patient's return, the original main complaint has resolved but the pattern symptom complex still reflects the presence of Kidney yang deficiency. You Gui Wan (Restore the Right (Kidney) Pill) is a strong Kidney yang tonic, acting to warm and tonify Kidney yang. This will also help prevent recurrence of the branch symptom of spontaneous seminal emission. Zuo Jin Wan (Left Metal Pill) Clears Liver Heat, Descends Rebellious and stops vomiting. It is indicated for patterns of Liver Qi Stagnation, Liver Qi Invading the Stomach, Heat in the Liver Channel with Stomach Disharmony and Excess Fire in the Liver Channel with Heat in Stomach. It is contraindicated with acid regurgitation due to Stomach Deficiency Cold, hypochondriac pain due to Liver, Gallbladder or Blood Deficiencies. It is contraindicated during pregnancy. The pulse is wiry-rapid and the tongue is red with yellow coating. Si Shen Wan (Four-Miracle Pill) is indicated for Kidney yang deficiency causing diarrhea, usually occurring with urgency at dawn. Its focus is on securing the sealing and storing of stool, specifically. Diarrhea is not present in the case of this patient, and the focus should be on warming and tonifying the root deficiency now that the essence has been consolidated and there is no abnormal discharge. Bu Zhong Yi Qi Tang (Tonify the Middle and Augment the Qi Decoction) is indicated in cases of seminal emission due to qi deficiency with a failure to astringe the essence. In such cases, we would expect signs of qi deficiency but fewer or no cold signs. We would also expect seminal emission to be worse following overwork, accompanied by loose stools, fatigue, loss of appetite, a pale tongue, and a weak pulse. Bu Zhong Yi Qi Tang (Tonify the Middle and Augment the Qi Decoction) would not sufficiently tonify yang or warm the Kidneys in this patient's presentation. Scheid, Volker, Dan Bensky, Andrew Ellis, and Randall Barolet. Chinese Herbal Medicine: Formulas and Strategies. 2nd ed. Seattle, WA: Eastland Press, 2009; Wu, Yan, and Warren Fischer. Practical Therapeutics of Traditional Chinese Medicine. Ed. Jake P. Fratkin. Brookline, MA: Paradigm Publications, 1997, pp. 197-201.",
      "exp_hant": "此病症在中醫稱為遺精。最初的證候組合為腎陽虛，封藏失職。金鎖固精丸是一種澀劑方，能固腎止遺精，並具有補腎陽、固精的作用。此方針對的是標證，而非腎陽與腎氣虛的本證。因此，在慢性病情中應與補益方併用，或於遺精此一標證消退後改用補益方。患者回診時，主訴已解除，但證候組合仍反映腎陽虛的存在。右歸丸是強效的補腎陽方，能溫補腎陽，亦有助於預防自發性遺精此一標證的復發。左金丸能清肝熱、降逆止嘔，適用於肝氣鬱結、肝氣犯胃、肝經有熱兼胃失和降，以及肝經實火兼胃熱等證候。此方禁用於胃虛寒所致泛酸，以及肝、膽或血虛所致脅痛。此方於懷孕期間禁用。其脈弦數，舌紅苔黃。四神丸適用於腎陽虛所致腹瀉，通常於清晨急迫發作。其重點在於固澀大便，此為其特定功用。本病例並無腹瀉，且此時精已固攝、無異常遺洩，治療重點應轉為溫補根本之虛。補中益氣湯適用於氣虛不能固攝精氣所致的遺精。此類情況下，應可見氣虛徵象，但寒象較少或無。遺精亦應因勞累而加重，並伴有大便溏薄、疲倦、食慾不振、舌淡及脈弱。就本患者的表現而言，補中益氣湯不足以溫補腎陽或溫腎。Scheid, Volker, Dan Bensky, Andrew Ellis, and Randall Barolet. Chinese Herbal Medicine: Formulas and Strategies. 2nd ed. Seattle, WA: Eastland Press, 2009; Wu, Yan, and Warren Fischer. Practical Therapeutics of Traditional Chinese Medicine. Ed. Jake P. Fratkin. Brookline, MA: Paradigm Publications, 1997, pp. 197-201."
    },
    {
      "number": 752,
      "question_en": "A 67 year-old male presents with dizziness for over six months. He says that the dizziness can get intense at times. He also reports a sore and weak low back and knees, forgetfulness, and difficulty sleeping. He denies feeling warmer at night or night sweats. His pulse is thin, rapid and wiry and his tongue is red with no coating. The herbalist decides to modify the formula Zuo Gui Wan (Restore the Left [Kidney] Pill) for this patient. Which of the following modifications would be most appropriate at this time?",
      "question_hant": "一位67歲男性主訴頭暈已超過六個月。他表示頭暈有時會相當劇烈。他也主訴腰膝痠軟無力、健忘及睡眠困難。他否認夜間發熱或盜汗。脈細數而弦，舌紅無苔。醫師決定以左歸丸的加減方治療此患者。此時下列何項加減最為恰當？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Add Ba Ji Tian (Morindae Officinalis Radix) and Yin Yang Huo (Epimedii Herba)",
          "hant": "加巴戟天、淫羊藿",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Delete Shu Di Huang (Rehmanniae Radix Preparata) and Shan Zhu Yu (Corni Fructus)",
          "hant": "去熟地黃、山茱萸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Add Zhi Mu (Anemarrhenae Rhizoma) and Huang Bai (Phellodendri Cortex)",
          "hant": "加知母、黃柏",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Add Long Gu (Fossilia Ossis Mastodi) and Mu Li (Ostreae Concha)",
          "hant": "加龍骨、牡蠣",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The base formula is one of the major prescriptions from Zhang Jie-Bin which focuses on warm tonification. Specifically, this formula nourishes the kidney yin, marrow, and essence. Along with the patient's age, the symptoms of soreness in the low back and knees, forgetfulness, and difficulty sleeping suggests that the kidney yin is weak. This is supported by the thin and rapid pulse and lack of coating on the tongue. Long gu and mu li are used together to help suppress rising yang. Since there is an underlying yin deficiency condition with a chief complaint of dizziness, the yang rising is the cause of the dizziness which will be helped using this combination. Zhi mu and huang bai are both bitter and although zhi mu does nourish the yin, it may be too drying for this condition. Also, both of these herbs are directed at the lower jiao and are cold so this may not benefit an already weak kidney yin. Ba ji tian and yin yang huo both tonify the kidney yang and thereby aid the fire in the body which can further damage the kidney yin. Shu di huang and shan zhu yu are important in their ability to nourish and astringe the kidney yin respectively. These herbs are necessary in the strategy of nourishing the kidney yin as can be seen by their inclusion in both this formula and liu wei di huang wan. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 370-372.",
      "exp_hant": "此基礎方為張景岳所創的重要方劑之一，著重於溫補滋養。此方特別滋養腎陰、填精補髓。結合患者的年齡，加上腰膝痠軟、健忘及睡眠困難等症狀，顯示腎陰虛弱。脈細數且舌無苔亦支持此判斷。龍骨與牡蠣合用有助於平抑上亢之陽。由於存在潛在的陰虛證候，主訴為頭暈，陽氣上亢即為頭暈之因，此配伍將有助於改善。知母與黃柏皆屬苦寒之藥，雖然知母能滋陰，但對此證候而言可能過於燥烈。此外，此二藥皆偏於下焦且性寒，對於本已虛弱的腎陰可能無益。巴戟天與淫羊藿皆能補腎陽，因而助長體內之火，可能進一步損傷腎陰。熟地黃與山茱萸的重要性在於分別滋養與固澀腎陰。此二藥為滋養腎陰策略中不可或缺者，可見於本方及六味地黃丸中皆有納入。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 370-372."
    },
    {
      "number": 753,
      "question_en": "Gary, 35, has been feeling feverish for the past three weeks. His pulse is large and deficient, and his complexion is pale and shiny. Which of the following formulas would be the most appropriate for his condition?",
      "question_hant": "Gary，35歲，過去三週感到發熱。脈大而虛，面色蒼白且帶光澤。下列何方最適合他目前的病情？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "bai hu tang (white tiger decoction)",
          "hant": "白虎湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "liu wei di huang wan (six-ingredient pill with rehmannia)",
          "hant": "六味地黃丸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "bu zhong yi qi tang (tonify the qi to augment the middle decoction)",
          "hant": "補中益氣湯",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "si jun zi tang (four gentlemen decoction)",
          "hant": "四君子湯",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "From the few indications given above, we can surmise that the feverishness is caused by qi deficiency, perhaps due to his long fight against some chronic infection. His pale and shiny complexion reflects internal deficiency with an external excess. The large but deficient pulse indicates the upward and outward movement of yang that deficient qi cannot contain. This is one of the patterns treatable with bu zhong yi qi tang. Although si jun zi tang also treats Qi deficiency, its focus is on the transporting and transforming functions of the Spleen. In such a case, the pulse would be frail and the complexion would be pale but wan. It would be more appropriate for cases of Spleen qi deficiency with spontaneous sweating rather than feverishness. The formula bai hu tang treats fevers due to Qi-level heat rather than qi deficiency. The hallmark indications are the four bigs: high fever, severe thirst, a flooding forceful pulse, and profuse sweating. In such a case, the complexion would be red rather than pale. The formula liu wei di huang wan treats tidal fever due to yin deficiency. Again, because of the heat, the complexion would likely be red rather than pale, and the pulse would be thready and rapid. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 151, 310, 321, and 365",
      "exp_hant": "從上述有限的資訊可推知，此發熱是由氣虛所致，或許是因長期對抗某種慢性感染所引起。他蒼白帶光澤的面色反映內虛兼外現之假象。脈大而虛則顯示虛弱之氣無法收攝，導致陽氣上浮外越。此為補中益氣湯所治之證候之一。雖然四君子湯亦治氣虛，但其重點在於脾的運化功能。此類情況下脈象應為濡弱，面色蒼白但無光澤。此方更適用於脾氣虛兼自汗的病例，而非發熱的病例。白虎湯治療氣分熱所致之發熱，而非氣虛。其特徵為四大症狀：高熱、劇渴、洪大有力之脈，以及大汗。此類情況下，面色應為紅赤而非蒼白。六味地黃丸治療陰虛所致之潮熱。同樣因為有熱象，面色可能偏紅而非蒼白，脈象則應細數。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 151, 310, 321, and 365"
    },
    {
      "number": 754,
      "question_en": "A male student has been taking high doses of Gui Pi Tang (Restore the Spleen Decoction) for six weeks to get him through a particularly difficult semester and now complains of hypochondriac fullness, abdominal cramps, and alternating chills and fever. He also describes feeling depressed, fidgety, and having sexual dysfunction. What formula is indicated for this patient?",
      "question_hant": "一位男大學生為熬過特別艱難的一學期，連續六週服用高劑量的歸脾湯，現主訴脅肋脹滿、腹部絞痛，以及寒熱往來。他也表示感到憂鬱、坐立不安，並有性功能障礙。此患者應選用何方？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "xue fu zhu yu tang (drive out stasis from the mansion of blood decoction)",
          "hant": "血府逐瘀湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "yue ju wan (escape restraint pill)",
          "hant": "越鞠丸",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "si ni san (frigid extremities powder)",
          "hant": "四逆散",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Chai Hu Shu Gan San (Bupleurum Powder to Dredge the Liver)",
          "hant": "柴胡疏肝散",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Gui pi tang can be quite cloying with ingredients like long yan rou and over time this can cause stagnation of qi, especially when the digestion is poor. The patient's current presentation of alternating fever and chills, depression, abdominal cramps, and hypochondriac fullness fit the formula chai hu shu gan san. Although the pattern involves liver qi stagnation, si ni san treats the complication of the pattern of frigid (cold) extremities which the patient is not currently suffering from. Yue ju wan treats the six stagnations and classic liver qi stagnation. This formula could be used to treat this pattern but is not the best choice. Xue fu zhu yu tang treats blood stasis in the chest and liver qi stagnation. There is no clear evidence of blood stasis in this patient's presentation. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 512-513; 116-120; 507-510; 564-567",
      "exp_hant": "歸脾湯中含有龍眼肉等滋膩之品，久服且消化功能不佳時，可能導致氣機鬱滯。此患者目前表現的寒熱往來、憂鬱、腹部絞痛及脅肋脹滿，符合柴胡疏肝散的方證。雖然此證候涉及肝氣鬱結，但四逆散所治為此證候併發四肢厥冷的情況，而此患者目前並無此症狀。越鞠丸治療六鬱及典型的肝氣鬱結。此方雖可用於治療此證候，但並非最佳選擇。血府逐瘀湯治療胸中血瘀兼肝氣鬱結。此患者的表現並無明確的血瘀證據。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 512-513; 116-120; 507-510; 564-567"
    },
    {
      "number": 755,
      "question_en": "A 25 year-old female patient comes to you for treatment of hyperhidrosis which has developed over the last few weeks. She has been run down from a very important work deadline and has not eaten or slept well for the last two months. Her pulse is thin and weak and she has a pale face with a white tinge. Her tongue is pale and she also complains of a light headache. You notice that she is wearing hand warmers and thick socks on a slightly breezy spring day (66 degrees and mostly sunny) and has dressed in layers. How would you modify the formula Shi Quan Da Bu Tang (All-Inclusive Great Tonifying Decoction) for this patient's current condition?",
      "question_hant": "一位25歲女性患者因近幾週出現的多汗症前來就診。她因一項重要的工作截止期限而身心俱疲，過去兩個月飲食與睡眠皆不佳。脈細弱，面色蒼白帶白色調。舌淡，並主訴輕微頭痛。你注意到她在微風徐徐的春日（華氏66度，約攝氏19度，大致晴朗）戴著手套、穿著厚襪並層層疊穿衣物。針對此患者目前的病情，你會如何加減十全大補湯？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Remove rou gui (contex cinnamomi) and huang qi (radix astragali)",
          "hant": "去肉桂、黃耆",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Remove ren shen (radix ginseng) and shu di huang (radix rehmanniae preparata)",
          "hant": "去人參、熟地黃",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Add mu li (concha ostreae) and long gu (fossilia ossis mostodi)",
          "hant": "加牡蠣、龍骨",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Add suan zao ren (semesn ziziphi spinosae) and wu wei zi (fructus schisandrae)",
          "hant": "加酸棗仁、五味子",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The formula shi quan da bu tang treats a dual deficiency of the blood and qi were the patient also suffers from cold from predominant qi deficiency. The complication in this case is the excessive sweating. For this, the herbs mu li and long gu are added to astringe the sweat and anchor the deficient floating yang rising to the surface causing the sweating. Rou gui and huang qi are added to ba zhen tang to create this formula in instances where there are evident cold signs. Due to the covering of her hands and feet and layered clothing during temperate weather, the patient is exhibiting signs that cold has manifested from her deficiency. These herbs should remain in the formula. Suan zao ren and wu wei zi are added to the formula when there are palpitations complicating the condition and none have been reported at this time. Removing ren shen and shu di huang does not make sense as these are the chief herbs of the two constituent formulas si jun zi tang and si wu tang and are the primary tonifiers of the qi and blood deficiency respectively. Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 348-350",
      "exp_hant": "十全大補湯治療氣血兩虛，患者兼有因氣虛偏盛所致之寒象。本病例的併發症在於過度出汗。針對此症，加入牡蠣與龍骨，以斂汗並潛鎮因虛而上浮外越之陽氣，此為汗出之因。肉桂與黃耆是在八珍湯的基礎上加入，形成本方，適用於寒象明顯的情況。由於她手足包覆保暖、於溫和天氣中層層疊衣，此患者正顯示出因虛而生寒的徵象。這些藥物應予保留於方中。酸棗仁與五味子則於併發心悸時加入本方，而本病例目前並未提及此症狀。去除人參與熟地黃並不合理，因二者分別為四君子湯與四物湯這兩個組成方的君藥，亦是補益氣虛與血虛的主要藥物。Formulas and Strategies 2nd Edition, Bensky, 2009, pages 348-350"
    },
    {
      "number": 756,
      "question_en": "A 42 year-old female presents with headaches for the last six months. She reports her headaches being throbbing in nature and accompanied by dizziness. Overall, she reports irritability, restless sleep and a bitter taste in her mouth. Her pulse is wiry and her tongue is red with a thin yellow coat. The practitioner decides to prescribe the formula Xue Fu Zhu Yu Tang (Drive Out Stasis from the Mansion of Blood Decoction) for this patient. How well does this prescription match the patient's presentation?",
      "question_hant": "一位42歲女性主訴頭痛已持續六個月。她表示頭痛性質為跳痛，並伴隨頭暈。整體而言，她表示易怒、睡眠不安穩及口苦。脈弦，舌紅苔薄黃。醫師決定為此患者開立血府逐瘀湯治療。此處方與患者的表現相符程度為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Zhi Bai Di Huang Wan (Anemarrhena, Phellodendron and Rehmannia Pill) matches the patient's presentation more accurately.",
          "hant": "知柏地黃丸與此患者的表現更為相符",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "It matches the patient's presentation and is the correct prescription at this time.",
          "hant": "此方與病情相符，為此時的正確處方",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Tian Ma Gou Teng Yin (Gastrodia and Uncaria Drink) matches the patient's presentation more accurately.",
          "hant": "天麻鉤藤飲與此患者的表現更為相符",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Xiao Yao San (Rambling Powder) matches the patient's presentation more accurately.",
          "hant": "逍遙散與此患者的表現更為相符",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Xue fu zhu yu tang is not the correct prescription at this time due to it being a formula which moves blood for blood stasis symptoms. This patient clearly has liver qi stagnation with depressed heat and internal wind. The formula which addresses these patterns is tian ma gou teng yin. Interestingly enough, this formula was created in the mid 20th century as a treatment for the western diseases of hypertension related headaches. The formula calms the liver, extinguishes wind, and clears heat. Zhi bai di huang wan clears heat while nourishing the kidney yin. This condition is excess and a base formula of liu wei di huang wan is not appropriate for this case. Xiao yao san does address the liver aspect of the patient's pattern but with a lack of blood deficiency signs, this formula is not correct for this case. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 647-649.",
      "exp_hant": "血府逐瘀湯此時並非正確處方，因其為活血化瘀之方，用於治療血瘀症狀。此患者明顯屬於肝氣鬱結兼鬱而化熱及內風。針對這些證候的方劑為天麻鉤藤飲。頗為有趣的是，此方創立於20世紀中期，作為治療西醫所稱高血壓相關頭痛的方劑。此方能平肝、息風、清熱。知柏地黃丸清熱兼滋養腎陰。此病情屬實證，以六味地黃丸為基礎方並不適用於本病例。逍遙散雖能處理患者證候中肝的層面，但由於缺乏血虛的徵象，此方並不適用於本病例。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, pgs. 647-649."
    },
    {
      "number": 757,
      "question_en": "A 42-year-old female patient has a history of external invasions for which she takes Yu Ping Feng San (Jade Windscreen Decoction). She comes into your office having been exposed to a coworker who was coughing and sneezing for the last two weeks while in close proximity to the patient. She currently complains of chills, fever and body aches for two days. The patient often feels tired and catches colds easily. Two days ago she caught a cold and began to feel chills, fever, headache, stiffness of neck, and aches over the body. She has nasal obstruction, cough with white sputum, fullness in chest and epigastrium, and is not sweating. She has a pale tongue with a thin white coating, and a weak and floating pulse. What is the treatment?",
      "question_hant": "一位42歲女性患者有反覆外感病史，平時服用玉屏風散。她前來你的診所，表示曾與一位過去兩週持續咳嗽打噴嚏的同事密切接觸。她目前主訴惡寒、發熱及全身痠痛已兩天。此患者平時常感疲倦，且容易感冒。兩天前她感冒發作，開始出現惡寒、發熱、頭痛、頸部僵硬及全身痠痛。她有鼻塞、咳嗽伴白痰、胸脘部脹滿，且無汗。舌淡苔薄白，脈弱而浮。應如何治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "gui zhi tang (cinnamon twig decoction)",
          "hant": "桂枝湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "yin qiao san (honeysuckle and forsythia powder)",
          "hant": "銀翹散",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "ren shen bai du san (ginseng powder to overcome pathogenic influences)",
          "hant": "人參敗毒散",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "xiao chai hu tang (minor bupleurum decoction)",
          "hant": "小柴胡湯",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is a case of a deficient normal qi concurrent with an external contraction wind-cold-damp pathogen. The weakness can be seen in the fatigue and weak pulse, as well as the propensity to catch colds easily. The wind cold damp invasion is shown through the floating pulse, chills and fever, stiff neck, and sputum. For this pattern, ren shen bai du san is the correct choice. This formula utilizes the dual strategy of expelling the pathogens (the main strategy) while also strengthening the qi. Gui zhi tang is for a disharmony of the ying and wei qi from a tai yang wind strike where there is sweating occurring. This presentation does not have sweating. Gui zhi tang would not adequately address the underlying deficiency. Yin qiao san is for wei level wind heat and this case is a wind cold which can be seen by the stiffness of the neck and body aches, as well as the lack of a rapid pulse. Xiao chai hu tang is the representative formula for the shao yang stage of the six stages from the shang han lun. This formula is a harmonization formula for pathogens in half exterior and half interior. This case is clearly an exterior case with interior deficiency. This is not appropriate for the patient at this time. Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs.47, 36, 104, 13",
      "exp_hant": "此為正氣虛弱兼外感風寒濕邪的病例。虛弱之象可見於疲倦及脈弱，以及容易感冒的傾向。風寒濕邪的侵襲則表現於浮脈、寒熱、頸部僵硬及痰液。就此證候而言，人參敗毒散為正確之選。此方運用雙重策略，以祛邪為主要方針，同時兼顧扶正益氣。桂枝湯適用於太陽中風所致營衛不和，且伴有汗出的情況。本病例並無汗出的表現。桂枝湯無法充分處理潛在的正虛。銀翹散適用於衛分風熱證，而本病例屬風寒證，可見於頸部僵硬、全身痠痛，以及脈象並不數。小柴胡湯為傷寒六經中少陽階段的代表方劑，是治療半表半裡病邪的和解方劑。本病例明顯屬於表證兼裡虛，並不適合此時使用此方。Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs.47, 36, 104, 13"
    },
    {
      "number": 758,
      "question_en": "A patient treats an exterior Tai yang stage condition with the formula Da Cheng Qi Tang (major order the qi decoction) for three days causing the pathogen to move to the Tai-Yin stage. The condition is now characterized by Spleen and Stomach Yang Xu with severe abdominal cramping pain not relieved by passing gas. Which formula is best for this condition at this stage?",
      "question_hant": "一位患者以大承氣湯治療太陽表證三天，導致病邪傳入太陰階段。此時病情特徵為脾胃陽虛，伴嚴重腹部絞痛且矢氣後不緩解。此階段何方最適合此病情？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "True Warrior Decoction (Zhen Wu Tang)",
          "hant": "真武湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Major Construct the Middle Decoction (Da Jian Zhong Tang)",
          "hant": "大建中湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Frigid Extremities Decoction (Si Ni Tang)",
          "hant": "四逆湯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Regulate the Middle Pill (Li Zhong Wan)",
          "hant": "理中丸",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The major formula for the Tai Yin stage according to the Shang Han Lun is li zhong wan. This formula treats middle burner yang deficiency. One of the characteristic presentations of this pattern is extreme abdominal pain not relieved by passing gas. Si Ni Tang treats primarily kidney yang xu through its main herb zhi fu zi and has a typical symptom of frigid extremities. According to the Shang Han Lun, zhen wu tang is a shao yin formula treating kidney yang deficiency with water overflowing. Da jian zhong tang is a formula from the Jin Gui Yao Lue used to treat extreme pain in the abdomen. This formula would be an acceptable choice for this condition although there is typically upsurging of cold qi showing in signs such as vomiting that accompany this pattern. Li zhong wan is the best choice for this case. Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs. 257, 274, 744, 268",
      "exp_hant": "根據《傷寒論》，太陰階段的主方為理中丸。此方治療中焦陽虛。此證候的特徵表現之一，即為矢氣後仍不緩解的劇烈腹痛。四逆湯主要透過其主藥附子治療腎陽虛，其典型症狀為四肢厥冷。根據《傷寒論》，真武湯屬少陰方，治療腎陽虛兼水氣泛濫。大建中湯出自《金匱要略》，用於治療腹部劇痛。此方對於本病情亦為可接受之選擇，惟此證型通常伴有寒氣上逆的表現，如嘔吐等伴隨症狀。就本病例而言，理中丸為最佳選擇。Bensky, Dan, et.al., Formulas and Strategies. Pgs. 257, 274, 744, 268"
    },
    {
      "number": 759,
      "question_en": "A male patient was diagnosed with shaoyang syndrome and prescribed the purgative formula Da Cheng Qi Tang for 4 days. He now complains of focal distention in the epigastrium, which is reportedly soft and not painful to palpation with no masses or hardness. His pulse is now wiry and rapid. The pathogenic progression of his middle jiao heat / cold complex should best be treated in which of the following ways?",
      "question_hant": "一位男性患者被診斷為少陽病證，並以攻下方大承氣湯治療四天。他現在主訴胃脘部局部脹滿，據稱按之柔軟且不痛，亦無腫塊或硬結。脈象現為弦數。針對其中焦寒熱錯雜的病邪傳變，下列何者為最佳治療方式？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Add Tao Ren (semen persicae) and Chi Shao (radix paeoniae rubra)",
          "hant": "加桃仁、赤芍",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Switch the formula to Ban Xia Xie Xin Tang (Pinellia Decoction to Drain the Epigastrium)",
          "hant": "改用半夏瀉心湯",
