        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This patient initially treated her wind-cold invasion with a formula intended to treat wind-heat. Yin qiao san is a diaphoretic (sweat inducing) formula that is cooling in nature. This caused the tai yang condition to move into the shao yang. The pathogen is no longer in the exterior but in-between the interior and exterior where the hot and cold sensations alternate. For this condition, xiao chai hu tang is the correct prescription. Gui zhi tang is for tai yang invasion with the presence of sweating and is not appropriate at this time. Dan shen yin treats blood stasis and qi stagnation in the chest and treats pain. This is not a case of blood stasis causing pain and dan shen yin is not the correct choice. Ping wei san treats cold-damp in the middle burner. This is not the current pattern for this patient and this formula is not the correct choice. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 104-109; 13-18, 594; 687-688",
      "exp_hant": "此患者最初以治療風熱之方治療其風寒外感。銀翹散為性偏寒涼的發汗解表方劑。這使得太陽病證轉入少陽。病邪已不在表，而是處於半表半裡之間，因而出現寒熱往來的表現。就此病情而言，小柴胡湯為正確之處方。桂枝湯適用於太陽病邪兼有汗出的情況，此時並不適用。丹參飲治療胸中血瘀氣滯並止痛。本病例並非血瘀所致疼痛，故丹參飲並非正確之選。平胃散治療中焦寒濕。此並非此患者目前的證候，故此方並非正確之選。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Bensky, pgs. 104-109; 13-18, 594; 687-688"
    },
    {
      "number": 761,
      "question_en": "A patient is diagnosed with kidney yang deficiency but has an aconite sensitivity. Which formula would do this patient the least amount of harm?",
      "question_hant": "一位患者被診斷為腎陽虛，但對附子過敏。何方對此患者造成的傷害最小？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
